local Text_AwakerStory = readonly({
  AwakerStory_100415_Content = {
    Text = "A.F.3@2 Feb 12th\nDuring the visit to the statue studio, the completed sculptures were painted with colors. The color design is quite innovative, but it contradicts the original design system of the sculpture set.\n\nAfterward, I agreed to take on all the coloring work for the statues for free. Perhaps there will indeed be opportunities for us to collaborate in the future.\n\nWitness: Sanga\n...\n\nA.F.3@2Apr 9th\nAttempted to dig up corpses in the Keygrave as models, but failed. Captured on site, invited the patrol personnel to pretend to be corpses.\n\nWitness: Ogier\n...\n\nA.F.3@2 Apr 11th\nStealing kitchen ingredients as reference objects for a painting. Although the ingredients were successfully saved, the timing of the spice marination and the flavors of the ingredients have been completely ruined, losing their value.\n\nAs for the attributes and sources of the ingredients... it's not convenient to disclose that for now.\n\nWitness: Doresain\n...\n\nA.F.3@2Jun 29th\nIllegally infiltrating the school's library, hanging your own massive painting in the center of the wall. At midnight, influenced by the school's Silver energy density, a bizarre creature emerged from the painting, causing damage to some unprotected artifacts.\n\nAfterwards, he voluntarily applied for maintenance work, during which the number of damaged artifacts exceeded the damage caused by the monsters. The school has urgently suspended his maintenance activities.\n\nWitness: Czort\n\n...\n\nA.F.3@2 Jul 23rd\nDiving into the Black Pool, attempting to use the pool water as paint. Tawil did not disturb him, but the power of the Black Pool itself caused him significant harm.\n\nI am actually looking forward to what kind of scene he will create with the Black Pool?\n\nWitness: Alistair\n...\n\n—\"Pickman Records: Violation Log"
  },
  AwakerStory_100415_Title = {Text = "Story: II"},
  AwakerStory_100415_UnlockDesc = {
    Text = "Affinity Level 5"
  },
  AwakerStory_100416_Content = {
    Text = "Before receiving that invitation from Necrovia, Pickman thought there would never be a place in this world for someone like him.\n\nThe extreme madness he witnessed at the royal banquet table kept him tossing and turning in sleeplessness. Those eyes that could see scenes from different worlds found true fullness at this feast.\n\nWhen he awoke from the Dream and Necrovia faded from his sight, Pickman's regret quickly transformed into an endless longing—he yearned to return to that dream city, to witness once more the infinite madness of that breathtaking scene. Following this desire, he attempted every mad act. In the end, he leaped into the D-Rift, painting with Dissolution, completely exposing himself to that horrifying darkness.\n\nEveryone has their own tasks to accomplish. He has eyes that can see the mad truth of the world, and he firmly believes that he was born to burn for art; this is his mission.\n\nAs he wished, Dissolution brought him madness and pain, allowing him to once again witness the scenes he experienced in Necrovia. The twisted world in his eyes became even wilder and more vibrant under the corrosion of Dissolution. Amidst the prolonged suffering, he picked up the paintbrush, painting day after day without pause. He is a devoted realist painter, and he must record these visions that only he can see.\n\nThe pain intensified, and when Pickman could no longer grip the brush in his hand, he knew his time was near. After completing the final stroke of his last painting, he lay down in the coffin he had long prepared, waiting for death to arrive.\n\nThe pain and chaos brought by Dissolution clouded Pickman's mind. In the cold embrace of death, he peacefully closed his eyes. But the next day, the bright moonlight awakened him once again. The traces of Dissolution and pain miraculously faded away. After several days of growth, his limbs became long and curved, and his canine teeth and claws became hard and sharp. He sensed the scent of graves and spirits, and the mad, chaotic sights of the world became clearer in his eyes than ever before.\n\nHe gazed joyfully at his half-human, half-ghoul body, a tremendous sense of happiness swelling in his heart. Fate had bestowed upon him a curse, but it also compensated for his rare talent. The experiences in Necrovia awakened the faint ghoul blood within him, and under the catalyst of dissolution, he completed his transformation.\n\nThe tombstones around him danced clumsily like a crowd celebrating together. The enormous Bloody Moon opened its crimson eye and smiled at him. His art does not belong to this world; now, he knows where he is destined to go.\n\nPickman lay atop his own coffin, spreading his arms wide, joining in this lonely revelry.\n\nHe is about to leave the city of humanity and go to the promised land that belongs to him.\n\nHe knows that everything he seeks is waiting for him there."
  },
  AwakerStory_100416_Title = {Text = "Story: III"},
  AwakerStory_100416_UnlockDesc = {
    Text = "Affinity Level 7"
  },
  AwakerStory_100417_Content = {
    Text = "A half-human, half-ghoul artist, he possesses an otherworldly talent that remains forever out of reach for ordinary souls.\n\nHis ghoul artworks dissolve the fragile boundary between the painted world and the real one, pulling viewers into a total, and often terrifying, immersion.\n\nYet Pickman vehemently rejects the title of mad surrealist.\n\nIn his own declaration, he has always been, and will only ever be, a realist—for he paints nothing but the world as it truly is."
  },
  AwakerStory_100417_Title = {
    Text = "Basic Information"
  },
  AwakerStory_100417_UnlockDesc = {
    Text = "Awakener Level 1"
  },
  AwakerStory_100418_Content = {
    Text = [[
A monster. A freak. Demon with the blood of monsters. Madman who desecrates art...

Before Pickman, a canvas unfurls, and the curses mix with other sounds, smearing brilliant colors across the canvas.

He leaps into this dazzling world, wandering in the mad colors. He eagerly hopes to lead others into his painting, to let them witness the most authentic visage of the world.

The sharp spikes of reality pierce his heart countless times; mutual understanding between people is more challenging than opening the boundaries of two worlds.

From humans to ghouls, from human cities to Necropolis, the road is long and winding. He has been wounded time and again, yet he rises again and again. He has long understood that there is neither truth nor falsehood. Pain and madness are the truth of the world. And his duty is to depict all of this faithfully.

The meaning of depiction lies only in the act of depicting itself.

He dedicates all his life and passion to painting. His expectations rarely receive a response; his pursuit never ceases.]]
  },
  AwakerStory_100418_Title = {Text = "Story: IV"},
  AwakerStory_100418_UnlockDesc = {
    Text = "Affinity Level 9"
  },
  AwakerStory_100419_Content = {
    Text = "The courses of the Painting Department in the Academy of Fine Arts are tedious and mundane, most of which have left no trace in my life, but I can still recall the mimetic painting class in A.F. 3@2.\n\nMr. Matthew is renowned in the art association, his classroom is crowded with people. We huddled in front of Matisse's \"Luxury, Calmness, and Delight,\" and at that moment, I noticed a thin young man in the corner madly smudging in a sketchbook. I approached him, ready to see his mimicked painting, but saw a chaotic stone sculpture of a graveyard.\n\n\"Look! The ghoul queen is giving birth, preparing for a blood feast for her child... how mad, how elegant!\"\n\nHe excitedly looked up at me, his pupils glowing with a strange blood-red under the gaslight, as if it was a coffin covered in red moss. I felt fear and dizziness, but I couldn't take my eyes off it. In those eyes, I saw images completely unworthy of this world.\n\nPickman, from the first time I saw him, I knew he was different from us, his life was destined to be difficult and extraordinary.\n\nAfter getting acquainted, I occasionally visited his studio. I witnessed him using decaying corpses as models and his own blood as paint. Standing in front of those crazy artworks, I felt as if I could hear the gnawing sounds coming from the canvas.\n\nNo matter which faction in the art world, no one recognized Pickman's creations; all exhibitions and salons turned him away. He appeared unfazed, still optimistically pursuing his art, but his purity made it impossible for him to hide his loss and pain. His talent was both shocking and frightening, and no one could truly accept it, including myself.\n\nIn the final days before leaving, Pickman fell into a state of great pain and excitement, which I originally thought was a psychological issue that was bound to occur, until one day, I saw his twisted limbs and claws, and witnessed the mad world in his eyes. That was a fear I couldn't contend with, and I could only try to forget it. Before I could completely end my connection with Pickman, he proactively found me to say goodbye.\n\nNow, standing in the modern art museum's pristine gallery, looking at the genuine Pickman's work discarded in the corner, I can still hear the sound of nails scraping from deep within the canvas. \"Underground Carnival,\" that was the painting he created when I first met him, and also the farewell gift he left me. Pickman might hold some taboo puzzles that should not be approached, but I still kept this painting. No matter what happened to him that I shouldn't know, one thing is certain - he is the most talented artist I have ever met.\n\nLast night, I dreamed again of that painting class room in my freshman year. The young Pickman was in the corner of the room, laughing loudly at me.\n\n\"Ghoul? No, Ever, what I painted from start to finish is the truth, is humanity!\"\n\nThe moonlight split into countless bloody points in his eyes. That was the first time the Abyss smiled at me. \n\n—Excerpt from <Italic:\"The Memoir of Painter Avery @2\">"
  },
  AwakerStory_100419_Title = {Text = "Story: I"},
  AwakerStory_100419_UnlockDesc = {
    Text = "Affinity Level 3"
  },
  AwakerStory_11158_Content = {
    Text = "Time: @1@2, A.F. 299\nLocation: Lab UG-C03, @2@1, @4, Londinium.\n\nParticipants: @1, @2, @4, @3\nTest Subject: W\nSubject Profile:\nThe subject's biological form is that of an adult human female, born on June 18, A.F. 280; origin unknown. While en route to her studies at @2 University, the original host succumbed to an illness and passed away. Subsequently, the extraterrestrial spiritual entity known as @1 occupied and reanimated the vessel, resuming the host's former life.\n\n@1 possesses the abilities of spiritual migration and replacement and can visually perceive Dissolution. Although human bodies cannot perceive Dissolution, the inherent abilities of @1’s species allowed the subject to perceive its presence on a spiritual level. Therefore, when the subject first observed Dissolution 2 years and 8 months ago, she attempted spiritual migration to avoid further degradation.\n\nWhile @1 retains the capacity to perceive Dissolution, the subject remains unable to sever its influence, and all attempts at spiritual migration have failed. After multiple futile attempts, the subject proactively contacted @3 University, requesting to be converted into an Awakener, which directly led to this experiment.\n\n—Excerpt from <Italic:Experiment Record: The Feasibility of In-Vivo Silver Core Extraction>"
  },
  AwakerStory_11158_Title = {Text = "Story: I"},
  AwakerStory_11158_UnlockDesc = {
    Text = "Affinity Level 3"
  },
  AwakerStory_11159_Content = {
    Text = "A tinkling sweet laugh echoes hollowly, and a petite figure appears in dim candlelight. She is both the fear and desire of the condemned, the dew and poison for the dying, bringing sweet pain and romantic madness. The \"snap\" from her ever-present whip on the skin is an evil symphony playing in the darkness."
  },
  AwakerStory_11159_Title = {
    Text = "Basic Information"
  },
  AwakerStory_11159_UnlockDesc = {
    Text = "Awakener Level 1"
  },
  AwakerStory_11160_Content = {
    Text = [[
After reuniting with Faint, Tinct settled down at Mythag University. After being injured again in the P-063 @ 2 Event, Tinct became even more fearful of strangers, leading her to become reclusive. Unlike her powerful and melodious singing voice, her everyday conversational tone is sweet and clear, but few have had the chance to hear it.

Some well-meaning individuals attempted to promote Tinct's performances on campus, even finding posters from her early opera house performances and plastering them around the campus.

Tinct is unwilling to cater to these wishes; such enthusiasm only stirs up memories of a past she wants to forget.

"End this absurd tragedy. As long as I'm by your side, I have no other desires. If possible, I wouldn't mind being forgotten by this world."

"Don't, Tinct. The days we will spend together are still long ahead. This is no longer our home planet, and I am no longer your burden. You should find the things you want to do and live for yourself."]]
  },
  AwakerStory_11160_Title = {Text = "Story: II"},
  AwakerStory_11160_UnlockDesc = {
    Text = "Affinity Level 5"
  },
  AwakerStory_11161_Content = {
    Text = "At Mythag University, the campus legend that \"preparatory students must fight Lotan to become investigators\" has spiraled out of control, driving fear of the black-clad swordswoman to an all-time high. Many students who specialize in theoretical research break into a cold sweat at the mere sight of a black hemline, dreading any chance of locking eyes with the \"battle maniac\" and meeting their end on the training ground.\n\nIn a brief exclusive interview conducted by Editor-in-Chief Hannah Peaslee, Miss Lotan offered the following remarks:\n\"I don't have time to play house with babies.\"\n\n\"Weaklings have no place being my opponent—are you one of them? Or do you have the nerve to face Chaos head-on?\"\n\n—As of press time, the editor-in-chief has not left her dormitory. This issue of the <Italic:Mythag Daily> was printed and distributed by intern editor Howard."
  },
  AwakerStory_11161_Title = {Text = "Story: II"},
  AwakerStory_11161_UnlockDesc = {
    Text = "Affinity Level 5"
  },
  AwakerStory_11162_Content = {
    Text = "A.F. 315, January, @2\nDr. Sylvia suggested that I jot down my thoughts in a notebook to help train my memory. Everyone says doctors know a lot and can surely help me. So I'm counting on it; tomorrow, I mustn't forget the purpose of this notebook! \n\n Today, I completed the production and assembly of the exhaust pipe. Now it can exhaust air without interfering with the auxiliary hose's movement. This should be the last step, right? At least I haven't found any issues so far, but I can't rule out forgetting a screw somewhere... That's right, I must have forgotten something—either a screw or a pipe, or maybe bearing lubrication? Engine oil? Honestly, I've always had this nagging feeling that something's off with the Phantom. It's always... lacking? Is that the word? It misses a crucial component, even more critical than the engine. Without it, I can't set off, can't embark on that journey into the unknown, because that is ours. @2 \n Why am I saying ours? Who am I with? Did I... have someone? I remember, it seems like... @2 @4 @3 \n Uh, my head hurts so much. \n\n But this notebook feels quite useful; that way, I can continue recalling from here tomorrow, and who knows, maybe I really will remember? \n\n—The only entry in Nautila's diary."
  },
  AwakerStory_11162_Title = {Text = "Story: IV"},
  AwakerStory_11162_UnlockDesc = {
    Text = "Affinity Level 9"
  },
  AwakerStory_11163_Content = {
    Text = "The unenlightened are pitiful, for they cannot comprehend the true essence of immortality. Worldly conflicts are meaningless, as they are but shallow diversions in the grand scheme of things.\n\nI have gazed upon it, I have tasted it, and I have long understood my purpose.\n\nBut, oh, how cruel is fate! Why did you... not choose your most loyal Priest once more?\n\n—It must be that you are bestowing upon me a trial, testing my faith. In the farthest reaches from my homeland, in moments devoid of your grace, my faith has endured through millennia, unwavering.\n\nI could not be the one to welcome your rebirth, but I have prepared everything for it. I will seek out a new eternal realm for you... The mix of resentment and honor weighs heavily upon me, and I must bear this responsibility alone...\n\nForgive my ugly jealousy. As long as I can once again witness your majesty, as long as I can rebuild your kingdom, I am willing to do anything."
  },
  AwakerStory_11163_Title = {Text = "Story: IV"},
  AwakerStory_11163_UnlockDesc = {
    Text = "Affinity Level 9"
  },
  AwakerStory_11164_Content = {
    Text = "Draped in shimmering jewels and trailing gossamer silk, she keeps her true self hidden beneath a facade of breathtaking splendor.\n\nThais may appear vain and frivolous—an impression held by many—but perhaps that is merely another mask she wears.\n\n\"My, what are you writing there? Here, let me help—"
  },
  AwakerStory_11164_Title = {
    Text = "Basic Information"
  },
  AwakerStory_11164_UnlockDesc = {
    Text = "Awakener Level 1"
  },
  AwakerStory_11165_Content = {
    Text = "Used flasks must be cleaned to look as good as new, tables burnt in experiments polished until they shine, and scales recalibrated every three days. Her fervor and respect for science and the mysteries of the world set high standards for everyone and everything around her.\n\nOf course, these standards also apply to herself—after all, not everyone can calmly embrace death and willingly become an Awakener."
  },
  AwakerStory_11165_Title = {
    Text = "Basic Information"
  },
  AwakerStory_11165_UnlockDesc = {
    Text = "Awakener Level 1"
  },
  AwakerStory_11166_Content = {
    Text = "A.F. 315, @2@1, 08:13 a.m.\n\nMTC On-Site Response Team 3 and members of the Dissolution Item Control and Management (DISM) Group β7 arrived at Dissolution Area L-E-933 (formerly the Rogers Wax Museum, @2 Southwark Street) to take over the task from MTC Team 1 and DISM Group α2, conducting area neutralization work.\n\n09:24 a.m.\n\nWhile clearing the subterranean area of the museum, DISM member James exhibited symptoms including headaches, nausea, and vertigo.\n\n10:47 a.m.\n\nRowland (Team 3), Zachary (DISM), and Bolton (DISM) fled the subterranean area. The trio reported that the underground darkness swallowed them, plunging them into a floating starry void. Tangible colors intertwined within the space—gorgeous yet bone-chilling. These colors then condensed into countless rats that rapidly surged toward them.\n\nBolton refused to continue and returned to the Committee's Londinium office. Rowland and Zachary accompanied Team 3 Captain Fisher back into the underground area for further inspection.\n\n1:03 p.m.\n\nFollowing a systematic search, Captain Fisher located and recovered Silver Core L3202 from the residual dissolution wax in the underground area. It was then transferred to Mythag University for further processing.\n\n—<Italic:Neutralization Report of Dissolution Area L-E-933>"
  },
  AwakerStory_11166_Title = {Text = "Story: I"},
  AwakerStory_11166_UnlockDesc = {
    Text = "Affinity Level 3"
  },
  AwakerStory_11167_Content = {
    Text = "24 discovered that their home had been robbed less than a month after moving in.\n\nFirst the cheese, then the bread, the milk, the tomatoes... the food in the house always seemed to dwindle, little by little, without a sound.\n\nShe waited patiently for several days, and at last caught the culprit—a mouse. Weaving left and right past the traps she had set, it snatched up two mushrooms and vanished behind the cellar door.\n\n24 opened the cellar door and descended the damp, moldering steps, only to find that they led down into an underground waterway.\n\nThe mouse scurried into the shadows, mushrooms in tow. 24 followed, and caught a glimpse of bright eyes in the darkness—like those of a wolf pup. The child was wrapped in tattered cloth and covered with old newspapers, shivering all over in the near-freezing air.\n\nSomething pricked faintly at 24's heart.\n\n\"Mushrooms are best not eaten raw. You'll get sick.\"\n\nThe child remained silent.\n\n24 went and cooked a pot of mushroom soup, set a small bowl of it on the table, and went to bed. She had to be up by 6 a.m. every day for work, with hardly any time to rest.\n\nWhen she woke the next morning, the bowl sat exactly where she had left it—but the soup was gone, every last drop.\n\nAfter that, 24 would occasionally cook a little extra to share with the neighbor downstairs. In return, the child would sometimes leave her small gifts—trinkets and toys found from who knows where...\n\nAnd so a quiet, unspoken understanding was formed between them."
  },
  AwakerStory_11167_Title = {Text = "Story: III"},
  AwakerStory_11167_UnlockDesc = {
    Text = "Affinity Level 7"
  },
  AwakerStory_11167_UnlockDesc_1 = {
    Text = "Complete Chapter 2 \"Waxen Legacy\" on Normal difficulty"
  },
  AwakerStory_11168_Content = {
    Text = [[
Our good friend, the resourceful Hannah Peaslee, somehow dug up the research materials on Celeste. Thanks to this audacious reporter, both the originally confidential materials and her brief interview with Celeste has now spreaded into every corner.

After reading the confidential materials, Hannah posed a question to her usually emotionless face.

"Most Awakeners have unfulfilled wishes, which lie in their basic motivations for cooperating with the university. However, your wish section is blank in this material. Don't you have any desire to accomplish anything? Or what is your meaning as an Awakener?"

"I have, I do have."

The girl's expression showed no cracks, as ethereal and noble as usual. If it were not for that brief answer and the anxiety within, the reporter would have almost thought that she miss the question.


"I will find my wish... everyone wishes so. Therefore I will find it."

Her soft voice resounded, delicate and fragile like an easily shattered dream.]]
  },
  AwakerStory_11168_Title = {Text = "Story: IV"},
  AwakerStory_11168_UnlockDesc = {
    Text = "Affinity Level 9"
  },
  AwakerStory_11169_Content = {
    Text = [[
Every word and action embodies loyalty, every move reflects virtue.

Although "knowing propriety and righteousness, being strict with oneself" is deeply engraved in the soul, this virtuous knight undoubtedly still bears the appearance of a child.

But please do not worry, even if the price is eternal demise, Ogier will spare no effort to fulfill his lord's commands.

May that day never come.]]
  },
  AwakerStory_11169_Title = {
    Text = "Basic Information"
  },
  AwakerStory_11169_UnlockDesc = {
    Text = "Awakener Level 1"
  },
  AwakerStory_11170_Content = {
    Text = [[
The young King slumbers upon his throne. Upon waking, he issues his decrees, his authority reaching every corner of the world.

Yet before the sun has set, the King is already weary. He has grown tired of his own power and transcendent wisdom; tired of the fanatical worship of his followers, and of the long dreams that have stretched across aeons.

None know what he witnessed during his long sleep, but they should be grateful for the bliss of their own ignorance.]]
  },
  AwakerStory_11170_Title = {
    Text = "Basic Information"
  },
  AwakerStory_11170_UnlockDesc = {
    Text = "Awakener Level 1"
  },
  AwakerStory_11171_Content = {
    Text = "\"The benevolent Father once said: Cherish all things within the sky, on the ground, in the water, and in the soil. For all beings are my offspring.\n\n\"Thus, I say: Render all suffering unto me. Let those tormented by life or plagued by disease be made whole. Let all pain and madness melt as frost before the rising sun. Let you, my brethren, receive joy everlasting. \n\n\"Burn me, grind my bones to dust, and rend my flesh asunder. For as long as you can find solace, I have little complaints.\"\n\n—B.F. 1@1, May 30, Sal @1doMartin @2I @1as, left at @3 the Tribunal"
  },
  AwakerStory_11171_Title = {Text = "Story: IV"},
  AwakerStory_11171_UnlockDesc = {
    Text = "Affinity Level 9"
  },
  AwakerStory_11172_Content = {
    Text = "Faint is a faded, hard-to-hatch seed.\n\nPeople pity her for her flaws and love her for her weaknesses.\n\nYet those who knew she had chosen to remain in the shell, had long since turned to dust—stardust."
  },
  AwakerStory_11172_Title = {
    Text = "Basic Information"
  },
  AwakerStory_11172_UnlockDesc = {
    Text = "Awakener Level 1"
  },
  AwakerStory_11173_Content = {
    Text = [[
After the @3@1 Event, Ryker became a special advisor at Mythag University.

Ryker is a competent advisor. From the mysterious disappearance of professors or inexplicable damage to instruments, to trivial matters such as searching for cats and dogs, Ryker can patiently and swiftly deliver satisfactory results.

Soon, due to his unique appearance, dignified and elegant demeanor, and helpful habits, Ryker became an idol figure beloved by countless young men and women in Mythag.

Professor Dexter once lamented, "The spotlight has been stolen by the youth."

But as he gradually became integrated into the campus, everyone noticed that Ryker's time in front of people began to decrease.

Meanwhile, in a certain abandoned basement of Mythag, the sound of dice rolling began to occur frequently.]]
  },
  AwakerStory_11173_Title = {Text = "Story: II"},
  AwakerStory_11173_UnlockDesc = {
    Text = "Affinity Level 5"
  },
  AwakerStory_11174_Content = {
    Text = [[
Those who meet her for the first time have no desire to approach or communicate, as their survival instincts fervently warn them to stay away.

She is completely mad, or rather, a wild beast through and through.

If given the choice again, she might prefer to be a beast rather than endure everything as a human.

She trusts no one, and when her scarlet eyes gaze upon you, what you see is not suspicion but indifference and murderous intent.

She has long since scorned suspicion, seeing all people as equally base.

If you need advice on dealing with her, do not attempt to tame a true beast, for it is anything but docile. At the slightest opportunity, her claws and fangs will pierce your throat.

Leave her presence before she focuses on you, and pray that her next prey is not you.]]
  },
  AwakerStory_11174_Title = {Text = "Story: II"},
  AwakerStory_11174_UnlockDesc = {
    Text = "Affinity Level 5"
  },
  AwakerStory_11175_Content = {
    Text = "Let’s dance! Dance a merry dance, dance a wild dance! Laugh along with her, and stoke the atmosphere to fever pitch.\n\nAnd then—it's time for the star to take the stage.\n\nThere, where the spotlights converge, the mad magician has already slipped her hand into her top hat. As for what she will pull from that endless void—be it a cascade of colorful ribbons, a flock of white doves taking flight, or the razor-sharp claws of some dreadful monster... I'm afraid only she can tell."
  },
  AwakerStory_11175_Title = {
    Text = "Basic Information"
  },
  AwakerStory_11175_UnlockDesc = {
    Text = "Awakener Level 1"
  },
  AwakerStory_11176_Content = {
    Text = [[
This is a souvenir Professor Dexter brought back from the Febvre Coast.

The mild ocean climate of Febvre is very pleasant. The century-old Sevada Sanatorium is located by the seashore, attracting countless vacationers each year.

In this glass bottle, wrapped in seaweed, are some translucent powders. It is neither a message left by shipwreck survivors nor a local sand art piece. Professor Dexter has noticed that the bottle contains silver essence powder, meaning it houses a spirit.

He said he bought it from a local fisherman who hesitantly narrated recent strange encounters. A few days ago, early in the morning, the fisherman encountered an unusual fish swarm while fishing. It was neither the breeding season nor the wintering season, yet the swarm lingered. When the heavy nets were pulled up, they found a strange bottle. The fisherman, curious but uneasy, feared the bottle might bring bad luck or a curse. After this, no fish were caught in this area for several days.]]
  },
  AwakerStory_11176_Title = {Text = "Story: I"},
  AwakerStory_11176_UnlockDesc = {
    Text = "Awakener Level 3"
  },
  AwakerStory_11177_Content = {
    Text = "Arithmetic: Zero points. Aurita even scored 2 points.\n\nEnglish: Failing. It took a long time to understand the difference between \"shift\" and \"bullshit.\"\n\n......\n\nHistory: Failing. Claimed Caligula was the most outstanding Roman emperor because he built many arenas.\n\nDanger Rating: C. Shows a degree of aggression when interacting with other Awakeners. Not a serious threat; no special attention needed.\n\nNotes: This individual has almost no self-care abilities (another victim poisoned by slavery), requires constant attention, and must not be allowed to use snowflake cream as a dental cleaner again.\n\n—Excerpt from A.F. 313, \"Mythag Annual Student Profile.\""
  },
  AwakerStory_11177_Title = {Text = "Story: II"},
  AwakerStory_11177_UnlockDesc = {
    Text = "Affinity Level 5"
  },
  AwakerStory_11178_Content = {
    Text = "Age@2, the ancient city of Akka.\n\nA thousand years of thirst finally broke loose—kill, drink, kill, drink—until nothing remained before him but an endless desert and a vast litter of desiccated corpses, so dreadful a sight that even the vultures dared not draw near.\n\nHe knelt in the yellow sand and laughed, and laughed, and laughed.\n\nGlorious! @1 glorious!\n\nAnd now—he would crown this magnificent feast of slaughter with his own blood.\n\nThe warrior bit open his own wrist, drained himself dry, and collapsed at last into the vast crimson pool he had made."
  },
  AwakerStory_11178_Title = {Text = "Story: IV"},
  AwakerStory_11178_UnlockDesc = {
    Text = "Affinity Level 9"
  },
  AwakerStory_11179_Content = {
    Text = [[
"Horla, from today onward, I will treasure all your poems. In the future, I'll trade my flowers for your poems!"

"Colette, you will definitely come back to save me...right?"]]
  },
  AwakerStory_11179_Title = {Text = "Story: IV"},
  AwakerStory_11179_UnlockDesc = {
    Text = "Affinity Level 9"
  },
  AwakerStory_11180_Content = {
    Text = "Yesterday at 6 PM, room CB-101, located in the basement of the Prince Building at Mythag University, was damaged by unknown individuals. The reinforced door was severely damaged, and there were black lightning-like scorch marks on both the interior and exterior walls, leaving the scene in disarray.\n\n\"Instantaneous super strong currents can lead to such markings, \" Dr. Adams from the Electrical Engineering department commented on the scorch marks on the wall, \"This requires an enormous voltage. If it were an ordinary device, it would be quite large and hard to conceal. But if it were silver... anything is possible.\"\n\nGiven that silver is under strict supervision within the awakening department, it is hard to imagine someone could use silver privately without detection, thus more attention turns to the Awakeners who possess silver energy.\n\n\"I would say, it was definitely her,\" a student from the awakening department who wished to remain anonymous told the reporter. When asked specifically who it was, he appeared somewhat nervous, \"It's 'her', the one known as 'Tick-Tock'! Haven't you heard the continuous current sound from her body? Whenever I think of electricity, I think of her, no doubt about it.\" \n\nMany students expressed similar suspicions. However, this Awakener, who acted like a mechanical puppet with a strange smile, was not without support; several investigators publicly backed Erica and urged everyone to focus on facts and evidence, warning against causing harm to others due to personal biases.\n\nIn response, Dr. Sokolova, the deputy head of the awakening department, declined to comment. The incident is still under further investigation.\n\n— Excerpt from \"Mythag Daily\", \"Initial Investigation of the CB-101 Room Explosion Incident\""
  },
  AwakerStory_11180_Title = {Text = "Story: II"},
  AwakerStory_11180_UnlockDesc = {
    Text = "Affinity Level 5"
  },
  AwakerStory_11181_Content = {
    Text = [[
She always arrogantly refers to herself as the "Divine Mother," coldly and hostilely keeping everyone outside her safe perimeter. It's difficult for those meeting her for the first time to connect her with the spoiled little princess.

"But they are essentially the same person," the Keeper, however, stubbornly insists to everyone. "You'd know if you ever saw her wolf down a cupcake alone."]]
  },
  AwakerStory_11181_Title = {
    Text = "Basic Information"
  },
  AwakerStory_11181_UnlockDesc = {
    Text = "Awakener Level 1"
  },
  AwakerStory_11182_Content = {
    Text = [[
Genius and madness are separated by a fine line. Once the brightest genius of Mythag, her downfall was like a collapsing building, leaving only the most deranged fiend crawling out from the ruins of reason.

She routinely donned the cloak of science, pouring life, humanity, love, and destruction into the crucible, concocting a poison to annihilate the world.]]
  },
  AwakerStory_11182_Title = {
    Text = "Basic Information"
  },
  AwakerStory_11182_UnlockDesc = {
    Text = "Awakener Level 1"
  },
  AwakerStory_11183_Content = {
    Text = "Don't expect much from the intellect of jellyfish; Aurita cannot comprehend what she has experienced. All she can affirm is that she once lived in that deserted village. Whenever the past is brought up, she deflects the conversation by feigning understanding, so Aurita contributes little to the study of D-Phenomenon or cataclysmic anomalies.\n\nHowever, as a rare harmless Awakener, Aurita is deeply cherished by the faculty and students of the Awakener Department. Even Professor Czort, the lead researcher in Dissolution biology, takes particular care of her.\n\nBy the way, she gained the ability to split and proliferate after merging with the jellyfish's collective consciousness. Even if what proliferates are just ordinary jellyfish, Aurita excitedly holds up her \"companions\" to boast door-to-door—though, unable to distinguish between individuals, she remains blissfully unaware that the \"new friend\" she presents each time is the exact same jellyfish."
  },
  AwakerStory_11183_Title = {Text = "Story: II"},
  AwakerStory_11183_UnlockDesc = {
    Text = "Affinity Level 5"
  },
  AwakerStory_11184_Content = {
    Text = "■ File Number: AF315-C01\n■ Awakener Codename: @2 Walker\nThis Awakener was first observed in A.F. 315, @1.\n\nDuring the initial \"Artificial Domain\" experiment, influenced by the psychic resonance of the homogenous object, the \"Artificial Domain\" based on the Spirit Realm of our university's @2-level student Ramona Dexter unexpectedly broke through dimensional boundaries.\n\nAt that time, the Keeper confirmed the existence of the world outside dimensions for the first time in that \"Artificial Domain\" and also confirmed how @2's power would affect Ramona Dexter.\n\nThereafter, researches on the \"Genesis Awakeners\" was officially launched by the Awakener Sciences Research Institute.\n\nMeanwhile, the planning of the teaching plan for new Power Control course for Ramona Dexter is also on the agenda."
  },
  AwakerStory_11184_Title = {Text = "Story: I"},
  AwakerStory_11184_UnlockDesc = {
    Text = "Awakener Level 3"
  },
  AwakerStory_11185_Content = {
    Text = [[
Draped in black, Miryam's emaciated body was concealed beneath her robes.

Silent, she bore a countenance of devout sorrow, much like the Virgin in a mural, exuding endless mystery.

She poured her entire being into waiting for a special moment.

It is almost here; the appointed day draws near.]]
  },
  AwakerStory_11185_Title = {
    Text = "Basic Information"
  },
  AwakerStory_11185_UnlockDesc = {
    Text = "Awakener Level 1"
  },
  AwakerStory_11186_Content = {
    Text = [[
Grabbed by Doll upon the moment of joining the university, Celeste has undergone a series of comprehensive assessment.

As an Awakener summoned from non-standard process, Celeste's mental state is incredibly stable. However, neither her spirit intensity nor her Gnostic index which evaluates the strength of slivercore meets the Awakener's standard.

Yet she still emerged into this world as an Awakener, like a flower with invisible petals brusts in abysmal nothingness.

Although no abnormalities has shown in daily activities or field missions, data record reveals Celeste's concerning situation: her will, already faint, continues to evansce.

By now, the Awakening Department is organizing a small order to sustain Celeste's existence by supplying religious belief. Those who are interested in joining and proficient in aquatic activities could contact Teacher Sylvia for further infomation.]]
  },
  AwakerStory_11186_Title = {Text = "Story: II"},
  AwakerStory_11186_UnlockDesc = {
    Text = "Affinity Level 5"
  },
  AwakerStory_11187_Content = {
    Text = [[
A scar jagged across his neck. A declaration of death for his people, while a coronation of majestic power for him.

When exile marks his failure, bitterness drown his breath; when despration hollows for surrender, and tides clamor for sacrificehe prays to the God for the power. His transcendent power.

Thus the God's apostle accepts his prayer, severing his head as an offering.

Thus the God's apostle acknowledges his prayer, emplacing the remnants of immortal on his exposed cervical spine.

Thus the God's apostle answers his prayer, leading him into the sanctum of eternity.]]
  },
  AwakerStory_11187_Title = {Text = "Story: III"},
  AwakerStory_11187_UnlockDesc = {
    Text = "Affinity Level 7"
  },
  AwakerStory_11188_Content = {
    Text = "She had an enviable birth: an orphan raised as the sole heir—how fortunate.\n\nShe had remarkable wisdom: speaking at one, debating at two, beginning her enlightenment at three.\n\nShe had admirable talent: a photographic memory and mastery of the sword. At an incredibly young age, she passed Mythag University's rigorous preparatory courses with full marks.\n\nShe had companions she could rely on, with whom she could venture into darkness and the unknown.\n\n<Italic:She had...>"
  },
  AwakerStory_11188_Title = {Text = "Story: III"},
  AwakerStory_11188_UnlockDesc = {
    Text = "Affinity Level 7"
  },
  AwakerStory_11189_Content = {
    Text = "Doll's joining is the only highlight of Mythag University in the eyes of the outside world.\n\nCountless scholars lament that even a prodigy cannot escape the shackles of the mundane—she actually chose to be enrolled by an obscure university for wealth, tainted by the smell of copper.\n\nWhile the outside world condemns her self-degradation, Doll has obtained something more precious than gold at Mythag University.\n\nShe has crossed the boundaries of material science, touching the veil of reality, beneath which lies something she would give her life to pursue.\n\nResearching the dangers of \"silver chip technology\" is no less perilous than dancing on the edge of a blade, and Doll has become the most earnest, diligent, and excellent dancer.\n\nWhen the D-mark appears, the scientific dancer does not cease her movement; instead, she spins within the limited time, either sedimenting or crystallizing her unique dance steps.\n\nUntil the D-phenomenon severely injures her physical body, spreading to her mind and eroding her rationality.\n\nEven so, she remains far from the center of truth.\n\nThus, the flame of life has dimmed, leaving the brilliant star of knowledge with this farewell: \"Awake me before the world forgets me.\""
  },
  AwakerStory_11189_Title = {Text = "Story: III"},
  AwakerStory_11189_UnlockDesc = {
    Text = "Affinity Level 7"
  },
  AwakerStory_11190_Content = {
    Text = [[
Every time His Excellency the Bishop visits Mythag University, he is warmly welcomed by teachers and students alike.

The young Awakeners would tug at his hand, asking him to tell more stories from before the Flood. Students would also seek his counsel, inquiring if the Bishop would lend an ear to their troubles and woes. Even the seemingly cold and strong Awakeners and knowledgable professors approach the Bishop when he has free time: either to share their nightmares or to discuss the truths of the Soul.

His patience is unending, never tiring; Anyone may find acceptance and warmth with him.

"Of course, my child, is there aught I can do for you?"]]
  },
  AwakerStory_11190_Title = {Text = "Story: II"},
  AwakerStory_11190_UnlockDesc = {
    Text = "Affinity Level 5"
  },
  AwakerStory_11192_Content = {
    Text = "She treats every person and every Awakener with great kindness, never showing any signs of aggression. Most of the time, she stays quietly in her room, gazing out the window. At her bedside, we discovered several well-worn classical novels, along with handwritten essays and poems on notepaper, written in a delicate, graceful hand.\n\n\"Compared to that Maiden, I am clearly the lucky one.\" She whispered to the shimmering campus pond, facing the setting sun.\n\nShe rarely takes part in outdoor activities—though rather than saying she is unwilling, it might be more accurate to say she simply doesn't know how. That Maiden-like Awakener seems to lack a great deal of common knowledge about everyday life.\n\nOn several occasions, we also witnessed her conversing with the fish in the fountain in a strange sound—like bubbles being exhaled, or the hoarse gurgle of someone drowning. Yet her expression remained calm and serene, as if she were exchanging comfort with a dear friend. In that moment, we all believed she had found true peace."
  },
  AwakerStory_11192_Title = {Text = "Story: II"},
  AwakerStory_11192_UnlockDesc = {
    Text = "Affinity Level 5"
  },
  AwakerStory_11193_Content = {
    Text = "At this point, discussing \"my own life\" with me may be asking too much.\n\nI have grown accustomed to dissipating into the high skies and concealing myself among the stars.\n\nThe person the onlookers are gazing at is not me; I am not the one being played with like a music box, nor the one drifting through the desolate starry sky. That is merely a tool selling its voice for survival, a walking corpse wandering in search of Faint. Only by believing that others' value far surpasses my own can I find meaning in all this effort.\n\nSo, at this point, please don't make me notice myself anymore.\n\n\"But, dear sister, don't dwell on those memories that have already passed.\n\nOpen your eyes and take a look—your one-of-a-kind song has already resounded throughout the universe.\""
  },
  AwakerStory_11193_Title = {Text = "Story: IV"},
  AwakerStory_11193_UnlockDesc = {
    Text = "Affinity Level 9"
  },
  AwakerStory_11195_Content = {
    Text = [[
Alva is very satisfied with her prosthetic limb.

"After that battle, I never imagined I would stand again. It's an honor to have the chance to fight for justice once more."

As for the low moans coming from the dormitory at midnight, just consider them non-existent when the new sun rises above the horizon.]]
  },
  AwakerStory_11195_Title = {
    Text = "Basic Information"
  },
  AwakerStory_11195_UnlockDesc = {
    Text = "Awakener Level 1"
  },
  AwakerStory_11196_Content = {
    Text = [[
Miryam led a simple, ascetic life on campus: solitude, contemplation, silent prayer, cleaning, and labor, repeating daily.

She was indifferent to others' awe, caution, discussions, and curiosity. In the campus far from her homeland, she seemed to have found a new form of spiritual practice.

In fact, she didn't mind conversations. If you were willing to spare some time, she would narrate the greatness of that immortal deity, the distant prehistoric civilizations, and the eternal kingdom ruled by the wise young king. Every time she spoke of it, her eyes would reveal a compassion that the listener could not grasp.

Notably, Miryam showed unusual devotion and respect for Tulu, despite Tulu's indifferent attitude.

If it became necessary to negotiate with Miryam, seeking Tulu's help might bring about a favorable change in the situation.]]
  },
  AwakerStory_11196_Title = {Text = "Story: II"},
  AwakerStory_11196_UnlockDesc = {
    Text = "Affinity Level 5"
  },
  AwakerStory_11197_Content = {
    Text = "Three months after being Awakened, Investigators and Keepers threw a party for Nautila. Not to celebrate her arrival, but to celebrate that she finally remembered the name \"Mythag University.\"\n\nAlthough she forgot it again the next day, parties can always be held again. Who knows? Maybe in another three months, she will truly remember.\n\nIt's hard to say whether Nautila's goldfish-like memory is a side effect of Dissolution or a result of Silver deficiency. However, short-term memory loss isn't entirely a bad thing. For a diligent mechanic, forgetting which screw was tightened means tightening them all over again—ensuring the equipment maintained by her is more durable.\n\nDoll really likes her for it; after all, not everyone has the skill to make machinery last for a decade with just one repair."
  },
  AwakerStory_11197_Title = {Text = "Story: II"},
  AwakerStory_11197_UnlockDesc = {
    Text = "Affinity Level 5"
  },
  AwakerStory_11198_Content = {
    Text = [[
Doll conducted extensive research on her but found no components in her torso, limbs, head, or pelvis that support vocalization. How she speaks remains one of Mythag's many mysteries.

In most cases, she communicates normally with others, but sometimes, the mysterious vocal component seems to have a mind of its own, uttering chilling and eerie words that send shivers down one's spine.]]
  },
  AwakerStory_11198_Title = {
    Text = "Basic Information"
  },
  AwakerStory_11198_UnlockDesc = {
    Text = "Awakener Level 1"
  },
  AwakerStory_11199_Content = {
    Text = "Hannah: Do you remember what happened before your disassembly?\n\nErica: The automaton's behavior began to spiral out of control, consciousness experienced fractures, and during those fractures, it would destroy everything. Everything would perish beneath the currents and flames.\n\nHannah: Erica?\n\nErica: ...\n\nHannah: I can't be that lucky to encounter the \"Tick-Tock Effect,\" right... Erica?\n\nErica: The head component is operational again; I apologize for the inconvenience earlier.\n\nAs I just mentioned, the automaton recognized its increasing threat to humans, and because it still regarded itself as human at that time, it was in great pain.\n\nHannah: You mentioned protection before; does that mean protecting humans?\n\nErica: Yes, the automaton hoped to protect.\n\nHannah: Then why didn't you tell me that just now?\n\nErica: ...\n\nHannah: Do I need to change the question?\n\nErica: No. I am no longer burdened by emotions and can answer.\n\nUpon realizing its own danger, the automaton attempted to short-circuit its body before the consciousness fragmentation to minimize self-inflicted damage.\n\nIn the end, the protection failed, and the human friend died.\n\nThe automaton felt sadness, regret, and despair.\n\nThe automaton self-destructed to ensure it would cause no more destruction, and then the Silver was recovered by Mythag University, creating me, Erica, body number EA307881.\n\n—Excerpt from a recording by Hannah Piszley titled \"0711, Tick-Tock Person Exclusive Interview\""
  },
  AwakerStory_11199_Title = {Text = "Story: IV"},
  AwakerStory_11199_UnlockDesc = {
    Text = "Affinity Level 9"
  },
  AwakerStory_11200_Content = {
    Text = "A fishing village with crystal-clear waters, a shoreline adorned like the Milky Way on a midsummer night, and the lighthearted laughter echoing from a touring caravan—these memories of a world that no longer exists flash back from time to time, only to be promptly cast aside.\n\nAs long as companions keep appearing by her side, new memories can always be made. Besides, the jellyfish are always there—at least, that is what Aurita believes.\n\nAfter all, to drift and propagate, and face down formidable threats through sheer numbers, is both the nature and the destiny of the jellyfish."
  },
  AwakerStory_11200_Title = {Text = "Story: IV"},
  AwakerStory_11200_UnlockDesc = {
    Text = "Affinity Level 9"
  },
  AwakerStory_11201_Content = {
    Text = [[
"Be wary of Pandia. Her danger is not reflected by her appearance. She's a demon."

These are the heartfelt words of countless investigators, born from bitter experience.

Pandia often creates sweet traps, luring other researchers or Awakeners into master-slave Contracts, then mercilessly manipulating their emotions and Souls.

Conversations with Pandia always end fruitlessly. She insists that she is merely spreading joy with her new lovers, and the Contracts are voluntary. After all, she also lets her slaves taste the sweet fruits.

However, there is someone at the school who can counter Pandia. Whenever Sorel passes by Pandia's dormitory, Pandia falls silent, no matter the topic. Rumor has it that Pandia once suffered a major setback while trying to beguile Sorel, but the truth remains a mystery.]]
  },
  AwakerStory_11201_Title = {Text = "Story: II"},
  AwakerStory_11201_UnlockDesc = {
    Text = "Affinity Level 5"
  },
  AwakerStory_11202_Content = {
    Text = "On A.F. 297, @1, @1 03:47, an unexplained explosion occurred southeast of @3 Republic @1@2@1 town. The shockwave triggered a 3.8 magnitude earthquake in the area, noticeable shaking reached villages 5 kilometers away from @1@2@1 town.\n\nAfter the incident, @1@2@1 town lost contact with other regions, and surrounding residents could not recall the town's location. Based on this, the Committee dispatched members for investigation, and dissolution material was detected at the edge of @1@2@1 town.\n\nAfter sealing off the small town, Mythag University investigators performed dissolution body clearing operations and recovered the E-1929 Silver from a strongly dissolved area suspected to be the explosion's center.\n\nE-1929 is particularly unique; its Gnostic index has been in an irregular fluctuation state for an extended period and emits a ticking sound like gears, only maintaining brief stability when linked with mechanical fragments recovered from the strong dissolution area. Based on this characteristic, the Mythag University Awakening Department wrapped E-1929 in mechanical fragments and quickly awakened it once the Gnostic Index tended to stabilize.\n\n—<Italic:\"E-1929 Silver Acquisition and Awakening Report Summary\">"
  },
  AwakerStory_11202_Title = {Text = "Story: I"},
  AwakerStory_11202_UnlockDesc = {
    Text = "Awakener Level 3"
  },
  AwakerStory_11203_Content = {
    Text = "Before the flames of history consumed everything, Agrippa was Capua's crown jewel.\n\nReckless and unrestrained, she fiercely whipped the silent gladiators; she loathed being stared at, as it exposed her inner vulnerability. But when it came to training slaves, Agrippa was an expert. Perhaps you'd be interested in the twenty different whips in her bedroom—specially prepared for you."
  },
  AwakerStory_11203_Title = {
    Text = "Basic Information"
  },
  AwakerStory_11203_UnlockDesc = {
    Text = "Awakener Level 1"
  },
  AwakerStory_11204_Content = {
    Text = "Soft black hair, full cheeks, eyes as bright as gemstones, and rosy lips—from childhood, Karen had always enjoyed special favor due to her natural beauty. By the time she reached adulthood, the gifts and flowers bestowed upon her by men daily could pile into a small mountain at her doorstep. Thus, she was not at all surprised when the palace steward announced she would be brought to the royal court to be trained as a noble handmaiden to the King. Was this not only right? She was born to be envied, born to be extraordinary, and born to be the center of attention.\n\nYet, beauty was the most common currency within the palace walls. No matter how breathtaking a flower from a small town might be, it appeared ordinary and rustic in such a place. Her appearance could no longer buy her special treatment; even the opportunity she craved most—to serve in the Great Hall during the Centennial Feast—was snatched away by another girl.\n\nWhy? Whatever that girl possessed, Karen possessed as well. Why was it not her?\n\nThen, her eyes fell upon the silver ornaments hanging from the other girl’s ears, and she understood.\n\nOn the day of the banquet, she drowned the girl in the lake and donned the silver-white earrings herself. Just as she had envisioned, she became the most radiant among the handmaidens, even earning the privilege of serving at the King’s side. The gazes of envy and jealousy from those around her filled her with an exquisite thrill—yes, yes, this was how it was meant to be. This was the happiest day of her life.\n\nShortly thereafter, she met her end within the emerald mist that swallowed the entire royal city."
  },
  AwakerStory_11204_Title = {Text = "Story: III"},
  AwakerStory_11204_UnlockDesc = {
    Text = "Affinity Level 7"
  },
  AwakerStory_11205_Content = {
    Text = [[
Dreams are projections of memories, reflections of daily life, and a summation of human existence.

Since childhood, Ramona has often had the same dream.

Immersed in warm, turbid water, she felt an intimate connection with something unknown, while hollow and monotonous drumbeats rippled through the water.

Upon waking, she always felt an emptiness, as if something had been taken away or erased from her life.

But to avoid worrying her father and troubling her already busy teachers, Ramona swallowed the questions that nearly escaped her throat and returned to her daily routine.]]
  },
  AwakerStory_11205_Title = {Text = "Story: III"},
  AwakerStory_11205_UnlockDesc = {
    Text = "Affinity Level 7"
  },
  AwakerStory_11206_Content = {
    Text = "Her life's experiences seemed crafted to bring her suffering. Kindness, tolerance, compassion, trust—all the tender aspects of her humanity were torn away, discarded along with gory flesh. \n\nThe word \"forgiveness\" was absent from her vocabulary; only the blood and hatred of others could resolve her own. \n\nBlood for blood, the fairest law revered by both warriors and slaves. \n\nA volcano that had simmered for a thousand years erupted in one night, and a hand crawled out of the underworld onto human soil. \n\nIt was a vengeful spirit, seeking to flood the world with rivers of crimson."
  },
  AwakerStory_11206_Title = {Text = "Story: IV"},
  AwakerStory_11206_UnlockDesc = {
    Text = "Affinity Level 9"
  },
  AwakerStory_11207_Content = {
    Text = [[
"Mommy, Mommy, I didn't cry when I got the shot!"

"You're so brave!"

"Because I knew Mommy was coming back! It didn't hurt at all!"

...

"Master, give me an order."

"Lie down on the operating table; the operation will start in fifteen minutes. Did you take your medicine on time?"

"I did, Master."

"I'll cut you here.  It doesn't hurt, right?"

"... It doesn't hurt, Master."]]
  },
  AwakerStory_11207_Title = {Text = "Story: III"},
  AwakerStory_11207_UnlockDesc = {
    Text = "Affinity Level 7"
  },
  AwakerStory_11207_UnlockDesc_1 = {
    Text = "Complete Chapter 4 \"In Silence\" on Normal difficulty"
  },
  AwakerStory_11208_Content = {
    Text = [[
It seems that Horla possesses a peculiar magic, drawing teachers and students who yearn for poetry and beauty to her side involuntarily.

Horla doesn't like to publish her poems, but the students of Mythag still manage to catch glimpses of her verses. The lines flowing from her pen often sweep across the campus in no time.

As the morning dew rises, someone softly recites her lines under the bell tower; at dusk, Nymphaea sits on a bench in Myda Square, flipping through her collection; after nightfall, students gather in the auditorium to rehearse the chapters she wrote.

However, even when graciously invited, Horla rarely pays attention to these activities, let alone participate in them personally. The mournful tone of those words and tearful occasions often leave her feeling lost.

"Have I spread new sorrow again?"]]
  },
  AwakerStory_11208_Title = {Text = "Story: II"},
  AwakerStory_11208_UnlockDesc = {
    Text = "Affinity Level 5"
  },
  AwakerStory_11209_Content = {
    Text = [[
When Ramona first appeared on campus, it stirred up a huge commotion.

At Mythag University, where Awakeners walked everywhere and peculiar people were common, having silver hair and heterochromia was not noteworthy. What made Ramona the topic of conversation was her identity as the "professor's daughter." 

Everyone crowded outside the mathematics department's office, hoping to catch a glimpse of Miss Dexter. There were so many people that the professor had to seek help from Miss Lotan to disperse the crowd. 

Once Ramona grew a bit older, and the professor finally felt comfortable letting her run around campus, those students who were sent away by Lotan found opportunities to speak to her. 

"What kind of person is the Noble Lady? Sorry, that character doesn't exist yet. I'm an orphan; my father kindly adopted me." 

To escape the entanglement, the little girl calmly revealed the truth, leaving everyone in guilt as she gracefully walked away.]]
  },
  AwakerStory_11209_Title = {Text = "Story: I"},
  AwakerStory_11209_UnlockDesc = {
    Text = "Awakener Level 3"
  },
  AwakerStory_11210_Content = {
    Text = [[
It was... a dazzling daylight and heat wave, an ecstasy of indulgent revelry.

Cheers roared like waves, the warriors bathed in blood and glory in the arena.

The girl returned home reluctantly, still wielding her whip, mercilessly striking the dazed gladiator in front of her.

This was her battlefield.

There were no thrilling duels, no flowers or applause. The tall warriors were the gentlest reindeer; all her curses and fury dissolved into the dark void, leaving not even a whisper of wind.]]
  },
  AwakerStory_11210_Title = {Text = "Story: IV"},
  AwakerStory_11210_UnlockDesc = {
    Text = "Affinity Level 9"
  },
  AwakerStory_11211_Content = {
    Text = "Unlike her obviously petite sister, Tinct's deformity manifests in other ways.\n\nWhether it be mistletoe or hermit crabs, Tinct resembles a spirit body unable to survive without other individuals.\n\nOn the desolate planet, everything she did was to cure Faint's illness; she was willing to try any possible way to sustain her sister's life, even at the cost of enduring what ordinary people could not bear.\n\nShe paid no heed to the nobles' mockery and humiliation, always conducting unequal trades with them calmly and placidly, even pleading for their mercy—which granted her a seat to escape the desolate planet. The moment she secured it, she gave it to Faint without hesitation.\n\nYet, at the last moment, Faint pushed Tinct onto the star stream fleeing the desolate planet—hoping her sister could finally free herself and start anew on a new planet.\n\nHowever, after the desolate planet's annihilation, Tinct embarked on a selfless drifting journey to find Faint, uncaring of being manipulated by others. Such Tinct was discovered by the @2 Church, and subsequently ended up in @3's hands.\n\nTinct never resisted. Rather, she hoped someone would tell her what was best to do—even if it were lies, deception, or an ephemeral illusion, it was better than standing paralyzed with no clue what to do.\n\nAt least, that suggested there was still hope for Faint's future."
  },
  AwakerStory_11211_Title = {Text = "Story: III"},
  AwakerStory_11211_UnlockDesc = {
    Text = "Affinity Level 7"
  },
  AwakerStory_11214_Content = {
    Text = "Hannah: How did you know that Mythag University could help you? You see, the general perception of us has always been \"an obscure, unremarkable university.\" Was it Ramona who told you?\n\nWinkle: Oh no, no, it wasn't. She did lead me in, but Ramona and I never really talk. My species, @1, has the ability of trans-spatial-temporal spiritual migration, so we know many things... Knowledge about Mythag is just one of them.\n\nHannah: So it was through that \"knowledge\" that you knew how to navigate the mist and find your way straight to the gate?\n\nWinkle: I must admit, I didn't know about the mist. I just kept walking, and before I knew it, I was here. Speaking of the mist, do you know how terrifying that stretch of road by the entrance is? There are no streetlights, and when the mist rolls in, even the sunlight dims. And all those dark shadows...\n\nHannah: Is that why you avoid leaving your office? A fear of shadows?\n\nWinkle: Shadows? No, no, you don't understand. It's not just the shadows, there's so much blackness, so many places where it could be hiding...\n\nHannah: It?\n\nWinkle: Shh! Keep your voice down! You'll bring it here—no, it's not intelligent, but why, why is it that even after I reached here, @2@3@1\nHannah: Miss Winkle, are you okay?\n\nWinkle: @2@3@1...\n\nHannah: Miss Winkle?\n\nWinkle: Enough, get out! I'm done with this interview! Your shadow, your recorder, your notes—they're all black, black, black, black! Out, out, OUT!\n\nHannah: Miss Winkle—\n—Transcribed from Hannah Peaslee's recording titled \"<Italic:0810, Winkle Interview (Failed Attempt 1)>\""
  },
  AwakerStory_11214_Title = {Text = "Story: II"},
  AwakerStory_11214_UnlockDesc = {
    Text = "Affinity Level 5"
  },
  AwakerStory_11215_Content = {
    Text = [[
In the "P-063 Opera House @2 Event," a metal box was discovered in a corner of the burnt backstage, and the Silver inside was recovered.

The current instruments at Mythag University are unable to identify the material of the box. After consulting @2 documents and analyzing its decorative engravings, Professor Doll concluded that the box might originate from an extinct civilization that perished in an explosion centuries ago.

The Silver remains quiet and unremarkable while inside the box but emits a continuous humming sound when removed. Professor Doll suspects that the metal box functions as a signal blocker, preventing special frequency signals from resonating with the Silver.

The model of the resonating Silver has also been identified.]]
  },
  AwakerStory_11215_Title = {Text = "Story: I"},
  AwakerStory_11215_UnlockDesc = {
    Text = "Awakener Level 3"
  },
  AwakerStory_11216_Content = {
    Text = "Awakener ID: MA-C06\nDanger Level: A\nSpecial Containment Procedures: MA-C06 is currently housed in Awakener Observation Room 7 with dim lighting. Fearing mind control by @3, MA-C06 refuses to sleep, only provided with a chair.\n\nDue to good behavior and friendly attitude, MA-C06 is allowed to use the greenhouse and explore parts of the campus with an Investigator escort.\n\n—\"Awakener Containment FileMA-C06\""
  },
  AwakerStory_11216_Title = {Text = "Story: I"},
  AwakerStory_11216_UnlockDesc = {
    Text = "Awakener Level 3"
  },
  AwakerStory_11217_Content = {
    Text = [[
Mythag uses the silver extracted from the bodies of the deceased to create the Awakener.

The Sculptors' Association induce the formation of silver from living bodies and refine it into the Awakener.

These are two entirely different ideologies. The latter, while having an extremely high ceiling, clearly violates ethical standards, thus becoming a taboo Research that persists despite prohibitions.

After the Wax Museum incident, 24 was brought back to Mythag. She spent a long time in the campus observation rooms and research labs, necessitating personal supervision whenever she went out.

Undoubtedly, this is an extremely uncontrollable living Awakener. During the subsequent observation period of half a year, 24's body continuously split into many personalities.

She suddenly found herself with unfamiliar friends and enemies, bought many strange items, and even learned to speak Chinese without realizing it.

Her life is never short of "surprises".

"24 is a discrete function composed of a series of isolated points," Doll commented, "Do not believe every word she says."]]
  },
  AwakerStory_11217_Title = {Text = "Story: II"},
  AwakerStory_11217_UnlockDesc = {
    Text = "Affinity Level 5"
  },
  AwakerStory_11218_Content = {
    Text = "\"I'm not an orphan,\" said six-year-old Jenkin. \"My mom just went to work. She'll pick me up after she's done.\"\n\nShe never wavered, nor did she dare to. This belief was the protective incantation she clung to whenever she jolted awake at night from nightmares filled with black slime. It was her only comfort whenever she tried to recall her mother's face but could only see a black shadow.\n\nGritting her teeth, she stood watch at the welfare home's gate through spring, summer, autumn, and winter. Only on the morning the home closed down did she wipe away her unseen tears and leave with her mouse friend.\n\n\"I am an orphan,\" said ten-year-old Jenkin. \"I don't have parents. I only have Brown.\"\n\nShe told this to herself and the mouse perched on her shoulder. It was true—people might be wary of children suddenly approaching; East End street children were infamous throughout Londinium—but no one suspected a mouse scurrying by their feet. Through this tacit cooperation, the girl occasionally enjoyed a full meal, and dreamed in the sewers of fireplaces and pastries.\n\nYet the bitter winter spared no one. It brought her sickness and high fever, bringing the Grim Reaper to a halt by her side. The girl lay dying, with only the mouse circling frantically about her, hoping for any attention at all.\n\nA young woman stopped and wrapped the girl in a warm embrace.\n\n\"I'm not an orphan,\" said thirteen-year-old Jenkin. \"I have my sister Mason and my best friend Brown!\"\n\nThe girl stood before an old house, holding the mouse close, her face bright with a radiant smile."
  },
  AwakerStory_11218_Title = {Text = "Story: III"},
  AwakerStory_11218_UnlockDesc = {
    Text = "Affinity Level 7"
  },
  AwakerStory_11219_Content = {
    Text = [[
When occupying Ramona's body, "Ramona" has never walked through the campus.

Lotan's boldness, Ogier's shy loyalty, William's calm composure, Doll's strict seriousness... No one remembers these moments more than she does.

But she always kept in mind: these beautiful things no longer belong to her.

Now, she needs to focus entirely on protecting another destined person... This is also to protect another precarious world and another innocent version of herself.]]
  },
  AwakerStory_11219_Title = {Text = "Story: IV"},
  AwakerStory_11219_UnlockDesc = {
    Text = "Affinity Level 9"
  },
  AwakerStory_11220_Content = {
    Text = "Jenkin's overly nimble hands once raised concerns that she'd become a fixture in the <Italic:Mythag Daily>—not as an interviewee, but as the mastermind behind several thefts.\n\nThough she did become a regular of the paper, it wasn't due to old habits. Provided there were enough pastries, even a master street survivalist was willing to set aside her former trade and enjoy a well-earned retirement alongside her mouse buddy.\n\nThe real reason she appeared in the paper so often? The editor pays far too generously.\n\nShh—keep your voice down, you never know where she might be, ready to trade what she's overheard with Hannahh for more candies and cakes."
  },
  AwakerStory_11220_Title = {Text = "Story: II"},
  AwakerStory_11220_UnlockDesc = {
    Text = "Affinity Level 5"
  },
  AwakerStory_11221_Content = {
    Text = "A new star of science and knowledge rises in an ordinary worker's family.\n\nMost of Doll's childhood was filled with the sounds of cylinder throbs and gear operations.\n\nBut a love for machinery was not enough to support the girl in climbing the rugged and steep mountain of science.\n\nWhat led her onto the path of knowledge was a plague.\n\nAn unknown madness raged through the city; hospitals were overcrowded, the morgue was overwhelmed, and everyone was on edge.\n\n\"The city's graveyards aren't enough—dig up grandma or burn mom, you have to choose one.\"\n\nThus, Doll watched her mother disappear into the flames.\n\nUnlike others who were cremated, among the fragments and ashes she once called \"mother,\" there flowed a shimmering silver mass.\n\n\"I want to know if I can see her again.\"\n\n\"I want to know if her kind soul is inside that.\"\n\n\"I want to know if that silver substance is the genesis of life, if it is the essence of the soul.\"\n\n\"I want to know if everything in this world has a common starting point.\"\n\nBefore getting the answers, Doll will not bow to the D-phenomenon."
  },
  AwakerStory_11221_Title = {Text = "Story: IV"},
  AwakerStory_11221_UnlockDesc = {
    Text = "Affinity Level 9"
  },
  AwakerStory_11222_Content = {
    Text = [[
Her ethereal beauty is always reminiscent of the bird of heaven, spreading its glossy wings towards utopia as her white dress flutters with caressing breezes.

However, does the girl who perches on the mast ever imagine herself flying in the azure sky?]]
  },
  AwakerStory_11222_Title = {
    Text = "Basic Information"
  },
  AwakerStory_11222_UnlockDesc = {
    Text = "Awakener Level 1"
  },
  AwakerStory_11223_Content = {
    Text = [[
Ruby earrings, sapphire necklaces, beautiful hair accessories woven from garnet and malachite... How dazzling, how beautiful, how full of charm they are! Wherever they appear, people flock to them.

These jewelry pendants are not mere "decorative items," no, they are the true stars of the world. Noble ladies wearing turquoise necklaces are immortalized in songs by poets; elderly ladies adorned with emeralds are seen as symbols of nobility. Even those lowborn girls, with a cheap bracelet on their wrist, can earn the endearing title of "Pearl Girl," attracting countless gazes.

Even dry branches and putrid bones can become objects of everyone's desire when adorned with a string of beautiful jewels.

If she could wear those necklaces and earrings, those bracelets and headpieces, surely she would become the center of attention as well.]]
  },
  AwakerStory_11223_Title = {Text = "Story: IV"},
  AwakerStory_11223_UnlockDesc = {
    Text = "Affinity Level 9"
  },
  AwakerStory_11224_Content = {
    Text = [[
A silver tongue is the nectar of a rosebud; lords and courtiers, the bees and butterflies that dance around its swaying bloom.

The thorns fed by desire have crept up on the rose window, coiling tightly around it.

People may gossip behind her back, and the crown may leave her hands torn and bleeding, but she will never relinquish the power she has drawn into her arms.

After all, this is the nourishment a rose truly needs to bloom.]]
  },
  AwakerStory_11224_Title = {
    Text = "Basic Information"
  },
  AwakerStory_11224_UnlockDesc = {
    Text = "Awakener Level 1"
  },
  AwakerStory_11225_Content = {
    Text = "Under the care and tutelage of that lady, she grew into someone kind and gentle, like a true noblewoman. Yet a single act of unwitting kindness toward a Slave was all it took for her \"parents\" to cast her aside without mercy.\n\nThe Spartans had never accepted her, and all her own kin despised her to the bone.\n\nIn an instant, she became a traitor in Everyone's eyes, stripped of any place where she could belong.\n\nIn that prison, every person radiated a thick malice, like some contagious plague—even though none of them had ever met before.\n\nThe endless torment in that sunless hell felt like eternity. She grew neurotically terrified of anyone approaching, unable to sleep each night. Only when she occasionally Fainted could she close her eyes in peace—yet upon opening them, she would plunge once more into an endless nightmare.\n\nWhat had she done wrong? How had everything come to this?\n\nHer Resentment drifted aimlessly with nowhere to settle, unable to untangle the logic of Fate.\n\nWas it because she was guilty?\n\nBut if she was guilty, then the guilt of Everyone else was tenfold.\n\nThat hatred accumulated day by day into bitter fury, and the endless Anger Burning through her Blood night after night finally, one day, incinerated the cage that held her.\n\nThe chains that had been Entwined around her for years now coiled around one screaming throat after another. Over the years, the chains had long since merged with her body—they fit her hands perfectly. Gripping those blood-soaked chains, she hunted down one filthy soul after another.\n\nRed, red, warm red, reeking red.\n\nSee? She knew it all along—not a single soul among them was pure."
  },
  AwakerStory_11225_Title = {Text = "Story: III"},
  AwakerStory_11225_UnlockDesc = {
    Text = "Affinity Level 7"
  },
  AwakerStory_11226_Content = {
    Text = [[
She knows everything.

She knows the bell tower rings in emergencies, that the Eridanus meteor shower will return in ten years, and that she possesses a unique power.

She knows nothing.

She doesn't know the secret spice in the cafeteria's curry recipe, how to calculate the radius of a planet after its annihilation, or the direction her future will take.

She finds it hard to let go of everything around her, yet cannot resist the path her intuition reveals.

On the journey toward truth and normalcy, Ramona needs steadfast companions to help her secure the road back to everyday life.]]
  },
  AwakerStory_11226_Title = {Text = "Story: IV"},
  AwakerStory_11226_UnlockDesc = {
    Text = "Affinity Level 9"
  },
  AwakerStory_11227_Content = {
    Text = [[
If only she had not awakened, those who are lost in the abyss should not gaze directly at the dazzling sun wheel.  

She should be a numb experiment material, someone buried by this world, and should not possess the perception of pain or the desire to be loved.  

Her mother's lingering attachment created the tragedy of her life, while Lily is still caught in the confusion of "whether to obey the arrangement of the world."  

Perhaps one day, she will find the answer from someone who defies fate]]
  },
  AwakerStory_11227_Title = {Text = "Story: IV"},
  AwakerStory_11227_UnlockDesc = {
    Text = "Affinity Level 9"
  },
  AwakerStory_11227_UnlockDesc_1 = {
    Text = "Complete Chapter 4 \"In Silence\" on Normal difficulty"
  },
  AwakerStory_11228_Content = {
    Text = "I seem to be involved in some supernatural event, recording all my findings here...\n\nWe were finishing our archaeology at Evrotas when I woke up and found the rest of the team had vanished, and the town looked like it reverted to a thousand years ago overnight.\n\nAncient ruins had risen, restoring the town to its original state, including countless residents turned to skeletons.\n\nExcitement, shock, and fear gripped my mind. Despite having seen countless skeletons, I tremble at the sight before me. Anyone experiencing this would be even more terrified.\n\nEveryone in this town seemed to have been brutally massacred by one person. Skeletons lay in the streets, in houses. The town gate is inexplicably tightly closed, and bodies trying to escape but brutally killed piled up by the gate, forming a small hill of bones.\n\nI found no exceptions, men, women, old people, children... so many were killed by a massive blunt weapon, their bodies or heads smashed. Staring at the dry bones, I almost saw the blood flowing.\n\nWhat happened here?\n\n...\n\nI searched aimlessly, found no clues until I entered the prison.\n\nThe sight there was particularly gruesome, the perpetrator destroyed the entire prison in great anger. The walls had twisted, brownish words, seeming to be written in blood by someone dying, I carefully distinguished, it seemed to read \"evil spirit\".\n\nEvil spirit? Does this refer to the killer, or did the town truly experience some supernatural event?\n\nIndeed, slaughtering the entire town alone is unimaginable, only a true ghost could ruthlessly take so many lives.\n\nAfter leaving the prison, the town seemed to have subtly changed, I could smell a faint bloody scent.\n\nWhile I sought a way out, the sudden sound of chains echoed through the town, as if someone was dragging something heavy forward.\n\nEvil spirit! It's the evil spirit... it's after me! I ran desperately, but the horrifying chain sound followed me everywhere.\n\nI was exhausted, hid under a table in a home, locked the door, but the chain sound still chased me. I heard it coming closer...\n\nI wish this were just a dream, that everything would disappear when I wake up, wait... the sound seems to be gone, maybe the spirit has left?\n\n...\n\nResearcher Note: The normal handwriting ends here, only three twisted words remain, roughly deciphered as:\nThe door opened\n—Excerpt from a deceased archaeologist's diary in the Evrotas Archaeological Team"
  },
  AwakerStory_11228_Title = {Text = "Story: I"},
  AwakerStory_11228_UnlockDesc = {
    Text = "Awakener Level 3"
  },
  AwakerStory_11229_Content = {
    Text = "Even when the gladiators burned the training ground and hung her parents' heads high on the wall, Agrippa couldn't believe it—how could these lowly, meek slaves have such audacity?\n\nIn Rome, there were two kinds of people: those who enslave and those who are enslaved.\n\nAgrippa was fortunate. She was the daughter of the largest gladiator training ground owner in Capua. She roamed freely, fearing nothing, doing as she pleased.\n\nBut now, she's like a frightened rabbit, cowering in the basement, with the revelry outside seeming like Hell.\n\nSlave rebellion. Such a foreign term. Agrippa is only fifteen; there's so much in this world she doesn't understand.\n\nIn the shadows, she sees a pair of red glowing eyes. It's Uvhash, the greatest money-maker in the training ground, locked underground due to its danger.\n\nThey never got along, and no one knows what they discussed that night. After the bloody night of flames, Agrippa was found dead in the dark depths, completely alone. She wasn't killed by slaves—someone drained her blood entirely.\n\nOf course, her head was eventually severed too, hung next to her parents', facing Rome."
  },
  AwakerStory_11229_Title = {Text = "Story: III"},
  AwakerStory_11229_UnlockDesc = {
    Text = "Affinity Level 7"
  },
  AwakerStory_11230_Content = {
    Text = "Hannah: In your view, is there any difference between the automaton you once were and the you now?\n\nErica: The former me retained \"emotions.\" \n\nHannah: What kind of emotions specifically, if you are willing to share?\n\nErica: I'm sorry, I don't understand your question.\n\nHannah: Uh, that is, if you feel this question is too personal, you don't have to answer.\n\nErica: I cannot perceive \"willingness or not,\" I'm very sorry.\n\nHannah: Then... could you tell me what your emotions were at that time?\n\nErica: The corporeal me survived the explosion: happiness, information.\n\nRealizing my spirit was transferred and preserved onto the automaton: nervousness, excitement.\n\nNoticing consciousness gradually slipping out of control and a strong desire for destruction arising: nervousness, fear, protection.\n\nHannah: Protection?\n\nErica: I'm very sorry, detailed information has been lost.\n\nHannah: Then let's change the question; this is something our readers wish to know as well. Why do you not have emotions now? What happened?\n\nErica: For unknown reasons, I was unable to restore sanity through the spirit link. The university took necessary measures to suppress all emotions with Silver devices, reducing aggressiveness and danger while retaining intelligence and utility.\n\n—Excerpt from \"Mythag Daily,\" \"Awakeners' Faculty Interview: Tick-Tock Person\""
  },
  AwakerStory_11230_Title = {Text = "Story: III"},
  AwakerStory_11230_UnlockDesc = {
    Text = "Affinity Level 7"
  },
  AwakerStory_11231_Content = {
    Text = "During the investigation along the southern coast of Cornwall, I discovered a derelict village unmarked on any known map. Upon investigation, we confirmed that it had been \"erased\" by an outbreak of dissolution.\n\nIn the village, we collected a large number of anomalous marine specimens, including carnivorous giant clams, heat-resistant sea angels, and most baffling of all, \"amphibious jellyfish\" found everywhere.\n\nIn a dilapidated house that had become a jellyfish nest, we recovered a fluid Silver Core weighing approximately 11.85 drams. While extracting the core, our team was attacked by mutated jellyfish; fortunately, their glands had decayed, posing no neurotoxic threat.\n\n—<Italic:Record of the Third Biology Department Field Survey, A.F. 308>"
  },
  AwakerStory_11231_Title = {Text = "Story: I"},
  AwakerStory_11231_UnlockDesc = {
    Text = "Affinity Level 3"
  },
  AwakerStory_11232_Content = {
    Text = [[
Fearful of light, fearful of gaze, fearful of love, fearful of embrace.

Desiring light, desiring gaze, desiring love, desiring embrace.

If only I could avoid harming others, if only I wouldn't trouble others, if only I were as smart as Tiuog, if only I were as brave as Jenkin...

Then I wouldn't be scorched by the blazing sun, nor despised by others, right?

With unfounded worries, the doll cautiously reached out its pale, almost translucent hand from the shadow into the sunlight.]]
  },
  AwakerStory_11232_Title = {Text = "Story: IV"},
  AwakerStory_11232_UnlockDesc = {
    Text = "Affinity Level 9"
  },
  AwakerStory_11233_Content = {
    Text = "She dances within the embrace of green flames, their dim flickering light falling across the dancer's young, devotion-filled face. With every turn, the emerald fire ignites the souls of the wicked, burning away every impurity upon the stage."
  },
  AwakerStory_11233_Title = {
    Text = "Basic Information"
  },
  AwakerStory_11233_UnlockDesc = {
    Text = "Awakener Level 1"
  },
  AwakerStory_11234_Content = {
    Text = "March\nWelcome to the Atlantica Touring Aquarium! I'm Aurita, your guide for today—please watch your step as you board the jellyfish caravan!\n\nDisplayed here in the tanks are rare jellyfish from tropical waters. Ta-da! Please take a look—\n\nApril\nWh-what happened... Where did everyone go... Curator! Curator! The jellyfish—Aurita's jellyfish are all gone!\n\nThe aquarium never had jellyfish exhibits? But I clearly remember...\n\nMay\nSince there are too few exhibits and no guests, we can't keep the business going... <Italic:sob>... Goodbye, everyone...\n\nIf—if we ever go on tour again someday, please come find Aurita!\n\nJune\nAurita is so tired... Am I sick...?\n\nOh...! The jellyfish! Sorry, Aurita can't scatter diatoms for you all right now.\n\nOnce Aurita feels better, let's all swim together again..."
  },
  AwakerStory_11234_Title = {Text = "Story: III"},
  AwakerStory_11234_UnlockDesc = {
    Text = "Affinity Level 7"
  },
  AwakerStory_11235_Content = {
    Text = [[
On the thirty-first day following the celestial bird, Sona-Nyl sails into a sea shrouded by streaming mist.

Celeste perches high on the mast, gazing upon her people below. Notes of the lutanist drift in sweet melodies. Songs praying for a smooth journey echo betwixt.

She does not aware of their destination, nor does she evaluate how much wealth and fame bestowing across the sea. She does not care whether the prayers are pious, nor does she unsettled by the rumors about her power, circulating surreptitiously around the sea. Being asked to bless the voyage, she does not need words to complete her duty.

And when the music ceases and the mist lifts, the sailors behold only a resistless raging sea. Lightning tears through the sky. Black rain pours down, bursting thunders of gigantic spray. Rushing torrent captures the fragile barque and throws it into the gaping abyss.

"God has forsaken us!" Kindreds scream in desperation. Bellows imprison her into the lightless dungeon.

Neglected and derelicted, the protector is left alone unquestioned with her failed duty, and one last lingering confusion.

Why... why did the barque sink?

The chain that once manacled her to the mast drown into the roaring splash. She plummets into the depth...

Like a white bird with snapped wings flaking from the sky.]]
  },
  AwakerStory_11235_Title = {Text = "Story: III"},
  AwakerStory_11235_UnlockDesc = {
    Text = "Affinity Level 7"
  },
  AwakerStory_11236_Content = {
    Text = "He is but a giant. His silhouette awing, his power indestructible. His weapon a colossal blade that no one else can lift. His victories, gleaming like oiled fur on the blade's fang, nourished by countless wars and savage sacrifices. His prize, a mountain of heads severed from his enemies and kin, crowned only by his own head on top."
  },
  AwakerStory_11236_Title = {
    Text = "Basic Information"
  },
  AwakerStory_11236_UnlockDesc = {
    Text = "Awakener Level 1"
  },
  AwakerStory_11237_Content = {
    Text = "Report on Anomalous Events in the Londinium Church District (Confidential)\n\nA.F. 315, February 3rd: During the anomalous event in the Londinium Church District, Bishop Salvador utilized the power of \"The Blessing\" to heal the Mythag Keeper and the residents of Londinium, exposing his identity as an Awakener in the process.\n\nDue to the insufficient spirit power of the linker, Bishop Salvador chose to exhaust himself to sustain \"The Blessing\" until the Keeper and the Awakener Ogier shattered the core of said anomaly—the Ritual Mirror. Subsequently, the Keeper took over Salvador's link, and \"The Blessing\" healed all individuals present, preventing any casualties.\n\nIt was discovered that Bishop Salvador's original linker was the former Bishop of the Church District, now the Archbishop of Londinium ■■■■■.\n\nIn A.F. 300, the Archbishop had accidentally awakened Salvador after coming into contact with the Holy Ash. Over the next five years, Salvador had served as an assistant priest in the Church District, succeeding him as the Bishop of the Church District following ■■■■■'s promotion.\n\nAfter the incident, the Keeper agreed to keep Bishop Salvador's Awakener identity confidential; thus, this information was not shared with the Mystia Treaty Committee. Apart from the core personnel of Mythag University, no one is currently aware of his identity as an Awakener."
  },
  AwakerStory_11237_Title = {Text = "Story: I"},
  AwakerStory_11237_UnlockDesc = {
    Text = "Affinity Level 3"
  },
  AwakerStory_11238_Content = {
    Text = "On a snowy day that November, 24 fell ill.\n\nAfter a week of grueling work, she came down with a severe fever and lay in bed for days on end.\n\nIn her daze, she seemed to hear little mice whimpering near her ears. After an unknown stretch of time, someone was standing at her bedside.\n\nShe recognized those eyes—it was the child from the sewer. Covered in mud, the child held out a grimy little pill to 24.\n\n\"For you. Take it,\" the child said bluntly, her voice surprisingly pleasant—so it turned out she was a girl.\n\n24 looked at the scrapes on her elbow and face but did not ask where the pill had come from. She simply held the girl's hand tightly.\n\nThe girl mumbled awkwardly, then said in a cool tone, \"I won't leave. I'll go once you're better.\"\n\nEven when I'm better—don't leave.\n\n24 answered silently, in her heart.\n\nThe first snow of winter fell over Londinium for an entire week. On the day it finally stopped, 24 was very happy—because not only had her fever broken, but she had also gained a sister."
  },
  AwakerStory_11238_Title = {Text = "Story: IV"},
  AwakerStory_11238_UnlockDesc = {
    Text = "Affinity Level 9"
  },
  AwakerStory_11238_UnlockDesc_1 = {
    Text = "Complete Chapter 2 \"Waxen Legacy\" on Normal difficulty"
  },
  AwakerStory_11239_Content = {
    Text = [[
"O sinners, this is the abyss of Desire, the bottom of Hell. The black hound roars here, the stench spreads here, and the death knell tolls here. You have gathered here due to your indulgent desires and cruel actions, and what awaits you is suffering and death."

Pandia once served in Newgate Prison, the most oppressive, gloomy, and sunless filthy corner of Londinium. Once bloodied heavy criminals were shackled and stripped of their dignity, kneeling to her in the Maze-like cell area, kissing her leather boots, humbly calling themselves her servants.

Whenever a new execution took place, she would summon new death row inmates, asking them to appreciate their own demise. As the executed squirmed in the hemp rope, she liked to sit high up, watching the worst of the worst tremble in fear and desperation.

But there was also a "Hell Cat" who observed that Pandia came to the iron gate of Newgate Prison countless times, tiptoeing to gaze outside London, as if waiting for a visitor from afar.

"In fact, I too can only be, a part of the miserable dark and damp dungeon that I can never escape."]]
  },
  AwakerStory_11239_Title = {Text = "Story: III"},
  AwakerStory_11239_UnlockDesc = {
    Text = "Affinity Level 7"
  },
  AwakerStory_11240_Content = {
    Text = [[
On July 3, A.F.3@1, being invited by the Nathaniel Forbes Green Foundation, Mythag University participated in the investigation towards the "ghost ship" Sona-Nyl.

Upon boarding the barque which had been declared sunk ten years ago, the communication signal from investigator Fingal Johansen had immediately out of reach.

On July 10, A.F.3@1, the university eventually managed to get him. Located at the northern shore of Leo Heights with 300 nautical miles away from the original destination, investigator Johansen declared that he lost sense of time and space at the second he stepped on Sona-Nyl, and could not recall anything that happened onboard.

Investigator Johansen can hitherto only vaguely remember a word: Elysian.

Due to the unharmful nature of the ghost ship itself, Mythag University decide to terminate the investigation today (A.F.3@1 year, December 24).

"File: Investigation of the Sona-Nyl Crash."]]
  },
  AwakerStory_11240_Title = {Text = "Story: I"},
  AwakerStory_11240_UnlockDesc = {
    Text = "Affinity Level 3"
  },
  AwakerStory_11241_Content = {
    Text = "Street life was never difficult for her.\n\nWhen hungry, she looked for work; if there were no jobs, she resorted to her own \"handiwork\" to get by. She and Brown worked in such perfect sync that they could scrape by without anyone else's help.\n\n/n\"We don't need anyone,\" she vowed, the mouse on her shoulder squeaking in agreement. \"We only need each other.\"\n\nBut every snowy night, she could not help but gaze at those windows glowing with warm yellow light, watching the people inside embrace and share warm wishes over a meager dinner.\n\nIt wasn't that she needed a roof over her head or soft pillows on a luxurious bed—she already had a companion she could trust. Yet she remained curious: what did it feel like to have a home for good?\n\nThat question found its answer the day Mason adopted her."
  },
  AwakerStory_11241_Title = {Text = "Story: IV"},
  AwakerStory_11241_UnlockDesc = {
    Text = "Affinity Level 9"
  },
  AwakerStory_11242_Content = {
    Text = [[
"Ramona" shows great restraint in appearing. As she mentioned, she only manifests in this world when called by the Keeper.

She always comes and goes swiftly, seemingly not wanting to engage further with our world beyond battle.

Is it fear of the nightmares that plague her? Or fear of longing for the things she has lost... We cannot know.]]
  },
  AwakerStory_11242_Title = {Text = "Story: II"},
  AwakerStory_11242_UnlockDesc = {
    Text = "Affinity Level 5"
  },
  AwakerStory_11243_Content = {
    Text = "A.F. 1@2/@1/@1 10:31 AM, the police received a report of multiple bloodstains discovered within @1@1 Manor. Detective Belford immediately headed to the scene, began an investigation, and found an unidentified bluish-green slime within the bloodstains.\n\n13:44, Detective Belford submitted the report, and the Mystia Treaty Committee promptly took over the case.\n\n14:25, the seventh response team of the committee arrived at the manor, controlled the related personnel, and sealed off the site. Based on the situation at the scene, the team leader speculated that there were at least five victims within the manor, and multiple instances of D-phenomenon were observed.\n\n18:00, investigators from Mythag University arrived at the scene, confirmed the existence of the D-phenomenon, and entered the manor with the Awakener for cleanup and investigation.\n\n23:11, the cleanup of the manor was completed. Investigators discovered a large number of mystical documents and ritual materials in the basement and study's secret room, and found an incomplete Awakener. The Awakener identified herself as \"Maid Karen,\" the chief maid of @3 Duke. When discovered, the Awakener was dressed in a maid's uniform, adorned with various styles of jewelry, and was working very hard to clean the basement. This Awakener had a human form, bluish-green skin, and semi-transparent adhesive-like extremities, suspected to be an incomplete or erroneously summoned product. The slime secreted from her matched in texture and color with the substance found on the severed limbs.\n\nThe investigators questioned her, and Maid Karen admitted to @1 facts and expressed that everything was to gain her master's attention. Upon learning that @3 Duke would be arrested, she murmured, \"Then where is my new master?\" and then disassembled into gel, leaving behind a Silver.\n\n01:37, the team leader of the seventh response team interrogated the related personnel and detained @1@1 Manor's owner, @3 Duke, according to the \"Treaty.\" \n\n03:09, investigators returned to Mythag University and logged the K-033 Silver into the database.\n\n—\"Incident Report of @1@1 Manor\""
  },
  AwakerStory_11243_Title = {Text = "Story: I"},
  AwakerStory_11243_UnlockDesc = {
    Text = "Affinity Level 3"
  },
  AwakerStory_11244_Content = {
    Text = "A.F. 3@2, a D-phenomenon occurred in coastal towns of the Agló Republic, spreading outward in a spiral from the port, affecting an area hundreds of meters wide and causing @1 deaths.\n\nInvestigations traced the phenomenon back to a fishing boat that set out on A.F. 3@2 @1 @1@1, catching a silver-patterned cod-like creature.\n\nThe creature's soft body ruptured when cut by a sharp tool, releasing fluid laden with shell fragments and other residues. Upon reaching the port, shell-like growths had appeared among the catch but were ignored until a fisherman perceived himself as a shell, twisting his body and ending up hospitalized. Only then was the event reported.\n\nMythag personnel later located the source of the phenomenon at @4 cannery, removed it, and secured Silver O-36.\n\n—<Italic:\"Awakening System Silver Acquisition Report: O-36\">"
  },
  AwakerStory_11244_Title = {Text = "Story: I"},
  AwakerStory_11244_UnlockDesc = {
    Text = "Awakener Level 3"
  },
  AwakerStory_11245_Content = {
    Text = [[
Jenkin pressed against the crack of the door to the counseling room, straining to listen.

Sylvia's voice was gentle and warm, while Aigis's sounded like a mosquito's whimper, intermittent and hard to decipher.

"Aigis, you need to learn to say no."

"But I... don't want to be a burden... I want to... repay..."

"Aigis hasn't been a burden to anyone. You see, Keeper allows you to move freely in school without any restrictions, isn't that a sign of trust?"

"You promised me not to casually agree to unreasonable requests from others. Especially from Caraboo, helping her with her confinement and cleaning will only cause trouble for our Keeper, okay?"

"Jenkin, how did you get in here?"

"J-Jenkin! I... I agreed to Caraboo myself! C-Calm down!"]]
  },
  AwakerStory_11245_Title = {Text = "Story: II"},
  AwakerStory_11245_UnlockDesc = {
    Text = "Affinity Level 5"
  },
  AwakerStory_11245_UnlockDesc_1 = {
    Text = "Complete Chapter 1 \"East District's Enigma\": Normal"
  },
  AwakerStory_11246_Content = {
    Text = "Winkle once had a name of her own.\n\nA name once steeped in her parents' tender love,\nOnce written over and over by friends, woven into memories,\nAnd marked upon the calendar alongside her birthday.\n\nWinkle once had a face of her own.\n\nA face that once grew under her parents' watchful gaze,\nThat once beamed with joy and softened with sorrow in the company of friends,\nAnd was captured in photographs alongside those memories.\n\nWinkle once had a home of her own,\nVastly distant from Kadath, and bearing no resemblance to it.\n\nIn the end, it perished alongside her parents' very existence—\nSwallowed by the blackness of @2, then utterly annihilated.\n\nWinkle had a profound and heavy fear.\n\nIt is pitch-black, horrific, all-consuming, and utterly irrational.\n\nIt dissolves and erodes everything, wearing it down to nothing;\nOnce tainted, one's very existence turns to ash.\n\nWinkle is left with only a name that once belonged to her.\n\nA name the human tongue cannot utter, nor even mimic.\n\nShe can only close her eyes in moments of absolute exhaustion,\nPraying for a dreamland where she might hear that familiar calling once more."
  },
  AwakerStory_11246_Title = {Text = "Story: III"},
  AwakerStory_11246_UnlockDesc = {
    Text = "Affinity Level 7"
  },
  AwakerStory_11247_Content = {
    Text = "She was born before recorded human history, in an ancient civilization that can no longer be verified.\n\nThere, the people from the stars built glorious realms and temples dedicated to immortal gods. She grew up immersed in faith, devout from a young age, determined to become an apostle of the gods.\n\nHowever, divine callings are not easily attained; she yearned for miracles and wonders but never witnessed any.\n\nIt was not until Tulu ascended to the throne that she finally rose to the position of high priestess—an unforgettable moment filled with profound ecstasy and joy that shook her very spirit.\n\nShe finally witnessed a miracle and understood the truth: this young king was the embodiment of the immortal she had longed for.\n\nYears later, a catastrophic flood destroyed their civilization. She heard the final prophecy about immortality from Tulu and returned to the temple to pray until her last breath.\n\nAfter countless ages, new humans repopulated the land, and the events of prehistory were forgotten.\n\nThus, Miryam's trials had only just begun."
  },
  AwakerStory_11247_Title = {Text = "Story: III"},
  AwakerStory_11247_UnlockDesc = {
    Text = "Affinity Level 7"
  },
  AwakerStory_11248_Content = {
    Text = "Survival is both an instinct and an unshakeable burden. In the face of a death that erases even memory, she alone is the proof that they ever existed—her parents, her friends, everything from her homeland.\n\nSo, she fled. She fled to an untainted world, to this ocean-covered planet, finding new life in the body of a deceased human girl.\n\nBut the black death has infinite patience.\n\nHuman eyes cannot see Dissolution, but she knew precisely what the chill at the edge of consciousness meant, what the darkness creeping through her mind signified—what humans call Dissolution has caught up, and without her knowing, had pinned her spirit and body together.\n\nAgain and again she tried to flee, and again and again she failed. Ultimately, utterly spent and with her mind pushed to its absolute limit, she could only drag her body toward the one place that might offer her salvation.\n\nNo matter the cost, she only wishes to live."
  },
  AwakerStory_11248_Title = {Text = "Story: IV"},
  AwakerStory_11248_UnlockDesc = {
    Text = "Affinity Level 9"
  },
  AwakerStory_11249_Content = {
    Text = "Ryker is known as the \"Lucky Detective\" by his detective friends.\n\nAs the name suggests, he is a lucky person: whenever he places a bet, he wins ten times the stake; whenever he guesses, he chooses the right answer.\n\nThe \"Lucky Detective\" doesn't have to be an actual detective; he‘s solved many cases by chance alone, so he was embraced on this path.\n\nHe doesn't solve cases by deduction, relying on luck instead. Just a tour around the crime scene and he stumbles upon the culprit; just walking along the road, he picks up key evidence.\n\nWith such good fortune, he's lived out a smooth twenty-five years.\n\nHe never worries about yesterday, nor frets about tomorrow."
  },
  AwakerStory_11249_Title = {
    Text = "Basic Information"
  },
  AwakerStory_11249_UnlockDesc = {
    Text = "Awakener Level 1"
  },
  AwakerStory_11251_Content = {
    Text = "April 1, A.F. 3@2, Silver Core Storage and Management Room, Mythag University Awakener Department, Londinium\nSilver Core G411, along with Silver Core G410, was purchased by Lord Dexter from the \"Lady Narcissus.\" The core measures 1.85 cm in length and 0.4 cm at its widest point, with a shape resembling a rhombohedron. Regardless of the angle or position from which it is observed, G411 emits bright yellow rhomboid ripples that radiate outward from the observer's visual focal point.\n\nProlonged observation may cause the observer to experience mental disorientation, diminished emotional responsiveness, and even lead to Puppetman Syndrome (potential symptoms include complete emotional apathy, loss of volition, severe malnutrition or even death resulting from suppressed appetite). Prompt psychological and emotional intervention is required should such symptoms manifest.\n\nAlthough its negative effects are milder compared to most Silver Cores, hermetic containment is strongly advised. Direct observation upon retrieval should be strictly avoided to mitigate the risk of G411-induced affective disorder.\n\n—Excerpt from <Italic:Mythag University Silver Core Storage Records>"
  },
  AwakerStory_11251_Title = {Text = "Story: I"},
  AwakerStory_11251_UnlockDesc = {
    Text = "Affinity Level 3"
  },
  AwakerStory_11252_Content = {
    Text = [[
Since the day she entered the prison, her memories have been stained with blood. 

The once mundane and warm recollections now feel like false dreams, blurred and cracked, turning into sharp Fragments embedded in her Caro. 

She can no longer recall the gentle embrace or caring faces; only eternal hatred and Question remain in her heart. 

Pain, humiliation, Betrayal... What caused all this suffering? 

She asks herself daily, but until freedom arrives, no one answers. 

So, she decides to seek the answers herself, interrogating every dirty heart torn from their screaming chests.]]
  },
  AwakerStory_11252_Title = {
    Text = "Basic Information"
  },
  AwakerStory_11252_UnlockDesc = {
    Text = "Awakener Level 1"
  },
  AwakerStory_11253_Content = {
    Text = [[
The small soul, which should have been lost to the river of history, relied on her mother's wish, the abundant spiritual energy from establishing the magic circle with @1@2@1, and the fusion with the giant creature frozen beneath Elworth, resurrecting as the monster "Lily".

Due to incomplete awakening, Lily at the beginning had no consciousness, merely a combat doll that obeyed orders.

Francis Oswood, a member of the Sculptors' Association, used Lily as a prototype to conduct illegal experiments lasting @2 years. From Francis's diary, it was known that Lily's state back then was extremely unstable, often going out of control and causing localized destruction, which forced Francis to frequently change residences.

With the intake of the gnosis elixir and the implantation of the silver chip, Lily regained her perception and some memories on an undocumented day. After some twists and turns, Francis took over the almost bankrupt Lai Hospital and transformed it into a testing ground.

During the "Hellhound" incident in Lai Town No. L-776, her mother, Francis Oswood, was trapped in her self-created anomalous dimension and lost contact.]]
  },
  AwakerStory_11253_Title = {Text = "Story: V"},
  AwakerStory_11253_UnlockDesc = {
    Text = "Affinity Level 10"
  },
  AwakerStory_11253_UnlockDesc_1 = {
    Text = "Complete Chapter 4 \"In Silence\" on Normal difficulty"
  },
  AwakerStory_11254_Content = {
    Text = "The rumors of humans landing in the polar regions have intensified this century. In response, Mythag University and the Mystia Treaty Committee have collaborated to form a joint investigation team.\n\nIn December of A.F. 3@1, the joint investigation team ventured deep into the Elworth ice fields with the aim of recovering potential mystical artifacts before the arrival of secular expedition teams.\n\n......\n\nOn December 10, A.F. 3@1, Investigator Johansson accidentally fell into an ice cave, discovering a hollow space beneath the ice field. The altitude is too low; the melting ice will submerge the hollow within three days. We must complete our exploration before temperatures continue to rise.\n\nOn December 12, A.F. 3@1, there are reasons to believe that a cult has long used the hollow as a sacrificial pit. At the bottom of the cave, we discovered countless humanoid skeletons. Yes, humanoid—with cartilaginous fins connected to their skulls.\n\n......\n\nOn December 13, A.F. 3@1, damn, damn, damn, damn! At the peak of the bone mountain, the investigator discovered the recent remains of a human!!!\n\nThe cult may not have yet withdrawn from the polar region. Due to the Committee's foolish \"persistence,\" no Awakener investigators were permitted to accompany us. We must leave immediately!\n\n——\"Motion on Blockading the Wild Sea Route: Part One\""
  },
  AwakerStory_11254_Title = {Text = "Story: I"},
  AwakerStory_11254_UnlockDesc = {
    Text = "Awakener Level 3"
  },
  AwakerStory_11255_Content = {
    Text = "Wanda is smart, rich, and beautiful. As she says, she lives for pleasure. She turns men into her slaves and places her moonlit, cold feet on their backs. The crowned Venus, she is the embodiment of evil and dreams; in this dark shadow, her slender figure shines."
  },
  AwakerStory_11255_Title = {
    Text = "Basic Information"
  },
  AwakerStory_11255_UnlockDesc = {
    Text = "Awakener Level 1"
  },
  AwakerStory_11256_Content = {
    Text = "When trying to query records of Lily Oswood, Erica triggered 81 error alerts. As someone who was once forgotten by the world, Lily's birth records and medical history have turned into a handful of black sludge.\n\nBut we can still observe her silver shape through special instruments: delicate twists, resembling strands of intertwined hair—more accurately, like a child's lanugo.\n\nIt is particularly noteworthy that Lily always expresses a special attachment to linkers, and perhaps identifying herself as \"mother\" rather than calling herself a \"companion\" or \"master\" may help to bridge a quicker relationship with her"
  },
  AwakerStory_11256_Title = {Text = "Story: I"},
  AwakerStory_11256_UnlockDesc = {
    Text = "Awakener Level 3"
  },
  AwakerStory_11257_Content = {
    Text = [[
At the age of ten, Ramona became a regular at the university training grounds. Daring to accept training from the Black-clad Swordsman despite being human, she earned the admiration of many investigators.

After officially beginning her prerequisite courses, her eidetic memory, perfect test scores, and elegant yet deadly swordsmanship elevated her status at Mythag. Discipline and excellence became her defining traits.

However, many were puzzled as to why, despite her outstanding abilities, Ramona never received solo missions. Having been admitted early, she spent a full five years in prerequisite courses, watching cohort after cohort of investigators enter the world of mysticism.

What was she waiting for? What mission had been entrusted to her?

The answer came when the new Keeper enrolled.]]
  },
  AwakerStory_11257_Title = {Text = "Story: II"},
  AwakerStory_11257_UnlockDesc = {
    Text = "Affinity Level 5"
  },
  AwakerStory_11258_Content = {
    Text = "Uniforms must be steamed and ironed, quilts must be hand washed, the fireplace must be spotless in summer and always have a fire burning in winter. Wooden floors must gleam, bookshelves must be dust-free, and black tea must always be kept at the right temperature for easy enjoyment.\n\nFor her noble, special, and unique new master—the Keeper who has given her life anew—she can do anything. She is the best maid in the world and must certainly be able to complete every task perfectly, refining every detail.\n\nHer master's praise always makes her extraordinarily happy, but it's not enough, still not enough. What can she do to gain more attention from her master? What can she do to make herself more eye-catching?\n\n\"It must be the lack of earrings, necklaces, bracelets, rings, and hair ornaments!\"She thrust the broom into the ground and muttered to herself, \"As long as I have shiny jewelry decorations, Karen will surely become cuter, and everyone will enjoy looking at Karen even more!\""
  },
  AwakerStory_11258_Title = {Text = "Story: II"},
  AwakerStory_11258_UnlockDesc = {
    Text = "Affinity Level 5"
  },
  AwakerStory_11259_Content = {
    Text = "At the beginning of A.F. 3@2, during the renovation of the city named Cité, an anomaly was discovered in a fire-damaged garden: ashes climbed the burnt walls of the greenhouse like vines, and the ash roses blooming on the vines shimmered with a metallic hue.\n\nFollowing the trail of the vines, an investigator from Mythag University retrieved this Silver. The moment she touched the silver powder, her fingertips were scorched black without any pain, but tears inexplicably rolled down her cheeks.\n\nThe weeping came without reason and dissipated into the ashes in an instant."
  },
  AwakerStory_11259_Title = {Text = "Story: I"},
  AwakerStory_11259_UnlockDesc = {
    Text = "Awakener Level 3"
  },
  AwakerStory_11260_Content = {
    Text = [[
When the mountaineer reaches the peak of Elworth.

When the competitor lifts the world's number one trophy.

When the devout listens to the Revelation in dreams.

When victory comes too easily, the accompanying satisfaction may turn into bland inertia.

Looking around, there are no opponents, no fun at all.

On the surface, Ryker yearns for an exhilarating game, craving the heart-pounding moment after an ALL-IN, desiring the surge of adrenaline.

"There is no need to say those things. Only I understand you. What you truly desire is simply failure.

Let me grant you the sweetest failure."]]
  },
  AwakerStory_11260_Title = {Text = "Story: IV"},
  AwakerStory_11260_UnlockDesc = {
    Text = "Affinity Level 9"
  },
  AwakerStory_11261_Content = {
    Text = [[
Helot is a sharp, cold blade.

Awakeners who have worked with her say she's an effective weapon, strong and always mission-ready. Once given a kill order, no matter how powerful the enemy, she will break through and take the enemy's head.

But that's all.

She might protect her team, but it's just following orders, not out of care. She doesn't trust them; they can't trust her to guard their backs.

What they don't know is that to her, turning a blade on allies is despicable, contemptible, and deserving of punishment.

Having tasted the bitterness of betrayal herself, she would never turn her sword against her comrades.]]
  },
  AwakerStory_11261_Title = {Text = "Story: II"},
  AwakerStory_11261_UnlockDesc = {
    Text = "Affinity Level 5"
  },
  AwakerStory_11262_Content = {
    Text = [[
The aftereffects of incomplete awakening, coupled with the psychological impact of switching Links, have caused significant regression in Lily's character and mentality. Her silence on campus is evident to all.

Apart from staying close to the Keeper and Awakener Lotan, Lily is rarely seen alone around the campus. She doesn't attend classes nor join other Awakeners in their games. When not in battle, she quietly awaits orders in her dorm.

Lily's room window faces the Silver Key Tomb at the back of the campus. As the sun sets, she stands by the window, staring blankly at the tomb bathed in faint yellow light.

The Silver Key-shaped tombstones cast long shadows in the setting sun, and Lily stands in silence, just like the tombstones outside.]]
  },
  AwakerStory_11262_Title = {Text = "Story: II"},
  AwakerStory_11262_UnlockDesc = {
    Text = "Affinity Level 5"
  },
  AwakerStory_11263_Content = {
    Text = "This is a city of flowers and poetry, where a lingering love poem is equivalent to a freshly cut rose and can be exchanged for a week's food for a family of three. The emergence of a masterpiece also signifies that a talented poet will rise to fame.\n\nThat person used to be a gardener who spent her days with fertilizer and dead branches, relishing the flattery and admiration brought by elegant verses. She no longer tended to gardening matters, even locking the greenhouse and forbidding anyone from entering the flower room.\n\nWhen asked by others, she would only reply that there was \"Inspiration\" hidden in the greenhouse.\n\nThey were born insignificant, the children of noble retainers. With the establishment of the Constante Federation, the old nobles were purged, and they lost their place to stay.\n\nThat was a maid who grew up accompanying the young lady but showed her talent for writing early on — but how could a servant read poetry?\n\nSurrounded by an ever-changing environment, the talent for poetry could not provide the girl with survival capabilities. Everything made the girl even more out of place and more melancholic and sad.\n\nUntil the gardener extended her hand — that hand, cut by thorns, bestowed upon her a garden. In this tiny kingdom, they spent the happiest time of their lives.\n\nThe peaceful life began to change with a poem received from the gardener.\n\nHer friend's talent was so moving that she wanted more people to see this poem dedicated to a friend.\n\nThe shy and melancholic friend was unwilling to sign, so the gardener signed her name in the signature place — \"If published, it would also be convenient for them to send reward money.\"\n\nThe gardener's change also started from the first draft fee.\n\nShe could not understand why she suddenly went from protector to burden.\n\nShe could not understand why her friend could effortlessly gain all the love and praise, while her own hard work was defenseless before talent.\n\nBlinded by desire and jealousy, she began to use her friend's trust to deceive her creations. The deceitful behavior could not be turned back. The seed was buried in the gardener's heart from the beginning, and as the reputation of the talented poet spread, it began to sprout, blooming into a bud during a street interview — the fervent fans asked the gardener questions about those secret and lingering emotions in the poems, which the gardener could not read and was soaked in sweat, hurriedly leaving the scene. Returning to the flower room late at night, faced with her friend's concerned gaze, the panicking flowers bloomed at that moment.\n\nAfter a fire shocking Cité, the talented poet announced her retreat, disappearing with the wealth and fame she earned in a short time."
  },
  AwakerStory_11263_Title = {Text = "Story: III"},
  AwakerStory_11263_UnlockDesc = {
    Text = "Affinity Level 7"
  },
  AwakerStory_11264_Content = {
    Text = [[
The past three years have seen a large number of shipwreck incidents in the Monge Triangle sea area, accompanied by several cases of totally missing.

According to a sailor's testimony, a "woman with a glowing head" has been witnessed on the deck of the victim vessel during the rescue operation.

The field investigators rushed to the Monge Triangle sea area, but his ship had lost contact after arrivial. When the reinforcements finally found the spearhead ship, it had already lost power, drifting by the current towards the center of the Monge Triangle. All crew members were severely dehydrated and feeble. Massive hallucinations with acute intensity have been reported.

During the medical examination of the crew, a Silvercore was found among Investigator Ivors' personal belongings. The investigator himself consistently denied any contact between the ship and any Awakener.

The Silvercore was later sealed by the Awakener Department, numbered 6291-S-S-01, scheduled to use as teaching materials for pre-investigators in A.F. 315.]]
  },
  AwakerStory_11264_Title = {Text = "Story: I"},
  AwakerStory_11264_UnlockDesc = {
    Text = "Affinity Level 3"
  },
  AwakerStory_11265_Content = {
    Text = "After being Awakened, we finally learned what kind of life Murphy led in the Order.\n\nShe spends a lot of time on her appearance before going out, always carrying a parasol. Afternoon tea is at 4 PM, accompanied by milk tea and strawberry jam scones. Maintaining cleanliness and elegance, living like a lady—this is her destiny, and she insists on living as such no matter where she is.\n\n(Note from the Archivist: I think her grabbing beef pudding with her hands is far from ladylike...)\n\nEven without servants to command, she lives exactly as she wishes, which is somewhat comforting.\n\nDue to a certain Event, she rarely interacts with Awakeners Miriam and Goliath, often ignoring them. She displays a complex expression when meeting Awakener Tulu.\n\nTalking about the past makes her irritable. Perhaps she just needs more time to heal."
  },
  AwakerStory_11265_Title = {Text = "Story: II"},
  AwakerStory_11265_UnlockDesc = {
    Text = "Affinity Level 5"
  },
  AwakerStory_11266_Content = {
    Text = [[
You need not fear his black eye patch; the smothering darkness will not obscure his boundless compassion. The sightless body may have perished, yet the will for redemption endures. Before him, everything should be loved, and everything will be loved in turn.

The words of the Our Father are forever engraved onto the Tablet, and through these blessed flesh and bones, He will bestow upon you "The Blessing".]]
  },
  AwakerStory_11266_Title = {
    Text = "Basic Information"
  },
  AwakerStory_11266_UnlockDesc = {
    Text = "Awakener Level 1"
  },
  AwakerStory_11267_Content = {
    Text = "He always wandered by the lakeside with a gloomy expression. Gradually, the students began to refer to the lakeside as \"the Territory of the Sullen Half-Fish Man\". Thus, he came every day like a lord, solemnly inspecting his domain. When he dove into the lake bottom, the swirling bubbles gently enveloped him; underwater, the jeers from the shore seemed to fade into obscurity."
  },
  AwakerStory_11267_Title = {
    Text = "Basic Information"
  },
  AwakerStory_11267_UnlockDesc = {
    Text = "Awakener Level 1"
  },
  AwakerStory_11268_Content = {
    Text = [[
The radiance of devotion illuminates her pilgrimage. A glorious ascension for the most devout follower of her true lord. A golden promise for the most loyal subject of her king.

It collapses. The Divine Realm is a sinking lie, a fortress without foundation, a vine drifting away from its soil. Her dolor billows. Her desolation turmoils. The remaining faith in the Divine Realm cannot keeps Faros afloat anymore. The poor wanderer eventually drowned.

Diving deep into the sea, her love and hatred agitates into swelling waves. The water whirls and spumes and eddies, splendor as the ceremony fireworks in her memory, a festival almost like a solace.

Her final torched gaze before being beheaded by the hero, must have been cling to the Divine Realm she couldn't forgo.]]
  },
  AwakerStory_11268_Title = {Text = "Story: III"},
  AwakerStory_11268_UnlockDesc = {
    Text = "Affinity Level 7"
  },
  AwakerStory_11269_Content = {
    Text = [[
She seems to be constantly circling around the motorcycle named "Phantasm": tightening a screw here, adjusting a pipe there... It's an endless project, and although many believe she has done the best repairs, she still immerses herself in it day after day. 

The reason lies in that vague feeling of "something is still missing".]]
  },
  AwakerStory_11269_Title = {
    Text = "Basic Information"
  },
  AwakerStory_11269_UnlockDesc = {
    Text = "Awakener Level 1"
  },
  AwakerStory_11270_Content = {
    Text = "\"4:30 6-mile morning jog along the Aethis River. Argued with an elderly passerby and kicked a poodle into the air.\n\n...\n\n12:00 Lunch: Honey pancakes, olive appetizers, and... five servings of roast lamb? Unbelievable.\n\n13:00 Headed to the Trout Fighting Club. Record: 10 wins, 0 losses. Fastest match: 3 seconds—the opponent forfeited out of sheer fear.\n\n19:00 Watched <Italic:The Shepherd-King> at Corvint Theatre with the Keeper, got thrown out for shouting dangerous political opinions.\n\n22:00 Found loitering near St. Marian Hospital. Highly probable motive: casing the facility for blood bags theft.\n\nObservation ends; danger level: SSS.\"\n\n—Excerpt from <Italic:Hannah's Awakener Observation Notes>"
  },
  AwakerStory_11270_Title = {Text = "Story: II"},
  AwakerStory_11270_UnlockDesc = {
    Text = "Affinity Level 5"
  },
  AwakerStory_11271_Content = {
    Text = "Faint saw the student secretly weeping in the laboratory.\n\nShe wasn't Faint's favorite student, but she was undoubtedly the one who liked her the most.\n\nThe girl never minded Faint's resistance and aloofness, nor was she afraid of Faint's uncontrollable abilities.\n\nShe would spend her entire allowance on sweets, just because she was worried that Faint didn't have enough energy; she would wear the clunky protective suit just to comb Faint's tangled hair.\n\n... <Italic:I must repay her>, Faint thought.\n\nSo, Faint did what she could.\n\n—<Italic:If she was just worried about failing exams, then I'll just threaten the others into failing instead, right?>"
  },
  AwakerStory_11271_Title = {Text = "Story: II"},
  AwakerStory_11271_UnlockDesc = {
    Text = "Affinity Level 5"
  },
  AwakerStory_11272_Content = {
    Text = "Mythag awakens and contains many Awakeners, but none are as unique as Thais.\n\nShe helps schoolgirls pick out makeup for dates; she helps the disheartened regain hope, and she helps investigators on the verge of mental collapse find their way back to the light.\n\nShe's like a lover, a sister, or above all, a mother. She has a gift for creating a quagmire called \"love\", quietly drawing people in and making them unconsciously willing to give everything for her—\nFollowing the third intervention to prevent a student from drinking the mysterious liquid she provided, the Awakener Management Office issued a restriction order against her.\n\n\"Thais is strictly prohibited from approaching any student unless accompanied by the Keeper.\""
  },
  AwakerStory_11272_Title = {Text = "Story: II"},
  AwakerStory_11272_UnlockDesc = {
    Text = "Affinity Level 5"
  },
  AwakerStory_11273_Content = {
    Text = [[
All meaning dissipates like sand, the world's false curtain fades in her eyes, and everything returns to the most primordial darkness.  

In this final performance on the pitch-black stage, the dancer of science still dances with all her might.  

She no longer cares about being slowly devoured by dissolution, as the ending of the play was written from the very beginning.  

As in the past, she will unreservedly dedicate the power of genius to the world in a manner closest to the truth.  

If you ask her gently, she will insist that she still holds love for humanity and the world; she wants to end all suffering in the world and bring people back to their true, original home.]]
  },
  AwakerStory_11273_Title = {Text = "Story: IV"},
  AwakerStory_11273_UnlockDesc = {
    Text = "Affinity Level 9"
  },
  AwakerStory_11274_Content = {
    Text = "A.F. 3@1, January.\n\nOn the Devil's Reef off the eastern coast of the Agló Republic, local fishermen reported they had salvaged \"a strangely shaped corpse\"—short and hunched, with protruding eyeballs, partially hardened skin, webbed fingers, and the most bizarre feature being symmetrical red marks on either side of the neck. If it weren't for the student uniform it wore, it would be hard to consider it a \"human corpse.\" \n\nWhen the investigators arrived, the strange corpse had already been burned by frightened fishermen as an omen, leaving only a suitcase that was quite popular among students at the time. The suitcase contained no change of clothes, only some illegible manuscripts, a compass, and a photograph of a middle-aged woman."
  },
  AwakerStory_11274_Title = {Text = "Story: I"},
  AwakerStory_11274_UnlockDesc = {
    Text = "Awakener Level 3"
  },
  AwakerStory_11275_Content = {
    Text = [[
The girl wears a plain dress, her skin still stinging from the rough scrubbing earlier. She doesn't understand why soldiers brought her here; a noble master's house is no place for slaves to come and go freely, and she is far too young to serve here.

The lady in the snowy white gown sits poised in the chair. The girl lowers her head, trembling with fear and nerves.

"I knew I wasn't wrong..." the lady says, "So much like her... truly."

Like? Does that mean she looks like someone else?

"Perfect. Simply perfect." The lady claps her hands happily, "It shall be you. From today on, I am your mother. Do you understand?"

Mother? But she already has a mother. Her mother was at home, crying out loud when she was taken away.

If so... what about her mother?

Confusion swirls in the girl's mind. She wants to ask, yet she understands all too well: a mistress's word was a slave's command, and disobedience meant severe punishment.

"I understand, Madam."

"What a good child. Let me think... I'll call you Helot. Do you like that name, Helot? I'm sure you do. Come, put on this dress and show it to mommy."]]
  },
  AwakerStory_11275_Title = {Text = "Story: III"},
  AwakerStory_11275_UnlockDesc = {
    Text = "Affinity Level 7"
  },
  AwakerStory_11276_Content = {
    Text = [[
Goliath is tyrannical and ruthless, but his power is undeniable. According to Miss Erica's battle records, his brutal brawn can no doubt guarantee his advantage even in isolated and vicious situations. I believe that Goliath does not care about the level of his partner's ability just because no one can hold a candle to him in his world.

However, everytime Goliath faces Miryam, fear always seeps from his eyes uncontrollably. It's hard to imagine what kind of existence would evoke such awe from this despotic ruler and brutal former-king.

Additionally, he has shown unusual concern for Miss Murphy. Sometimes he was witnessed to wander around the university's surrounding maze, maybe waiting for Murphy to return from her mission. Sometimes he would distantly observe Murphy's condition, seemingly worrying about possible injuries during her tasks.

Miss Peaslee also notices this. Once she said to me half-jokingly, "Hey, don't you think he's trying to be an ordinary father?"

"Observation record from an intern researcher"]]
  },
  AwakerStory_11276_Title = {Text = "Story: II"},
  AwakerStory_11276_UnlockDesc = {
    Text = "Affinity Level 5"
  },
  AwakerStory_11277_Content = {
    Text = "Winkle's office is known as the North Star of Mythag University. It remains perpetually illuminated, with every corner where a shadow might lurk driven away by an array of lights—from lanterns and kerosene lamps to tungsten bulbs and candles.\n\nHer fear of darkness even causes her to avoid sleep. Thus, day and night, she can always be found huddled beneath the largest lamp, scrawling indecipherable symbols upon the draft papers scattered all over the floor."
  },
  AwakerStory_11277_Title = {
    Text = "Basic Information"
  },
  AwakerStory_11277_UnlockDesc = {
    Text = "Awakener Level 1"
  },
  AwakerStory_11278_Content = {
    Text = [[
Caecus despised humans, even as a child. 

Once, he saved a drowning little girl but was accused by other children of being a monster; he tried to keep his distance, yet they chased him, shouting "stinky frogman." 

During those gloomy years, the only glimmer of hope for him came from Uncle Oren's letters. His vast knowledge contained endless tales of monsters that captivated young Caecus. However, the happiness was fleeting, as Uncle Oren inexplicably vanished a few years later.

At the age of 16, Caecus returned to visit his grandfather and accidentally discovered Oren's manuscript. He finally understood the noble meaning hidden within the twisted patterns on his body.

Hmph, humanity is ultimately a lowly species.

From then on, he no longer succumbed to pessimism but patiently waited for the day destiny would arrive.]]
  },
  AwakerStory_11278_Title = {Text = "Story: III"},
  AwakerStory_11278_UnlockDesc = {
    Text = "Affinity Level 7"
  },
  AwakerStory_11279_Content = {
    Text = [[
Few people in school remember that the boy was once called the "Death Knight". 

Only at midnight does the scenery of that day transform into a nightmare, infiltrating the boy's dreams.

The dissoluted bodies invading the campus, the collapsed bell tower, the barely surviving "Keeper". 

"Don't cry, Ogier, it's not your fault..." 

The iron cavalry invading the home, the tilted palace, the black blood flowing from the princess's fingers.

"Don't sacrifice yourself for me, Ogier, you've done enough already..." 

The grains of memory entwined with pain wash over the boy's spirit.]]
  },
  AwakerStory_11279_Title = {Text = "Story: III"},
  AwakerStory_11279_UnlockDesc = {
    Text = "Affinity Level 7"
  },
  AwakerStory_11280_Content = {
    Text = "Some Awakeners struggle to adapt to their new vessels and lives, while others embrace the change, pivoting eagerly into their second life.\n\nTulu belongs to neither category. Never has any Awakener displayed such blatant, naked indifference toward the modern world.\n\nHis aptitude is peerless; perhaps he has already peered through the veil of current crises and global shifts. Yet, he prefers to lose himself in the depths of sleep.\n\nDespite having no desire for fame, he has become a figure of renown among both humans and Awakeners at the university. Researchers scrutinize his every move, churning out paper after paper on his behavior. The Departments of Archaeology and Astronomy frequently send invitations to academic symposia, almost always requesting him by name.\n\nTulu's influence among his fellow Awakeners is equally profound: Murphy grows sullen at the mere sight of him; Goliath seems perpetually locked in a silent, private rivalry with him; and Miriam treats his every word as divine law.\n\nTo all of this, he maintains a singular lack of affect—harboring no expectations, making no demands. He grants the occasional request only as the whim strikes him; otherwise, he remains unreachable."
  },
  AwakerStory_11280_Title = {Text = "Story: II"},
  AwakerStory_11280_UnlockDesc = {
    Text = "Affinity Level 5"
  },
  AwakerStory_11281_Content = {
    Text = [[
Even now, as an Awakener, Sorel cannot forget those nobles who fawned over her, nor the endless parade of their sycophantic faces.

How utterly nauseating those smiling faces were: slick, mercenary, dripping with undisguised lust and calculation. Yet she had no choice but to weave a gentle web around such faces.

She would weave the most meticulous of webs, reaching into every dark corner, winning over every person, securing every ounce of leverage. She had to be like water slowly brought to a boil, letting those people grow comfortable in it, so that by the time they wished to remove their masks, they would find there was no escape.

But when she finally came to her senses, the one with no escape turned out to be herself.

No escape. No rest. No quitting.

Sorel had long since lost the right to turn back. Aside from standing above everyone, there was no other path for her to walk.]]
  },
  AwakerStory_11281_Title = {Text = "Story: IV"},
  AwakerStory_11281_UnlockDesc = {
    Text = "Affinity Level 9"
  },
  AwakerStory_11282_Content = {
    Text = [[
"I want to wear purple crystals as black as wine." 

"I want to don a luxurious gown made of ostrich feathers." 

"I want to be the only light at the banquet." 

The maid blinked her amber eyes. She had many more beautiful wishes, but she could no longer voice them. Before her frozen body loomed an endless green flame, silently blooming in the dark night.]]
  },
  AwakerStory_11282_Title = {
    Text = "Basic Information"
  },
  AwakerStory_11282_UnlockDesc = {
    Text = "Awakener Level 1"
  },
  AwakerStory_11283_Content = {
    Text = [[
She calculated the speed of her sword, the angle to avoid attacks.

She calculated the feasibility of escape plans and the probability of the world moving toward the future.

Until the very end, she never stopped calculating.

Just as she never stopped walking this desolate path.]]
  },
  AwakerStory_11283_Title = {
    Text = "Basic Information"
  },
  AwakerStory_11283_UnlockDesc = {
    Text = "Awakener Level 1"
  },
  AwakerStory_11284_Content = {
    Text = "The artist from Cité cares not for other people. She only pursues the absolute form of pure beauty, etching ephemeral moments into eternity.\n\nAs her inspiration surges forth, her chisel never ceases; as her works witness completion, her body is submerged in coral-colored shades. In the corner of her workshop which she pays no heed, her agony and delight intertwine, sprouting from her very existence."
  },
  AwakerStory_11284_Title = {
    Text = "Basic Information"
  },
  AwakerStory_11284_UnlockDesc = {
    Text = "Awakener Level 1"
  },
  AwakerStory_11285_Content = {
    Text = "@3Built in the Second Samnite period, decorated in the exquisite Third Pompeian and Lemovician styles, this is a typical residence of the wealthy merchant class during the Roman era. Featuring two courtyards and four triclinia, @1@1\n.....all reduced to ashes in the famous slave uprising... According to contemporaneous anecdotes, a massive pale spider was sealed beneath the ruins, referred to by locals as the \"God of the Maze,\" and they firmly believe that those who tread upon the spider's territory will become disoriented among countless passages and entrances, ultimately becoming hosts for its offspring.\n\nAn interesting horror story, but it will not deter us @2@1\n—Excerpt from \"@2Archaeological Notes on the Ruins\"\n\n.....The situation is dire, Sir Goodman. Moretti and his party have been missing for several days now. We all understand this has nothing to do with the legend of the \"God of the Maze,\" yet it is indeed unsettling. We have decided to end the investigation early and return to Durham.\n\nAdditionally, the archaeological team discovered a cluster of Silver-like objects in the ruins, which may be related to the @1 you mentioned earlier...\n\n—Excerpt from Clarkson Johnson's \"A Letter to Goodman\""
  },
  AwakerStory_11285_Title = {Text = "Story: I"},
  AwakerStory_11285_UnlockDesc = {
    Text = "Awakener Level 3"
  },
  AwakerStory_11286_Content = {
    Text = [[
A.F.2@2, November, a major earthquake struck the Beren region.

The next day, two professors were ordered to head to the disaster area to search for the missing Mythag investigation team.

The team was last active along the Mare Internum coast, primarily tasked with exploring, excavating historical relics, and searching for possible leads related to the "D-phenomenon." 

On November 8, at the location where team members were reportedly last seen, Professor @2 discovered an unrecorded palace ruin and recovered a Mythag-standard silver key, numbered I-@2, but did not find any team members.

On November 9, two Silvers were unearthed at the site, which were later taken back to Londinium and sealed due to their historical value, to be Awakened on another day.]]
  },
  AwakerStory_11286_Title = {Text = "Story: I"},
  AwakerStory_11286_UnlockDesc = {
    Text = "Affinity Level 3"
  },
  AwakerStory_11287_Content = {
    Text = [[
On her first day at Mythag, Wanda was severely accused of "arbitrarily trampling on others".

According to a student who wished to remain anonymous, he just happened to pass by the library and accidentally made eye contact with Wanda, and was then thrown to the ground. @2 was put on @3 (the student refused to disclose more details).

The process of Damage took no more than five minutes, and the situation was severe and appalling.

The Mythag Disciplinary Committee (hereinafter referred to as MDC) expressed high concern and deep sympathy regarding this matter. A specialized task force has been established to conduct thorough ideological and behavioral reform for Wanda, in order to help her quickly integrate into campus life.]]
  },
  AwakerStory_11287_Title = {Text = "Story: II"},
  AwakerStory_11287_UnlockDesc = {
    Text = "Affinity Level 5"
  },
  AwakerStory_11288_Content = {
    Text = "\"At the day of @1 @1, the university cemetery was vandalized again. This marks the third grave-robbing incident this month.\n\nAfter weeks of investigation, the Awakener Sanga has been preliminarily identified as the suspect by the association.\n\nNo doubt anyone visiting her workshop would be shocked by those various grotesque and blasphemous ocean-themed sculptures before questioning their material sources: the shell necklace Natasha wore for her burial; Aberdeen granite that shared similarities with tombstones. Unlike Pickman, who loves explaining his artistic concepts, Sanga is more elusive—our all queries resulting in nothing more than a smile.\n\nDon't touch her chisel, and don't stay alone with her in her workshop—Professor Dexter warned us. However, radical measures are necessary to uncover the truth behind the grave robberies.\n\nIt's 00:45 on @1 @1. Member @2 of the Detective Enthusiast Association has sneaked into Sanga's workshop. Wish me good @3\"\n\n—Excerpt from \"Detective Enthusiast Association, Investigation Record S-618\""
  },
  AwakerStory_11288_Title = {Text = "Story: II"},
  AwakerStory_11288_UnlockDesc = {
    Text = "Affinity Level 5"
  },
  AwakerStory_11289_Content = {
    Text = [[
Lotan has so many labels attached to her that no one knows how to approach this black-clad swordswoman.

Too humble and she will shatter your knees for being too boring; too arrogant and she will slash your insolence with her greatsword; too tough and she will soften your soul through battle.

But perhaps this is the arrogance befitting one born with the planet itself. As a former guardian, she has every right to her arrogance.]]
  },
  AwakerStory_11289_Title = {
    Text = "Basic Information"
  },
  AwakerStory_11289_UnlockDesc = {
    Text = "Awakener Level 1"
  },
  AwakerStory_11290_Content = {
    Text = "Whenever night falls, Nautila will burrow into the storeroom with her mother, pick up various tools, and piece together a unicycle called Phantasm.  \n\n\"Why not just buy one directly?\" the young girl looked up and asked her mother, who was holding the tools, \"Then we could go out and adventure right away.\"  \n\nHer mother held her hand, teaching her how to weld metal quickly and well while saying:  \n\"Machines, like people, each have different temperaments and personalities. Only those who truly understand us can spend longer time with us.\"  \n\n\"Like friends?\"  \n\n\"Except that machines are made by us—that's right, like friends.\"  \n\nThe huge wheels must be sturdy, and the engine must be durable, because once they set off, they won't easily turn back. They want to travel the world together and complete a grand adventure.  \n\nIllness took her mother away, leaving behind a workshop full of tools but void of life. Nautila held the unfinished Phantasm, determined to complete her and her mother's dream with this cold friend.  \n\nUntil the last journey."
  },
  AwakerStory_11290_Title = {Text = "Story: III"},
  AwakerStory_11290_UnlockDesc = {
    Text = "Affinity Level 7"
  },
  AwakerStory_11291_Content = {
    Text = "Year 3@2 Summer, legends of sea monsters spread across the Irian Isles.\n\nFishermen claimed to have spotted a five-story-tall cephalopod near the shore. Its skin was deep crimson, with black concentric rings on its tentacles.\n\nI heard this rumor while verifying suspected D-phenomenon in Mianland with Senior Johansen. The next day, the senior set sail for the Irian Isles, and I wrote this report in the Amirante Ocean.\n\nOn the third day of sailing, vast fish carcasses appeared: mackerel, flounder, dolphins, and even a pregnant sperm whale—I swear! Old sailors blamed oxygen depletion caused by overbreeding, but I felt like we were missing something...\n\nOn the eighth day of sailing, my seasickness worsened, and severe nausea made it nearly impossible to eat. Despite nearing the Irian Isles, Johansen insisted on returning@3... I didn't understand, but I trusted the senior.\n\n—Bale Columbus \"Year 3@2 Summer Internship Report\""
  },
  AwakerStory_11291_Title = {Text = "Story: I"},
  AwakerStory_11291_UnlockDesc = {
    Text = "Awakener Level 3"
  },
  AwakerStory_11292_Content = {
    Text = [[
Murphy: Fauxborn has died once before.

It was not a willing step through the threshold called "Divine Descent"; she witnessed the "God" being born from her own chest. How ridiculous: it was a hideous, unconscious, and unknowing mass, yet she was forced to give up her vibrant, splendid life for it.

More ironically, the twisted fate remained relentless. At the moment the God was born into the world, she accepted the unwilling sacrifice through intense pain. After a long period resembling sleep, Murphy opened her eyes in astonishment, only to find the scene before her identical to her final moments.

"Murphy" died. "Murphy: Fauxborn" was Awakened.

Her Linker is a squirming blood clot, deaf and mute, that she herself gave birth to.

The God gives birth to the Princess, the Princess re-conceives the God, and the God reawakens her remains. A pathological fate clings tightly to her, an endless, unbreakable cycle. Her devout mother is ecstatic, the Seafarers prostrate themselves in prayer, and her dignity is restored, more glorious than ever before.

But the original "Murphy" is truly gone forever. The girl who once, with a burst of foolish innocence, attempted to rebel against an unfair destiny, now embraces the crown of vanity she once despised and boards a cruise ship that can never reach the other shore.]]
  },
  AwakerStory_11292_Title = {Text = "Story: III"},
  AwakerStory_11292_UnlockDesc = {
    Text = "Affinity Level 7"
  },
  AwakerStory_11293_Content = {
    Text = [[
I love the sea. Febvre's sea. The Prussian blue sea. The sea with warm, moist breezes. The sea that looks like a painting from the sanatorium's window. The sea with returning sails. The sea nurturing countless lives like a mother.

Now, I've finally returned to the tranquil sea, back to before birth, back to being enveloped in my mother's amniotic fluid. The currents gather the unfortunate Fragments, piecing me together among bones and coral. The deep-sea fish swim past, listening to the laments of fate's suffering.

Mother, if I could be born again, would I be happier?]]
  },
  AwakerStory_11293_Title = {Text = "Story: IV"},
  AwakerStory_11293_UnlockDesc = {
    Text = "Affinity Level 9"
  },
  AwakerStory_11294_Content = {
    Text = "The Evrotas archaeological team has been plagued by a mysterious illness for ten days, and the situation remains dire.\n\nThe illness strikes without warning and with ferocious intensity. Patients typically experience severe hallucinations, accompanied by a loss of bodily sensation and sensory deficits that worsen over time, eventually leading to partial or total paralysis. While the contagion appears confined to the archaeological site on the west bank of the Evrotas River—affecting mostly workers and resident scholars—authorities cannot rule out the possibility of further spread.\n\nA former worker revealed to reporters that symptoms had already surfaced fifteen days ago—on the very day the \"Evrotas Shackles\" were unearthed. Readers following the news may recall these well-preserved, rust-free shackles that clearly originate from an ancient civilization. They arrived in the Kingdom of Leonia yesterday and have been handed over to Mythag University for further research. The link between the illness and the shackles, however, takes on a distinctly supernatural tone.\n\n\"Everything went wrong at the camp the moment we dug them up,\" the worker noted. \"Many had nightmares of a girl bound in a cage by chains... This is a curse—the curse of the shackles! There is no other explanation.\"\n\nAs of today, relevant authorities have cordoned off the area. The Evrotas excavation has been completely suspended.\n\n—<Italic:The Ancient Curse? Mysterious Illness Sweeps the Evrotas Archaeological Team.>"
  },
  AwakerStory_11294_Title = {Text = "Story: I"},
  AwakerStory_11294_UnlockDesc = {
    Text = "Affinity Level 3"
  },
  AwakerStory_11295_Content = {
    Text = "The Silver from Ryker's awakening was excavated from the interior of the renowned Remouahe monument, the Triangular Giant Tower. It is streamlined and perfectly bullet-shaped, matching the size and form of bullets used in the SAA revolver, embedded within the skull of a young male corpse.\n\nTouching this Silver evokes magnificent and grand visions of the Triangular Giant Tower, causing the body to instinctively curl up and crawl. If the toucher resists desperately and looks ahead, they will see the blurred figure of a crowned man backlit, followed by an instant interruption of consciousness, causing the Silver to naturally slip from their fingers.\n\n\"The tip of the Triangular Tower has not yet been eroded; it should be a scene soon after its completion.\"—Researcher B.R. Longman\n\"I can hear horrifying whispers from dark souls.\"—Researcher K. Waters\n\"I must denounce the inhumane experiments arranged for us by Mythag. The side effects of repeatedly touching this Silver are enough to cause complete loss of bodily control. In short, I refuse to touch it again.\"—Researcher L. Lopez"
  },
  AwakerStory_11295_Title = {Text = "Story: I"},
  AwakerStory_11295_UnlockDesc = {
    Text = "Awakener Level 3"
  },
  AwakerStory_11296_Content = {
    Text = "A.F.18@1/@1/@2 Infantry Regiment, the Kingdom of Remouahe, Port Alexandria\nThe situation in Port Alexandria is stabilizing. The 3rd and 4th battalions, along with three companies of musketeers, have crossed the canal to proceed to @4 for the next stage of operations. Now only the 1st battalion and a company of musketeers remain in Port Alexandria.\n\nA squad encountered rebels during a patrol and quickly dealt with them. They brought back an interesting trinket that looks like silver but is heavier. I've stored it in the safe; the commander will like this gift.\n\n.....\n\nDay 13 of the garrison, soldiers from various companies are showing abnormal behavior, including but not limited to attacking comrades, officers, destroying inventory, and military equipment. These soldiers, along with the earlier madmen, are now under my direct supervision in confinement.\n\nTheir eyes are bloodshot, and they drool, looking more like pitiful animals than soldiers. Madness is spreading here; I'm worried it will become a plague.\n\n.....\n\nDay 30 of the garrison.\n\nTo date, 370 soldiers have shown mad behavior. After 20 days of severe hysteria, 331 of them developed limb numbness and paralysis. Their aggression remains strong; two military doctors were bitten while trying to treat them.\n\nThe madness continues to spread. I've reported the situation, hoping for swift action.\n\n.....\n\nThe Committee took over the Alexandria garrison for 10 days; people still fall into madness, my brothers one after another. Why are only we suffering this damned plague? Why are the locals fine? Why do the rebels who hassle us remain unaffected?\n\nMy head hurts more and more, and the doctors are helpless—they fell into madness before me and became those biting monsters.\n\nI fear I will also go mad.\n\nThey say we have to wait for the Mythag University people. Damn them, we fought for our country, we shouldn't be treated this way.\n\n.....\n\nI know now, I finally know. It's a vengeful spirit within that piece of silver, seeking revenge on all who invaded this land. That one-legged woman wants us to leave, wants us all gone, to return everything here to its original owners. Yes, yes, it should be this way, we never should've come, never started this war, I @1@3@4@2@1@2@3\n— Excerpt from the \"@2 Infantry Regiment 1st Battalion Acting Commander's Log\""
  },
  AwakerStory_11296_Title = {Text = "Story: I"},
  AwakerStory_11296_UnlockDesc = {
    Text = "Awakener Level 3"
  },
  AwakerStory_11297_Content = {
    Text = "She was not born thirsting for blood. Once, she basked in warmth as fervent and fleeting as a night-blooming epiphyllum. Betrayal and imprisonment fanned the flames of her defiance; the fire of vengeance soon scorched Maysia. Steeped in endless resentment, she has since shuttered her heart to all..."
  },
  AwakerStory_11297_Title = {
    Text = "Basic Information"
  },
  AwakerStory_11297_UnlockDesc = {
    Text = "Awakener Level 1"
  },
  AwakerStory_11298_Content = {
    Text = "Due to the fact that the Genesis Awakener, formerly known as the \"Brain in a jar,\" has a history of breaking free from the S355 restrainer, it has been relocated by Dean Czort and placed in a new special dissolution restrainer.\n\nThis restrainer is located deep within the Black Pool. To ensure that there are no other instruments or items within a 30-meter radius of the restrainer, the Black Pool monitoring team has arranged for at least one patrol every 60 minutes.\n\nDuring monitoring, it has been noted that this Awakener remains conscious and almost never engages in sleep activities. The Awakener once attempted to narrate to the patrol members about its previous illegal Silver chip modification experiments, and a team member fell into madness after brief communication.\n\nCurrently, all patrol teams consist of three members, who are strictly prohibited from making contact or conversing with the Awakener and must wear soundproof earmuffs throughout the patrol.\n\n......\n\nThe confidentiality restriction level of this Awakener has reached the highest level of Awakener management. No one informed of the details is allowed to disclose information about this Awakener inside or outside of Mythag, and without the dean's approval and personal escort, visits are prohibited.\n\n— Excerpted from \"Mythag Black Pool Monitoring Team Report Records\""
  },
  AwakerStory_11298_Title = {Text = "Story: II"},
  AwakerStory_11298_UnlockDesc = {
    Text = "Affinity Level 5"
  },
  AwakerStory_11299_Content = {
    Text = [[
It truly exists.

It is the gaze cast by God, the branch God extends towards the universe.

It delights in the grandeur of history and hungers for the flourishing of civilization.

It seeks to transcend withering, to surpass death itself.

She longs for low, resonant chants, for dust and salt-laden winds, for silver leaves and the moonlight over Morsul.

Fiend, witch, sorceress... the judgments of mortals are mere trifles.

If even a single drop of blood escapes the black encroachment, They shall once more draw eternity into Their arms.]]
  },
  AwakerStory_11299_Title = {Text = "Story: IV"},
  AwakerStory_11299_UnlockDesc = {
    Text = "Affinity Level 9"
  },
  AwakerStory_11300_Content = {
    Text = [[
Rose's spike pierces the poetry page, leaving transparent bloodstains. The scent of alcohol fills the air, and colorless flames spread everywhere.

In that blaze, Horla holds the last poem, silently marking the end of the concealed genius poet's path.]]
  },
  AwakerStory_11300_Title = {
    Text = "Basic Information"
  },
  AwakerStory_11300_UnlockDesc = {
    Text = "Awakener Level 1"
  },
  AwakerStory_11301_Content = {
    Text = "Her teenage years were spent in a military camp. \n\nLike all children raised in military camps, she firmly believes in the glory of the legion and regards it as her life. Her world is simple: what the commander acknowledges is right, and what the commander forbids is wrong. \n\n\"Swing your sword towards the enemy; we will grant true freedom to this land; strike down the invading army; do not feel sympathy for them; current sacrifices are all for future stability and prosperity.\"\n\nShe trained under such slogans and entered the battlefield with them. After a desperate rescue mission, she received an injured leg and the title of a war hero. From then on, she retired with medals and became a new recruit instructor, completely unaware of how this injured leg would reveal a new world to her. \n\nHumbled by her injury, Alva angrily left the army. Once on the streets, she truly discovered how the commander's glorious speeches were nothing but lies—liberation was merely a pretext for invasion, and people in foreign lands suffered greatly. \n\nThis was not her ideal nation; this was not a radiant future without blood and tears. \n\nThus, she raised the blade of atonement against her former comrades and vowed to fight for true justice."
  },
  AwakerStory_11301_Title = {Text = "Story: III"},
  AwakerStory_11301_UnlockDesc = {
    Text = "Affinity Level 7"
  },
  AwakerStory_11302_Content = {
    Text = "\"Welcome to Lady Daffodil's Exchange Shop. We barter goods and collect heads. Our rates are perfectly fair—fair to all, no deception.\"\n\nAmidst the swirling gray mist, the woman gently tapped the ash from her antique wooden pipe. Beneath the swaying brim of her hat, a flickering smile hovered at the corners of her lips, laced with ambiguity."
  },
  AwakerStory_11302_Title = {
    Text = "Basic Information"
  },
  AwakerStory_11302_UnlockDesc = {
    Text = "Awakener Level 1"
  },
  AwakerStory_11303_Content = {
    Text = "Everyone quickly accepted one fact: where there's Jenkin, there's Brown, and where there's Brown, there's Jenkin. And whenever Brown acted alone—make no mistake—Jenkin was behind it.\n\n\"What do you mean by 'stolen'? I have an alibi!\"\n\nSo said the girl, holding the item Brown had \"borrowed.\""
  },
  AwakerStory_11303_Title = {
    Text = "Basic Information"
  },
  AwakerStory_11303_UnlockDesc = {
    Text = "Awakener Level 1"
  },
  AwakerStory_11304_Content = {
    Text = [[
In A.F. 180, as the Northern Hemisphere suffered a severe drought, the Korasuyu River ceased to flow.

Local residents unearthed a monstrous skeleton from the riverbed's silt. Since the Korasuyu River signifies "turbid water" in local culture, the skeleton was named the "Bone of Chaos."

Marine biologists identified it as the skeleton of a humpback whale, approximately 32 feet long and entirely covered in a silvery substance. The following year, this skeleton was auctioned at the Aethis auction house for 130 million Leonian Florins.

The auction house refused to disclose the true identity of the buyer, but rumors suggest that the skeleton was transported to a private university on the outskirts of Londinium.]]
  },
  AwakerStory_11304_Title = {Text = "Story: I"},
  AwakerStory_11304_UnlockDesc = {
    Text = "Affinity Level 3"
  },
  AwakerStory_11305_Content = {
    Text = "The arrogance of disregarding others is merely an empty show of force. Beneath that elegant dress lies a rebellious heart known only to herself.\n\nTrapped in a beautiful cage crafted by sacred narratives, Murphy understands better than anyone the hypocrisy of humans and gods: the gaze of the congregation upon her is nothing but fear and pity, and the care shown by her \"nurturers\" is merely for a sacrificial offering. The end goal of her mission will not be glory, but her own death — she already knows the outcome. How could she be lost in the distant kingdom painted by doctrines?\n\nThe plans for deification, the revival of the old king, so many unrealistic expectations placed upon her — yet no one has ever cared whether she is willing to accept a doomed fate for an uncertain future.\n\nThe canary does not wish to remain forever trapped in a cage; thus it flaps its wings toward the thorny fence. Determined to wager her life to break free from the shackles of destiny, she must now decide the direction of her flight herself.\n\n\"My name is Murphy... don't think you can order me around! I know what I should do and what I shouldn't do.\""
  },
  AwakerStory_11305_Title = {Text = "Story: IV"},
  AwakerStory_11305_UnlockDesc = {
    Text = "Affinity Level 9"
  },
  AwakerStory_11305_UnlockDesc_1 = {
    Text = "Complete Chapter 5 \"Eye of the Storm\" in the normal mode of the main storyline."
  },
  AwakerStory_11306_Content = {
    Text = "An ocean spirit who once faced demise in solitude has found a miraculous second life on land.\n\nWhether naturally optimistic or choosing to forget to escape suffering, her guileless innocence exudes an irresistible charm that draws people to her side—perhaps this is a subtle ploy of hers to expand her \"circle of friends.\""
  },
  AwakerStory_11306_Title = {
    Text = "Basic Information"
  },
  AwakerStory_11306_UnlockDesc = {
    Text = "Awakener Level 1"
  },
  AwakerStory_11307_Content = {
    Text = "Born from Chaos, she embodies pure chaotic power, an untamed free spirit, and an undefined order.\n\nShe craves challenges and battles; only by unleashing her irrepressible destructive urge can she fulfill her creator's sole wish.\n\n—To safeguard this planet until the end. She has yearned for a truly exhilarating battle for far too long."
  },
  AwakerStory_11307_Title = {Text = "Story: IV"},
  AwakerStory_11307_UnlockDesc = {
    Text = "Affinity Level 9"
  },
  AwakerStory_11308_Content = {
    Text = [[
Do I deserve to have wishes?

If I do, can I become a part of my sister?

To make her whole, to make us whole.

Only then could I express "love" without reservation, and she could embrace "love" with an undivided heart.

Dear Tinct... perhaps this is what I, as the firstborn child, should do for you...]]
  },
  AwakerStory_11308_Title = {Text = "Story: IV"},
  AwakerStory_11308_UnlockDesc = {
    Text = "Affinity Level 9"
  },
  AwakerStory_11309_Content = {
    Text = [[
"Unforgiving Critiques", "Low-scoring Test Papers", "Substandard Research Reports"

During Doll's decades of teaching career, few students obtained certificates from her. Most students were driven away by her overly harsh attitude and turned to other professors. Over time, Professor Doll's notorious reputation spread among the students.

But there are still students who believe she uses these standards to select "disciples". Only those with the strongest will deserve to hold the key to open the door of truth and follow her to unveil the reality of the world.

Supported by such a belief, even though the possibility of graduating under Doll is minuscule, applications for mentorship under Doll still continuously flood her office.

Sometimes, Ramona, who was temporarily called to review the applications, couldn't help but think that if the students believed this way, it wouldn't be so bad.

In Ramona's view, she merely held the standard of awakeners to demand human students, nothing more]]
  },
  AwakerStory_11309_Title = {Text = "Story: II"},
  AwakerStory_11309_UnlockDesc = {
    Text = "Affinity Level 5"
  },
  AwakerStory_11310_Content = {
    Text = [[
Daffodil's whereabouts at Mythag University are nothing short of ghostly. After all, she possesses taboo knowledge of interdimensional travel, allowing her to come and go as she pleases, entirely unfettered by Black Pool's Silver Core Hub.

She routinely deals in mysterious instruments and materials of dubious origin, and sometimes assists other Awakeners in briefly evading the oversight of Mythag University.

Later, through negotiations, she opened her own "Worry-Relief Shop" in a disused room beside the infirmary on campus.

Of course, all goods for sale must first be registered and vetted by Mythag University.]]
  },
  AwakerStory_11310_Title = {Text = "Story: II"},
  AwakerStory_11310_UnlockDesc = {
    Text = "Affinity Level 5"
  },
  AwakerStory_11311_Content = {
    Text = "Recorder: Erich von Werner\nDate: November 7, 19@1\nCoordinates: 68°14′S, 67°10′W\nDue to an unusual number of floating sperm whale carcasses in our route, we were forced to land on this cursed island of ice. Below a glacial waterfall in the south shore fjord, the expedition team discovered the remains of a fifty-foot-long cephalopod. Its body was a deep indigo blue, densely covered in phosphorescent, luminous blue concentric rings, the edges of which secreted a thin layer of mucus. After we sampled and purified the substance, an unsettling quantity of blue crystals precipitated from the mucus.\n\nThe suckers on the creature's arms exceeded two feet in diameter, and the inner walls of the suckers were etched with patterns resembling an unknown script. The main nerve cord was in a semi-transparent, gelatinous state, maintaining a faint pulse even in the -30°C environment (see attached Figure D-7). Dr. Harris, the accompanying biologist, attempted to collect a tissue sample from the nerve cord, but the moment the scalpel made contact, the entire carcass instantly disintegrated into powder. Indigo-blue dust became visible, suspended throughout the laboratory.\n\nDuring the voyage home, Dr. Harris developed persistent delirium. He repeatedly drew geometric shapes combining spirals and polyhedrons on the cabin walls, screaming, \"They are spawning beneath the Antarctic ice sheet!\" On the morning of the second day, a patrolling crew member found him drowned in the ballast water tank. Autopsy revealed his alveoli were filled with indigo-blue microorganisms (identical to the octopus corpse dust). The captain ordered the incineration of all clothing that had come into contact with the samples.\n\nMay no one else ever touch the nightmare lurking beneath the ice.\n\n— Appendix No. 37, Antarctic Expedition Log"
  },
  AwakerStory_11311_Title = {Text = "Story: I"},
  AwakerStory_11311_UnlockDesc = {
    Text = "Affinity Level 3"
  },
  AwakerStory_11312_Content = {
    Text = [[
How could we ever forget the hero Uvhash? He was the finest of men. The warrior fell to his knees in the sunset-drenched sands, his body bathed in warm blood. Vultures circled above, singing his dirge:
<Italic:No tears shall honor you, no weeping shall lay you to rest,
For in life, your name had already conquered Rome.>]]
  },
  AwakerStory_11312_Title = {
    Text = "Basic Information"
  },
  AwakerStory_11312_UnlockDesc = {
    Text = "Awakener Level 1"
  },
  AwakerStory_11313_Content = {
    Text = "@1, A.F.@2\nDear Lord Cavendish,\n\nPlease forgive me. I took the liberty of asking Butler Frey to bring me ink and paper. I am struggling to maintain my last shred of sanity and dignity as I write this letter. Since I fell ill with this horrible disease, I haven’t been able to see Mother, Bobby, or you. Missing you all is enough to drive me crazy.\n\nI have been locked in this basement for... 353 days? I don't know. Maybe 326 days.\n\nIt's freezing here, and everything smells like it's rotting. My wounds are oozing black slime, and the rats have gnawed them beyond recognition. But it's okay. Pain is a good thing; it keeps my mind clear.\n\n\"An evil vampire,\" \"a disgrace to the family\"... locking me away was undoubtedly a wise decision. My soul has long been controlled by the devil. As I write this letter, I have just drained the blood of a deceased homeless man. Butler Frey said you had people find him on the street. Although the blood tasted a bit spoiled, I'm still glad to know that you care about me.\n\nAlso... could you give me a blanket? I have no clothes to cover myself now, and winter in Londinium is just too cold.\n\nEven now, I still really miss the time when we were kids, spending our holidays together at Whelton House.\n\nYour sincere sister,\nLeigh\n—Excerpt from <Italic: The Cansington Vampire Incident—Case Summary: Evidence C-601>"
  },
  AwakerStory_11313_Title = {Text = "Story: III"},
  AwakerStory_11313_UnlockDesc = {
    Text = "Affinity Level 7"
  },
  AwakerStory_11314_Content = {
    Text = [[
A.F. 31@1, December, the police received a report from the manager of the second theater in @2 Garden. The reporter claimed that there had been four small-scale fires in the theater within a week, and rumors of the "Ballet Ghost" were rampant among the members of the dance troupe renting the theater.

To ensure the smooth premiere of the ballet "Swan's Lament," the police launched a joint investigation with the West District Fire Department.

The day before the performance, Mythag University finally took over the investigation. The investigators noted traces of Gnosis residue behind several fire points. Eventually, Investigator @3 discovered an Awakener in the underground ruins of the second theater.

This Awakener was not a mindless individual; she identified herself as "Liz." After communication, the Awakener Liz eventually admitted to her arson crime. After the premiere of "Swan's Lament," Investigator @3 took Liz back to Mythag University for formal incorporation.

According to historical records, when the fire broke out at the second theater in @2 Garden on A.F. 29@1, a ballet was being performed. Among those who perished in the flames were a number of nobles in the audience, as well as a young prima ballerina named "Elizabeth Sur."]]
  },
  AwakerStory_11314_Title = {Text = "Story: I"},
  AwakerStory_11314_UnlockDesc = {
    Text = "Awakener Level 3"
  },
  AwakerStory_11315_Content = {
    Text = [[
One step, then another, I slowly walked into the water. The nurse at the sanatorium never allowed me to go this far. I hope a patient who will soon be unable to afford the sanatorium's fees doesn't cause her too much blame.

The sunset's afterglow reflected on the sea. Waves approached gently, lifting my skirt softly. The seawater's body temperature felt warm like a mother's embrace.

My body had never felt as light as it did at this moment; a desolate volcano lay within my chest, and now only the sea breeze remained there.

"Let's go home."

I heard the sea calling me in my parents' voices. They went to the other side of the sea to raise money for my treatment. If I hadn't been given such an unfortunate body, they wouldn't have had to struggle so much. If only I could vanish quietly into the sea on a moonlit night... I had thought this countless times, but thinking of my parents' sorrowful faces, I could only give up.

But one day, on a moonlit night, the ship my parents were on quietly disappeared into the sea.

"Let's go home."

I used all my strength to quicken my pace. The sea always calmly accepts all the suffering souls, and for me, the place where my parents are is the eternal refuge.

When the darkness descends from all sides, I was finally able to breathe freely for the first time in my life]]
  },
  AwakerStory_11315_Title = {Text = "Story: III"},
  AwakerStory_11315_UnlockDesc = {
    Text = "Affinity Level 7"
  },
  AwakerStory_11316_Content = {
    Text = "His transcendent wisdom exacts a heavy toll on his body; he must sleep for more than fifteen hours a day, and even in his waking hours, he is haunted by a persistent lethargy.\n\nWithin his dreams, he sometimes feels the fury of the gods; at other times, he glimpses the intersection of fractured timelines. Occasionally, he even wanders into the furthest depths, coming face-to-face with the Divine itself.\n\nHe has never sought their revelations or prophecies, yet no matter how he tries to evade them, the visions always come to pass.\n\nHe never asked for offerings. To be worshiped, to be feared—these were burdens thrust upon him by others, and they hold no interest for him.\n\nTo be reborn was nothing more than an unwelcome interruption of an eternal dream.\n\nNo need for invocation. No need for prayer."
  },
  AwakerStory_11316_Title = {Text = "Story: IV"},
  AwakerStory_11316_UnlockDesc = {
    Text = "Affinity Level 9"
  },
  AwakerStory_11317_Content = {
    Text = "...\n\nExperiment Date: @2, A.F.@1\nExperiment Objective: Observe and record mutational responses of a Dissolution patient following tissue and organ grafting.\n\nExperiment Steps: @3 @4\nThe experiment was conducted on the subject using tissues and organs sourced from her deceased brother, in order to observe the rejection response between first-degree relatives. The poor wretch was shot dead while evading police capture. @3 experiment was highly successful; the wound turned red and sprouted tentacles... with blood spurting out like liquid rubies.\n\n@3 @3\nThe subject demonstrated remarkable endurance, refusing morphine injections.\n\nPost-experiment, her bloodlust intensified, and her temperament became... indescribable, not a type I am adept at handling.\n\n—Excerpt from Herbert's <Italic:Dissolution Experiment Records, Group4, No. @1>"
  },
  AwakerStory_11317_Title = {Text = "Story: I"},
  AwakerStory_11317_UnlockDesc = {
    Text = "Affinity Level 4"
  },
  AwakerStory_11318_Content = {
    Text = [[
Do not approach, do not touch, do not look directly, do not pity; there are beings in this world that are meant to dwell alone in the darkness.

Though it is not her intention, if you gaze affectionately into her eyes because of her frail figure, timid voice, or childlike clothing, you will fall into eternal stillness and silence.]]
  },
  AwakerStory_11318_Title = {
    Text = "Basic Information"
  },
  AwakerStory_11318_UnlockDesc = {
    Text = "Awakener Level 1"
  },
  AwakerStory_11319_Content = {
    Text = "Day 45 of joining the dance troupe. I stood on stage as the lead performer.\n\nThe scorching lights struck the hem of my skirt, and the tiny diamonds scattered a dazzling brilliance across the air. The glare made it hard to see, but the thunderous applause told me that my performance shone brighter than any gem.\n\nIn endless spinning, all the dust of the world is purified by the dance, and the beauty of art is carried out to every corner. This is my wish and my mission as a dancer—\n\nBut who are those people lurking in the dark corners beneath the stage?\n\nLisette, the girl known for her carefree and upright nature—why is she whispering with that notorious lord?\n\nAngelica, the genius who always looks down on the other dancers—why is she lifting her skirt for that infamous playboy?\n\nSuch disgrace... such filth! Oh God, my muse, tell me—what must I do to guard my stage from the darkness? What light is needed to dispel this filth—"
  },
  AwakerStory_11319_Title = {Text = "Story: III"},
  AwakerStory_11319_UnlockDesc = {
    Text = "Affinity Level 7"
  },
  AwakerStory_11320_Content = {
    Text = "From her childhood, Casiah exhibited an extraordinary talent for mimicry.\n\nNo matter how intricate the dance, she could replicate it flawlessly after just one viewing; no matter how complex the magic trick, she could master it with only one lesson. Voice, facial expressions, even smiles and the subtle aura a person carried—Casiah could perfectly replicate them, even to the point of being utterly indistinguishable from the original. Had she been born into different circumstances, or found a different calling, that gift might have carried her toward an entirely different life.\n\nUnfortunately, she was just a child growing up in an obscure, low-rent circus. The circus people only thought of profiting from her talent, while the patrons outside the tent—they came only to purchase joy, with no pity to spare.\n\nNo one cared for Casiah's happiness, but fortunately, Casiah did not care either. Every time she observed the laughing audience, the bickering troupe members, the fortune teller silently weeping over her photos, she felt only a detached curiosity: Why do they make these faces off-stage? Why do they keep performing when no one is watching? Why do they call it a \"manifestation of emotion\"?\n\nWhat is happiness? What is sadness? And what does it feel like to experience the despair and terror of impending death, just as the \"benefactor\" who slit her throat once spoke of?\n\nAs a human, she could find no answers. But as a child of magic, as a being capable of collecting \"emotions\" from others, perhaps she could finally gain an experience she had never possessed.\n\nThus, she founded the Magical Carnival and brought it around the world.\n\nPeople come to purchase joy, yet pay with every last desire.\n\n\"Roll up, roll up, come one, come all—step into my carnival! For just a little joy, just a little sorrow, you'll witness the greatest spectacle this century has ever seen!\""
  },
  AwakerStory_11320_Title = {Text = "Story: III"},
  AwakerStory_11320_UnlockDesc = {
    Text = "Affinity Level 7"
  },
  AwakerStory_11321_Content = {
    Text = [[
It began with nothing more than a glass of grape soda standing in for red wine.

In an unnoticed corner, Sorel adopted a delicate, pitiable expression, drinking with a mere two or three students.

Next came a modest afternoon tea.

In the student cafeteria, Sorel politely turned down the macarons offered by the students, her eyes lingering with a hint of genuine affection.

And finally, it culminated in a grand salon, and the full blossoming of a rose.

The lounge was lavished with flowers and jewels; the brilliant rose and young students toasted one another, thoroughly enjoying the elegant gathering.

The newly appointed Keeper witnessed it all, silently praying that her next move would not be "to become the principal of Mythag University."]]
  },
  AwakerStory_11321_Title = {Text = "Story: II"},
  AwakerStory_11321_UnlockDesc = {
    Text = "Affinity Level 5"
  },
  AwakerStory_11322_Content = {
    Text = "In the gray, viscous Sea of Primordial Essence, emptiness prevails; the notions shared by travelers crossing dimensions remain confined to abstract descriptions and imagination.\n\nIt wants to confirm with its own eyes the \"places of human yearning,\" to witness the magnificent wonders of the mortal world, and to experience the bittersweet nuances of human love and loss.\n\nYet above all, it desires a specific person, someone to cherish, someone to trust.\n\nA fair trade means equality, detachment, and accounts settled—not a fraction more is paid, nor a fraction less taken. But it yearns for something different—an unconditional trust to bridge the divide, to break through cautious probe, to thaw the lingering ice.\n\nIt had found that, then lost it. But it would find it again."
  },
  AwakerStory_11322_Title = {Text = "Story: IV"},
  AwakerStory_11322_UnlockDesc = {
    Text = "Affinity Level 9"
  },
  AwakerStory_11323_Content = {
    Text = "Watched by countless nights, the sculptor suffered from Dissolution slips beneath the murmuring waves, falling into writhing dreams:\nAs Lemuria's spirals inflamed by her kindreds, its majestic walls arise in her hands.\n\nAs the Father and His servants slumbering into epics, their statues find immortality under her carving.\n\nHer senses dull. Her body stiffens. Her chisel nearly escapes.\n\nCoral-like white mists have crept to her forearms. Hands tremble under her gaze. A smile flickers. Her life will fade like an extinguishing candle, while her body will step beyond eternal's door.\n\nHer wish fullfilled as she sinking onto the seabed. Coral shattering to foam, black slime of Dissolution threads into the ocean—she finally embraces the City long-lost in currents, and mingles with its splendor—together, ever after."
  },
  AwakerStory_11323_Title = {Text = "Story: IV"},
  AwakerStory_11323_UnlockDesc = {
    Text = "Affinity Level 9"
  },
  AwakerStory_11324_Content = {
    Text = [[
"Indulgence and lust lead to eternal fire as a warning..."

For 23 days, the monk stood outside her gate, reciting monotonous scriptures.

Wanda had him tied up and brought in.

The monk said, 'Why worry about suffering? Where the Lord's spirit is, there is freedom.'
She stripped him.

The monk said, 'Why worry about clothes? The lilies of the field neither spin nor bow.'
She severed his limbs.

The monk said, 'Why worry about blood? All flesh dies.'
Wanda laughed, 'I will not only make you bleed, but also turn you into my slave, forever.'
'Why?' the monk lifted his head, 'Shouldn't you show mercy to your companion as I showed mercy to you?'
Wanda studied the monk. His eyes were as blue as the clear sky.

She gouged out his eyes.

Unable to bear the torture, the monk eventually died. The local parish feared her wealth and power, and no one dared to accuse her.

Before dying, the monk said, '@2 is near, you should...'
Years passed, and Wanda had long forgotten the monk's face and name, only remembering his eyes. On the night she was about to be devoured by @2, she recalled the monk's unfinished words.

'@2 is near, you should...'
In her blurred consciousness, she speculated on the monk's last words, but found nothing."]]
  },
  AwakerStory_11324_Title = {Text = "Story: IV"},
  AwakerStory_11324_UnlockDesc = {
    Text = "Affinity Level 9"
  },
  AwakerStory_11325_Content = {
    Text = "\"You bear a noble mission, the hope of His return to the world.\"\n\n\"Be good, obey... When He wakes again, everyone will dwell in the eternal realm.\"\n\nThe secret girl, whose birth could not be revealed, became the high priest's treasure for some reason. The once-neglected infant transformed into the saint linked to destiny and a mysterious civilization.\n\nThe ascetic mother raised her; worship and adoration surrounded her. Whatever she desired, someone would offer without hesitation.\n\nHad the D-phenomenon not occurred, had the vessel of God not weakened, she would have simply succeeded the high priest, leading the followers in an orderly manner.\n\nYet, everything she gained came at a heavy price—a fate she never wished for, predestined to end inescapably.\n\nTo become the Mother of God, bearing the prophesied child—the glory of the saint demanded her willing sacrifice of body and life.\n\nThe day a second heart began beating in her chest, her soul turned into a surging torrent, destined to vanish with time."
  },
  AwakerStory_11325_Title = {Text = "Story: III"},
  AwakerStory_11325_UnlockDesc = {
    Text = "Affinity Level 7"
  },
  AwakerStory_11325_UnlockDesc_1 = {
    Text = "Complete Chapter 5 \"Eye of the Storm\" in the normal mode of the main storyline."
  },
  AwakerStory_11326_Content = {
    Text = [[
In June of A.F. 282, acting upon an investigation request submitted by the Mystea Treaty Committee, we dispatched a survey team to the New Leonia region.

Since the meteorite impact a year ago, the area has experienced an abnormally elevated mortality rate.

Furthermore, investigators discovered several species of mutated flora at the impact site. Instrumental analysis confirmed that these plants contain high levels of radiation, suspected to have been introduced by the meteorite.

However, no extraterrestrial minerals were found within the impact crater. According to villager testimony, on the third day after the impact, a group of scientists in white coats dissected and removed the meteorite in its entirety.

(Note: Suspected to be a non-governmental scientific organization; identity remains unverified.)

Following coordination between the Committee and local authorities, all residents have been evacuated, and the area has been officially declared a prohibited living zone.

According to calculations by the Mythag University Physics Laboratory, this residential ban must remain in effect for at least 80 years.]]
  },
  AwakerStory_11326_Title = {Text = "Story: I"},
  AwakerStory_11326_UnlockDesc = {
    Text = "Affinity Level 3"
  },
  AwakerStory_11327_Content = {
    Text = "Lotan has her own criteria when it comes to choosing worthy opponents.\n\nShe finds academic warriors tiresome; most have read themselves into a stupor, their heads filled with nothing but theoretical maneuvers that fail on the field.\n\nMilitary standouts, meanwhile, are too shackled by red tape and moral dogma to offer any real thrill.\n\nOnly those rare geniuses—blessed with raw talent and an innate instinct for slaughter—can earn her favor.\n\nA primordial beast, as old as the planet itself, kept her thirst for battle in check and waited with near-religious patience for her chosen opponent to reach his zenith. What a gifted youth he was—commanding power from the abyssal deep, his formidable spirit capable of bridging even the Outer Gods. Given time, he would surely have grown into a warrior worthy of her blade.\n\nBut perhaps the vast stretches of time had dulled her judgment. This time, the Spirit of Chaos misjudged her mark. As for the details, Lotan refuses to speak of it to anyone.\n\nAll we know is that since then, she has held nothing but utter contempt for those who lack ambition or wallow in mediocrity."
  },
  AwakerStory_11327_Title = {Text = "Story: III"},
  AwakerStory_11327_UnlockDesc = {
    Text = "Affinity Level 7"
  },
  AwakerStory_11328_Content = {
    Text = "Silver Core Number: B-005\nDate of Excavation: @3, A.F.1@1\nExcavation Site: Rural Flemish Lowlands—ruins of an unnamed ancient Roman mausoleum\nDetailed Record: The core's original bearer, Ludwig Prynn, was sentenced to burn at the stake by the local Inquisition following a necromancy incident. Prynn claimed to have acquired this Silver Core on the battlefields of the Ninth Holy Crusade. He then traveled to the outskirts of Brabantum, where, alongside his \"Servant from the Stars\" and \"Invisible Companion,\" he conducted blood rites to summon the \"Great Unnamable.\"\n\nRecorder: Ward Philips\n—<Italic:Awakener Silver Core Acquisition Report: B-005>"
  },
  AwakerStory_11328_Title = {Text = "Story: I"},
  AwakerStory_11328_UnlockDesc = {
    Text = "Affinity Level 3"
  },
  AwakerStory_11329_Content = {
    Text = "In solitude, one must act as a team. The twenty-four minds are crowded together—they whisper and chuckle in the dark, tearing at 24's soul, craving to devour her.\n\nThe stench from the corner sewer, the cotton drifting through the workshop, the stale black bread... The past has long faded, and no one remembers the ordinary worker from the East District. She has finally shed her weary body, only to step into a new quagmire."
  },
  AwakerStory_11329_Title = {
    Text = "Basic Information"
  },
  AwakerStory_11329_UnlockDesc = {
    Text = "Awakener Level 1"
  },
  AwakerStory_11330_Content = {
    Text = "Among these sisters, one of them should never have been born.\n\nOn the Desolate of the Lyra constellation, Faint and Tinct spent half their lives shrouded in malice.\n\nBut who is the unacknowledged one?\n\nSister Faint is powerful yet uncontrollable; the life force she plunders seems to flow away like a river, leaving her to barely survive by licking the remaining dewdrops.\n\nSister Tinct is beautiful yet struggles to be independent; her life is as stubborn as duckweed, yet rooted nowhere, causing her to revolve around her sister.\n\nPerhaps they both believe they are the one who should not exist. It's just that Faint made her decision earlier—using her own life as a threat, she forced her sister onto the journey of departure.\n\n\"Leave, Tinct. Don't let me hold you back.\"\n\n\"You shall sing among the stars, becoming the most dazzling color.\""
  },
  AwakerStory_11330_Title = {Text = "Story: III"},
  AwakerStory_11330_UnlockDesc = {
    Text = "Affinity Level 7"
  },
  AwakerStory_11331_Content = {
    Text = [[
Like a real lighthouse, most of the time her presence is nothing more than a steady glow at a corner, peaceful, isolated. Her words only illuminates when confusion stirs the air, while her guidances clearer than nautical navigation.

Only when she meets with other Aequor visitors does the light reveal her shadow, twisting under paranoid madness.

In contrast to her serene and intellectual appearance, Faros has unexpectedly profound knowledge in ocean voyages. Despite the unresolved suspicions of abducting and sacrificing sailors, she has assisted the university in revising numerous nautical documents under the Keeper's supervision.

According to feedback from sailors of cooperative vessels, Faros's revisions, though effective, often (though not clear whether she is intentionally or not) steer the course towards the Monge Triangle.

The university has then prohibited Faros from accessing any ocean-related materials.]]
  },
  AwakerStory_11331_Title = {Text = "Story: II"},
  AwakerStory_11331_UnlockDesc = {
    Text = "Affinity Level 5"
  },
  AwakerStory_11332_Content = {
    Text = "A \"golem\" forged by Caligura's court alchemist, Marcus Antys, at the cost of countless living souls.\n\nDue to the imperfection of the alchemical ritual, he had to drink a large amount of blood daily. He killed Caligura's political enemies and helped him claim the throne of Rome.\n\nThe tyrant Caligura was murdered less than four years into his reign. The golem was also locked in the underground of the destroyed altar by enraged and fearful mobs, forced to endure hunger and thirst for nearly a thousand years.\n\nThroughout the long centuries, he survived on the blood of rats. The thirst ingrained deep within his nature slowly drove him mad.\n\n<Italic:Not enough, far from enough...>\nDuring the @2 period, a Lavantian sorcerer found him, promising to free him on one condition: he must slaughter the Remouans on the battlefield.\n\n<Italic:A deal like that? How could he refuse.>\nHe completed the task with ease, but there was a small complication: in his frenzy, he slaughtered every soul on the battlefield and drained them dry—including the sorcerer, and ultimately, himself."
  },
  AwakerStory_11332_Title = {Text = "Story: III"},
  AwakerStory_11332_UnlockDesc = {
    Text = "Affinity Level 7"
  },
  AwakerStory_11333_Content = {
    Text = "Awakening Material: Silver Core #G752a, unearthed from a festering mud heap at the ruins of Londinium's Newgate Prison. Investigator @2 accidentally slipped on a shattered skull while walking through the dim, grimy prison corridor and stumbled upon it by chance.\n\nThe awakening result deviated from expectations—what emerged from the black D-Slime was not some vicious death-row convict or a hulking executioner, but a petite young maiden with a sly smile."
  },
  AwakerStory_11333_Title = {Text = "Story: I"},
  AwakerStory_11333_UnlockDesc = {
    Text = "Awakener Level 3"
  },
  AwakerStory_11334_Content = {
    Text = "The name @2 appears time and again upon the pages of history.\n\nPriestess. Mother. Queen. Sorceress. Too many titles have been attached to this name, leaving scholars unable to determine which one truly defines the Awakener we know today.\n\nThais herself does not hesitate to share her past with us—all of it is her, yet none of it is entirely her.\n\n\"It was she who was born of noble blood.\"\n\nThais was always the most radiant girl in the temple. As the child of the High Priest, she moved with a fluid grace and carried the gentle warmth of moonlight.\n\n\"It was she who knelt before the Tree.\"\n\nThais was the vibrant leaf on the \"Tree\"; her devotion had earned her the blessings of It.\n\n\"It was she who was bled dry.\"\n\nWhen cataclysm struck and the pillars of civilization crumbled, the ancient, ignorant civilization chose her—their most exceptional daughter.\n\n\"It was she whose veins now pulse with crimson sap.\"\n\nThe \"Tree\" revered by all made its own choice. Its branches took root within her, granting her a near-eternal life.\n\n\"But it was not she who wished to destroy civilization.\"\n\nThe annihilation of the world was never what Thais desired.\n\n\"But Miss Thais, what do you truly desire?\"\n\n\"My dear, didn't we agree? When our bond bears fruit, you will have your answer.\""
  },
  AwakerStory_11334_Title = {Text = "Story: III"},
  AwakerStory_11334_UnlockDesc = {
    Text = "Affinity Level 7"
  },
  AwakerStory_11335_Content = {
    Text = [[
Alva had doubted her righteousness, but those bewildered days and nights brought her profound enlightenment.

Illusions are tangible.

The initial starting point never changed; the justice she fights for is not an organization turned aggressor, not an individual shouting slogans, but a genuine existence within her beliefs.

All life, all innocence, all dreams, aspirations, and beautiful yearnings can easily turn to ash under gunfire.

What is lost in war will never return, like hellish demons devouring all goodness.

Thus, those who start wars for selfish desires must also taste the ashes of destruction. There will be true heroes, with noble intentions, selflessly fighting for the bright future of all.

This is the value called justice.

......

Wrong, then correct it.

Make the sacrifices worthwhile, make this phantom pain of severed legs and limbs worthwhile.

If there is anything unfortunate destroyed, reclaim it with these new prosthetics.

Those small and fragile things will never lose their shine.

Everything is for that truly bloodless, tearless utopia.]]
  },
  AwakerStory_11335_Title = {Text = "Story: IV"},
  AwakerStory_11335_UnlockDesc = {
    Text = "Affinity Level 9"
  },
  AwakerStory_11336_Content = {
    Text = [[
Beware: a siren's mesmerizing charm lurks under her seemingly calm and rational words. Never show curiosity towards the unique appearance beneath her malformed helmet; never forget her long-lasting dissatisfaction with this humanoid body.

Her gleaming light once lured moths to its molten warmth. Her burning fire once guided the lost to their doom. Now, only confusion flickers in her lighthouse.]]
  },
  AwakerStory_11336_Title = {
    Text = "Basic Information"
  },
  AwakerStory_11336_UnlockDesc = {
    Text = "Awakener Level 1"
  },
  AwakerStory_11337_Content = {
    Text = [[
The flood that swept across the world washed away the treasures of civilization, but it also cleared the dust from history's pages.

When the waters finally receded, fragments of a forgotten past surfaced among the ruins of ancient Morsul.

The "Tree" stood at the Karage River's source, weeping crimson sap that flowed downstream to nurture civilizations.

The "Tree" was undying, ever-verdant through the ages.

Ultimately, modern historians concluded that the "Tree" had no physical form; rather, It was a metaphor for ancient civilization, a sacred, incorporeal symbol.

In every unseen corner of the world, its seeds have quietly taken root.]]
  },
  AwakerStory_11337_Title = {Text = "Story: I"},
  AwakerStory_11337_UnlockDesc = {
    Text = "Affinity Level 5"
  },
  AwakerStory_11338_Content = {
    Text = "\"Master, whip me.\"\n\nThe fire of desire burned in her eyes that should have dried up, melting wax dripping like tears.\n\nThirst, pain, curses, filth—all the humiliation she craved, all the pleasures she offered, finally arrived upon her in this moment."
  },
  AwakerStory_11338_Title = {Text = "Story: IV"},
  AwakerStory_11338_UnlockDesc = {
    Text = "Affinity Level 9"
  },
  AwakerStory_11339_Content = {
    Text = [[
She is the singer among the stars, the shimmering stardust.

She is the bird trapped in a gilded cage, the discarded phonograph.

When her home planet collapse into the void, she is compelled to embrace the hope of life, becoming a wanderer in the unclaimed depths of space, an eternal seeker singing in search of home.

"Sister... Though I am the one who can walk freely among us, you have always been the one supporting me."]]
  },
  AwakerStory_11339_Title = {
    Text = "Basic Information"
  },
  AwakerStory_11339_UnlockDesc = {
    Text = "Awakener Level 1"
  },
  AwakerStory_11340_Content = {
    Text = "This projected body remains in the form of a girl who passed away prematurely. With tattered clothes, pale skin, and eyes filled with shadows of the past, it silently tells of a history entwined with illness and suffering."
  },
  AwakerStory_11340_Title = {
    Text = "Basic Information"
  },
  AwakerStory_11340_UnlockDesc = {
    Text = "Awakener Level 1"
  },
  AwakerStory_11341_Content = {
    Text = "Since the @2 incident, Caecus has reconciled with us and become an external member of the Awakening system. His understanding of @1 knowledge is merely superficial, yet he is eager to showcase and share it. \n\n In front of people like Tulu, Miryam, and Goliath, he is filled with humility, but he casts a gloomy and unfriendly gaze toward other races—especially humans. Researchers who have read the files understand his paranoia, but some hot-tempered Awakeners cannot tolerate it. This tense atmosphere often requires Sylvia to mediate and diffuse the situation, and a trust relationship has gradually developed between Caecus and Sylvia. \n\n Under Sylvia's guidance, Caecus has awakened the \"tolerance of higher races,\" avoiding provocations from others without comment. \n\n \"That child often recalls his human mother with warmth. It is said that a mother is the benchmark for a child's understanding of the world, and his hostility toward humans is essentially acquired. So, he just lacks some guidance and care,\" Sylvia wrote in her psychological counseling records."
  },
  AwakerStory_11341_Title = {Text = "Story: II"},
  AwakerStory_11341_UnlockDesc = {
    Text = "Affinity Level 5"
  },
  AwakerStory_11342_Content = {
    Text = [[
The Awakener's file manager has transferred her file to the student administration several times, but she has repeatedly sent it back herself, burying it under a mountain of documents.

"Just leave it here. It will eventually need to be delivered."

Her tone remains as calm as ever, but her gaze flickers unpredictably.

What monumental emotions lie beneath this calm?]]
  },
  AwakerStory_11342_Title = {
    Text = "Basic Information"
  },
  AwakerStory_11342_UnlockDesc = {
    Text = "Awakener Level 1"
  },
  AwakerStory_11343_Content = {
    Text = [[
"If it's your first time carrying out an investigation mission, go find little Ogier to accompany you!" 

In response to the anxiety of new investigators, experienced seniors always offer this advice. Ogier's popularity among students is evident from this. 

Although his old-fashioned personality occasionally causes minor incidents, they support each other and lift one another up. Ogier always achieves the most harmonious rhythm with the investigators. In recent years, having Ogier accompany new investigators on their first missions has become a consensus among everyone at the school. Jokes like "Ogier prepares a cloak for female investigators" and "Ogier blushes when he sees legs" have also spread among the students. 

The title of "Death Knight" has gradually been forgotten, drowned in trust and warmth, leaving only a tiny thorn embedded in the young boy's heart.]]
  },
  AwakerStory_11343_Title = {Text = "Story: II"},
  AwakerStory_11343_UnlockDesc = {
    Text = "Affinity Level 5"
  },
  AwakerStory_11344_Content = {
    Text = [[
On a clear morning twelve years ago, in the eastern district of Londinium, a baby girl tightly wrapped in a scarf appeared at the door of the poorhouse. This was not uncommon in the paranoid eastern district, but what angered young Sarah was that, in the harsh winter, the heartless abandoner had also wrapped the baby girl's mouth and nose in the scarf. Moreover, this baby girl neither cried nor made a fuss; if not for those clear and bright eyes blinking a few times under the impact, Sarah would have almost thought she was dead.

Just as Sarah thought she would become another "sister" to a well-behaved child, the then-director sent this child, for the price of one Leo Fang, to the tailor of the eastern district market.

"We can't afford to raise that child. Becoming a tailor's daughter, although she will suffer a bit, at least she can learn a skill."

What can a child not even two months old know about "skills"?

Feeling her empty stomach, Sarah did not refute the director's decision.]]
  },
  AwakerStory_11344_Title = {Text = "Story: III"},
  AwakerStory_11344_UnlockDesc = {
    Text = "Affinity Level 7"
  },
  AwakerStory_11345_Content = {
    Text = "Cité Art Salon Exhibition, A.F.2@1.\n\n\"Let me take her home!\" The assailant shouted while hammering at the sculptor August's final work, \"The Nameless Ms. Coral,\" before hastily stopped by the congregation. However, this unstrung old man had surprisingly turned out to be none other than the long-reclusive August himself.\n\nFor a time, speculations and discussions about \"The Nameless Ms. Coral\" flooded in.\n\nSome people said it was inspired by a female apprentice named Sanga, who was the actual owner of August's best works. August is merely a shameful plagiarist.\n\nSome people said that Sanga came from an illustrious family—her father was a renowned writer, and her brother was a diplomat. In order to pursue the sculpture art, she disengaged with her family and set alone to Paris, living penuriously until her death.\n\nSome people said Sanga suffered from a strange illness. Ominous black ooze streamed on her body, and her each carving transformed a part of her flesh into coral. \"The Nameless Ms. Coral\" was actually her coraled appearance, not a sculpture at all.\n\nOther people said...\n\nThe apprentice, the devoted, the patient. Words pile upon Ms. Coral, sculpting her as the crowd dispersed from the exhibition hall. She blinks in the pouring moonlight. She's still waiting, and waiting—for her moment of returning home."
  },
  AwakerStory_11345_Title = {Text = "Story: III"},
  AwakerStory_11345_UnlockDesc = {
    Text = "Affinity Level 7"
  },
  AwakerStory_11346_Content = {
    Text = [[
At the onset of the terrible plague, Wanda ordered the castle gates to be welded shut, retreating into a life of complete isolation and indulgence.

There were jesters jesting and poets reciting spontaneously. There were musicians playing, as well as food and wine.

All joy and peace resided within the castle, while the outside was a world shrouded in @2 darkness.

Just as the area outside the walls became a wasteland, Wanda held an exceptionally luxurious masquerade for her hundreds of followers.

It was a three-day, three-night extravagant and debauched revelry. As the midnight bell tolled on the third day, some guests went completely mad, while others turned into puddles of black goo. Wanda's face cracked like porcelain, black @2 oozing from the seams of her mask.

Frightened followers huddled next to Wanda, trembling, but she remained calm.

With a whip, she commanded those who had gone completely mad to continue drinking and playing music without pause.

The bizarre masquerade ended on the fourth morning, and the opulent hall was filled with black @2 sludge and red blood.

No one knew what had transpired here.]]
  },
  AwakerStory_11346_Title = {Text = "Story: III"},
  AwakerStory_11346_UnlockDesc = {
    Text = "Affinity Level 7"
  },
  AwakerStory_11347_Content = {
    Text = [[
According to the "Cataclysm Event Record III," the Keeper brought back this piece of Silver Core from the Londinium Orphanage. Accompanying the Silver Core was a tiny, patch-covered teddy bear.

This Silver weighs about 2.1 grams, is slender and smooth, resembling a teardrop. Those who come into direct contact with the Silver will fall into a Stasis State, maintaining the posture of touching the Silver until Awakened by someone else. To prevent accidental contact, Researcher Doll kept this Silver in a closed glass orb and replaced the teddy bear's eyes.

"It looks as if it has been crying every day."]]
  },
  AwakerStory_11347_Title = {Text = "Story: I"},
  AwakerStory_11347_UnlockDesc = {
    Text = "Awakener Level 3"
  },
  AwakerStory_11347_UnlockDesc_1 = {
    Text = "Complete Chapter 1 \"East District's Enigma\": Normal"
  },
  AwakerStory_11348_Content = {
    Text = "The smell of rust spread through the air.\n\n<Italic:That is... the smell of \"food.\">\nThe girl slowly opened her eyes. Her mind was a complete blur after being injected with large doses of sedatives for so long. Lying in front of her was a beagle with its throat torn out—<Italic:Bambi>, she thought. <Italic:Or was it Bobby?>\nJust as the girl was lost in memories, a sharp pain shot through her abdomen—she was attacked by her \"food\". The bound vagrant before her trembled violently, seemingly screaming at the top of his lungs.\n\n\"Vampire! Monster... monster!!\"\n\nYet, the girl heard none of it. She only stared blankly, gently touching the blood on her abdomen.\n\nA large amount of warm blood poured from the wound like slippery satin, joyfully spreading across the floor.\n\nSo, she could still feel pain. She could still bleed.\n\nTears slid silently down her face. She reached out with her thin, blood-stained hands, and gently cupped her prey's face.\n\n\"Next time... could you please try a little harder?\""
  },
  AwakerStory_11348_Title = {Text = "Story: IV"},
  AwakerStory_11348_UnlockDesc = {
    Text = "Affinity Level 9"
  },
  AwakerStory_11349_Content = {
    Text = "When he was chosen from among thousands of children and ascended the throne, Tulu was not even as tall as the blue stone throne.\n\nYet, no one dared to question his indifference or his perpetual slumber; all understood these to be the signs of a King listening to the divine.\n\nThe young King's decisions invariably solved every hardship, and his prophecies never failed to pass.\n\nTulu accepted this life: entering the dreams of a \"God,\" meeting an existence beyond comprehension, ruling his nation through oracles, and sinking once more into sleep.\n\nThe gears of this civilization turned on the will of the divine. He was content to simply follow the current—to be nothing more than the sole \"messenger\" for a higher power.\n\nHowever, Tulu held one prophecy back, the only one he never spoke: that the nation would be destroyed by a deluge, and their civilization would be entombed beneath the sea.\n\nBecause he knew all, he knew that their destruction was immutable. But he resolved that, in their final hours, they should not live in terror and despair.\n\nThis was his final decree—made not as an \"Divine Envoy,\" but as a King."
  },
  AwakerStory_11349_Title = {Text = "Story: III"},
  AwakerStory_11349_UnlockDesc = {
    Text = "Affinity Level 7"
  },
  AwakerStory_11350_Content = {
    Text = [[
After being awakened, Murphy: Fauxborn frequently has a dream of escaping. In the end of that dream, she holds her "Mother's" dagger and plunges it through her own chest under the brilliant moonlight. The dream then abruptly ends, and the moment she opens her eyes, they meet the gaze of the ivory statue at the foot of her bed.

In Mythag, Murphy: Fauxborn acts like a younger version of her "Nurturer." She wears white mourning clothes year-round, rarely laughs or speaks lightly with others. Only when the conversation turns to her preference for sweets does a crack appear in her flawless, saintly facade.

<Italic:(Archivist's Annotation: I hope next time she wishes to enjoy cupcakes, she will ask for it immediately, rather than leaving a note requesting delivery to her room after everyone's afternoon tea has ended.)

She maintains a distance from any Awakener with relation to the Seafarers. Unlike her other-world counterpart, she never deliberately avoids contact with them; however, the frozen, emotionless expression and thinly veiled hostility in her sarcasm subconsciously drive away those who don't want a confrontation.]]
  },
  AwakerStory_11350_Title = {Text = "Story: II"},
  AwakerStory_11350_UnlockDesc = {
    Text = "Affinity Level 5"
  },
  AwakerStory_11351_Content = {
    Text = [[
At the age of twenty-five, Ryker encountered a strange suspect while investigating a murder case in a locked room.

After obtaining an absolutely complete chain of evidence, the suspect mysteriously vanished from the police station, with the handcuffs still intact. Of course, this was the responsibility of the on-duty police, but Ryker still received his reward.

Ryker took this reward and traveled overseas for a vacation. He then encountered the fleeing suspect by a stall. The suspect was placing bets, and upon seeing Ryker, remained unfazed, merely inviting him to join the game and promising that if Ryker won, he would willingly surrender.

Ryker didn't win a single round.

He lost his pipe, lost his tie, lost his hat, and lost his trench coat.

When he was completely naked, the suspect returned all his clothes to him, stating that those stakes were too small. Without hesitation, Ryker asked what the suspect wanted to bet on and readily agreed when the other proposed wagering an arm.

After several additional stakes, the suspect pulled out a revolver. Facing a life-or-death gamble, Ryker picked up the gun without hesitation and aimed it at his temple.

After a gunshot, Ryker collapsed. The suspect summoned back his undead to mock his ignorance. However, Ryker's first words were, "What are we betting on next?"

His arrogance finally piqued the demon's interest. The suspect, whose true name was "N@2@3," decided to let the wager continue.

"N" produced three top hats and told him to make the "best choice" that would allow him to restore his body.

Ryker chose a hat, and "N" opened one that was empty, asking if he wanted to change his choice. Ryker shook his head.

- Don't you understand probability?

- I just believe in my luck.

"N" revealed the third top hat, which was also empty. Finally, he lifted Ryker's hat, and inside was a mass of strange black mist. The mist surged toward Ryker, transforming into a bizarre beastly form. "N" replaced him with the body that had already been wagered.

- For one with the keen sense of a beast, isn't this incarnation a perfect match? So, this is the "best choice"!]]
  },
  AwakerStory_11351_Title = {Text = "Story: III"},
  AwakerStory_11351_UnlockDesc = {
    Text = "Affinity Level 7"
  },
  AwakerStory_11352_Content = {
    Text = "This is the Promised Land, an artistic utopia, the ultimate paradise—dance should be the dancer's home, kept in eternal purity.\n\nSo long as I burn, filth cannot taint our Church... This is my mission, my hope... Let me burn brightly, and I shall cleanse away all impurity, for everyone."
  },
  AwakerStory_11352_Title = {Text = "Story: IV"},
  AwakerStory_11352_UnlockDesc = {
    Text = "Affinity Level 9"
  },
  AwakerStory_11353_Content = {
    Text = "Shh... Don't be afraid. It's just the sound of rats decaying in the damp cellar. From the deepest abyss, a crimson desire festers. The imprisoned soul yearns for blood, just as the blind long for light and the lecherous thirst for flesh. And the way to please her is quite simple: lash out at her and humiliate her to your heart's content."
  },
  AwakerStory_11353_Title = {
    Text = "Basic Information"
  },
  AwakerStory_11353_UnlockDesc = {
    Text = "Awakener Level 1"
  },
  AwakerStory_11354_Content = {
    Text = "Until now, the oldest known human civilization was believed to have originated in Mesopotamia, a fact supported by a wealth of solid archaeological evidence.\n\nHowever, humanity is never content with the known. When facing the vast, black seas of infinity, we do not hesitate to set sail into the unknown.\n\nPerhaps this is not the first time we have been granted such warnings or hints. Theosophists once proposed a chilling hypothesis: that the cosmos is an awe-inspiring cycle, and our current world—and humanity itself—is but a transient link within it.\n\nFar too many things have perished silently in these cycles, leaving not a shred of evidence behind. This is, in fact, a mercy; some forces are so ancient and extreme that even their lingering vestiges could exert an immeasurable and devastating influence on our era.\n\nTake, for instance, the accidental discovery made by the crew of the Vigilant on the floor of the Southern Ocean. It has pushed our understanding of prehistoric civilization back by tens of thousands of years.\n\nFrom this, we have learned of a civilization—complete with its own state, monarch, and peculiar faith—that was swallowed by a global deluge and has long lain dormant beneath the waves.\n\nWere it not for the Mystia Treaty Committee's assistance in containment and censorship, human history might have been rewritten. But the world as it stands is not yet prepared for such a cataclysmic revelation."
  },
  AwakerStory_11354_Title = {Text = "Story: I"},
  AwakerStory_11354_UnlockDesc = {
    Text = "Affinity Level 3"
  },
  AwakerStory_11355_Content = {
    Text = "Casiah reached into the hat, and it was empty.\n\nCasiah reached into the Gate, and it was empty.\n\nCasiah reached into her chest, and it was empty.\n\nThe collected joy and sorrow, fear and fury, the warmth and chill of human connection, the buzz before the show began, the cheers at each dramatic twist, the whistles at the highlights, the applause at the final bow, and the hollow silence as the crowd dispersed—all slipped away from this hollow chest, leaving no trace of ever having existed.\n\nStaring into the mirror, Casiah began to mimic the audience's expressions. The wrinkles at the corners of her eyes, the flexing of her cheeks, the exact curve of her lips—everything was identical to theirs, yet utterly devoid of any true sentiment.\n\n<Italic:If only I could feel it... If only I could transcend mere mimicry... If only I could become one of them... Or, if only someone... could stay...>\nThen surely this \"void\" in her chest would finally be filled."
  },
  AwakerStory_11355_Title = {Text = "Story: IV"},
  AwakerStory_11355_UnlockDesc = {
    Text = "Affinity Level 9"
  },
  AwakerStory_11356_Content = {
    Text = "Travel info: Curious History Exploration - Luxurious 7-Day Tour to Cambrian Castle\nDate: A.F.3@2 June 18th-25th\nGuide: Thomas @2@1\nBrief itinerary:\nCome on, uncover the mystery of the most infamous haunted castle from 300 years ago—Cambrian Castle!\n\nWe're tired of reading about the seductive lady and her twenty-five attendants in old books and silent films; it's all the same—so boring!\n\nAccording to a Mythag expert who wishes to remain anonymous, there's been a new discovery in the area! @2@1 covered in thorns...\n\nCall quickly @2@1@1. This trip will be unforgettable, chills guaranteed!\n\n—Excerpt from \"Worster Tour Group Disappearance CaseFile Summary: Evidence S-145\""
  },
  AwakerStory_11356_Title = {Text = "Story: I"},
  AwakerStory_11356_UnlockDesc = {
    Text = "Awakener Level 3"
  },
  AwakerStory_11357_Content = {
    Text = "As someone at the forefront of Dissolution research, Doll has long been acutely aware of the encroaching footsteps of annihilation steadily pursuing her from behind. Moreover, she is all too familiar with the concept of Dissolution itself. \n\nThrough her relentless yet often fruitless pursuit of truth, Doll gradually comes to realize that human bodies may possess an inherent blindness—those bound to reality can never perceive the scenery of the other shore, no matter how hard they try. \n\nSo, as the black sludge dissolves the body, will it also guide the soul to the true other shore? \n\nShe sits silently alongside the ancient tablets' maxims, allowing Dissolution to erode her mind. Regardless of what lies at the end of this path, she can no longer turn back. \n\nFortunate yet unfortunate, she has wagered her very existence for the chance to enter the inner side of the world. In an instant, reality, illusion, and destruction simultaneously engulf her. \n\nIn the blink of an eye, she witnesses everything in the universe—the essence of Dissolution, the truth of the world—all that she has yearned for in life is here. \n\nAll scientific beliefs and rational convictions dissolve into bubbles, and the once-unshakable spiritual barrier crumbles abruptly. \n\nThe genius known as Doll has vanished; what remains now is merely a vessel occupied by nothingness."
  },
  AwakerStory_11357_Title = {Text = "Story: III"},
  AwakerStory_11357_UnlockDesc = {
    Text = "Affinity Level 7"
  },
  AwakerStory_11358_Content = {
    Text = [[
"In the year of A.F.3@2, the Marine Ecology Team of Mythag University discovered an oddly shaped coral reef while conducting species observations in the southern seas...

"Have found peculiar fragments; probably consist of elements wholly unspotted on Earth. Flexibility preserved in water, but hardened quickly after exposed to air. The joint research conducted by the Biology and Astronomy departments suggests that it is highly likely to be classified as unknown extraterrestrial material..."

"Awakened at A.F.3@1, awaken code-name Sanga.

The sculpting behaviour has been performed since awakening. The resulting art style, known for its bizarre surfaces and grotesque lines, is difficult to attribute to any specific genre. Though constantly unsettling its viewers, those works stay far from helping the dissolution research."]]
  },
  AwakerStory_11358_Title = {Text = "Story: I"},
  AwakerStory_11358_UnlockDesc = {
    Text = "Affinity Level 3"
  },
  AwakerStory_11359_Content = {
    Text = [[
Beheading death's cold embrace, he survived and transformed. The glitter on his blade fades. The mask of apostle conceals his savage expression.

He did revere instinctively when that miracle manifested. But no god could capture his fear, and no cult could earn his faith.

A giant should not yield to others. A warrior should not lower his head.

His past already wreathed in dust, his war still longing for final triumph. The desire for conquest run through his veins, etching into bones like a sigil bearing the bestowed power. Perhaps, one day, death will end his dominion. Perhaps, one day, he will rise to the sole supremacy.]]
  },
  AwakerStory_11359_Title = {Text = "Story: IV"},
  AwakerStory_11359_UnlockDesc = {
    Text = "Affinity Level 9"
  },
  AwakerStory_11360_Content = {
    Text = [[
Haven't you had such dreams? Suddenly inheriting a massive fortune, suddenly gaining immense power... enough to trample those who once disdained and hurt us.

Then, at the moment you wake up, faced with relentless reality, you fall deeper into despair.

But my dream is true, my fate has arrived.

Know this: you are the weak ones.

Can physical frailty and a wilting soul not uphold a noble bloodline? No, that's impossible, because the name Oren is our family's pride and symbol. Endowed with the bloodline and name, I am no longer that bullied freak; I am someone with noble blood.

So... please... stop looking at me with those suffocating eyes...]]
  },
  AwakerStory_11360_Title = {Text = "Story: IV"},
  AwakerStory_11360_UnlockDesc = {
    Text = "Affinity Level 9"
  },
  AwakerStory_11361_Content = {
    Text = "Hannah: Ms. Alva, you've been at Mythag University for quite a while. You're very popular; some girls even handed me love letters for you! Want me to read them?\n\nAlva: That's really... cough, I mean, thank you everyone? But wasn't I here to share my day?\n\nHannah: Didn't know the instructor had such a cute side! I might hide outside campus after this interview publishes, to avoid jealous girls! So, back to the point, can you share a day of the charming instructor's life?\n\nAlva: I'm afraid you'll be disappointed; my day is ordinary. I get up at 4 AM for exercises to adapt my leg to activity.\n\nAt 6 AM I go to the cafeteria. Though I don't need to eat as an Awakener, it's a habit.\n\n8-12 AM, I guide investigators in combat, sometimes extra training for Keepers. Afternoon training adjusts with the schedule, sometimes at 1 PM, sometimes at 3 PM.\n\nWeekly, I go to Nautila for prosthetic tuning. Though she forgets things, she does good work; every maintenance lessens my pain.\n\nHannah: What do you do for fun?\n\nAlva: Fun... an unfamiliar concept to me. Recently, I went to the beach with Aurita and the others; spending time with these innocent kids relaxes me. Swimming also benefits physical strength. Back when I was a recruit, my instructor—\nHannah: That's all for today! For more of Alva's stories, stay tuned for the next \"Mythag Daily Share\"!\n\n—Excerpt from Mythag Daily's \"Special Interview Column: Mythag Daily Share\""
  },
  AwakerStory_11361_Title = {Text = "Story: II"},
  AwakerStory_11361_UnlockDesc = {
    Text = "Affinity Level 5"
  },
  AwakerStory_11362_Content = {
    Text = "Before the full truth came to light, no one had ever suspected that Doll could be the true culprit behind that string of sensational incidents.\n\nAfter all, her presence on the Mythag and Dissolution front lines had always stood like a pillar of strength, a beacon atop a tower—a rock-solid source of reassurance in everyone's hearts.\n\nWhen countless shining stars of humanity's night sky were shattered and scattered by Dissolution, this once-unwavering beacon of humanity was finally, cruelly, extinguished—transformed into a shadowy agent born of the same Darkness she once opposed.\n\nTornadoes, floods, earthquakes… inefficient murder clearly didn't suit a genius's plans. With intellect undiminished by even a fraction, she retrofitted the very Silver Technology she had once taken such pride in into lethal weapons for \"moving the world,\" delivering gift after gift of Destruction to places beyond Mythag's sight.\n\nWhen she was finally captured, her puppet body could no longer be precisely controlled by her corroded mind. That face, once calm as still water, was now rife with twisted, eerie Emotes—as though merely meeting her gaze would plunge one into the abyss of Madness.\n\nEveryone unanimously chose to ignore her occasionally muddled murmurings, even though they may have truly revealed the truth of the world.\n\nFor her fate had proven once again that humanity is, in the end, a species that needs meaning to survive."
  },
  AwakerStory_11362_Title = {Text = "Story: I"},
  AwakerStory_11362_UnlockDesc = {
    Text = "Awakener Level 3"
  },
  AwakerStory_11363_Content = {
    Text = [[
Daffodil sold herself to the Silver Core Research Laboratory of Mythag University at a staggering price.

Before that, the laboratory head Doll had repeatedly expressed strong dissatisfaction with the one-way communications that only Daffodil could initiate.

But only Daffodil and a certain deceased high-ranking member of Mythag University know how such a "one-way communication" was established through a dangerous transaction.]]
  },
  AwakerStory_11363_Title = {Text = "Story: I"},
  AwakerStory_11363_UnlockDesc = {
    Text = "Affinity Level 3"
  },
  AwakerStory_11364_Content = {
    Text = "Proud, willful, self-centered... Many who have interacted with her would describe her personality as such. She seems to have always been treated like the center of the universe in her last living arrangement; perhaps it was this meticulous care that cultivated her spoiled nature.\n\n\"Hey! What are you looking at? Didn't I say that if I call you three times, you have to respond to this young lady?!\"\n\n—One must be very careful, even when reading the documents."
  },
  AwakerStory_11364_Title = {
    Text = "Basic Information"
  },
  AwakerStory_11364_UnlockDesc = {
    Text = "Awakener Level 1"
  },
  AwakerStory_11365_Content = {
    Text = "On a street corner in a port city sat a tiny exchange shop, run by a proprietor skilled in handling mysterious events.\n\nNot long after the flood, Daffodil—who was not yet known as Daffodil at the time—arrived near St. Peidro. Soon after her arrival, victims of the \"mysterious head disappearance\" began to surface throughout the harbor city.\n\nThe owner investigated, tracked it down, and after exhausting every measure to subdue it, struck a bargain with it. The shopkeeper promised it her own head upon her death, but until then, it must serve as her assistant and could no longer hunt at will.\n\nAnd so the creature, after a thousand years of wandering, began to work and live by her side.\n\nIt had once immersed itself in the memories of countless heads, tasting both fleeting joy and festering resentment. But this absurd happiness was merely a pastime to while away its prolonged existence, masking the profound, drifting loneliness.\n\nOnly while accompanying the shopkeeper did it experience genuine friendship for the very first time. It realized that infinite heads offered nothing but a hollow comfort; only true human connection could fill its perpetual void.\n\nHowever, this brief happiness lasted less than ten years. The shopkeeper, who had never once set aside her work, passed away unexpectedly.\n\nAnd so it severed her head, inheriting her appearance, shop, and name, becoming \"Daffodil.\"\n\nFrom that day forward, Daffodil embarked on a journey with her little exchange shop. She continues to claim heads as payment from those who seek her help, keeping them as private collectibles.\n\nBut she never hunted at will again.\n\nNever again."
  },
  AwakerStory_11365_Title = {Text = "Story: III"},
  AwakerStory_11365_UnlockDesc = {
    Text = "Affinity Level 7"
  },
  AwakerStory_11366_Content = {
    Text = [[
Return to her home, trace back to her origin, reunion with her lost dreamshe doesn't care how does her wish reflect in people's words. Even her body has altered to an Awakener, tides of her homeland still clamor in her soul.

The breath of sea-bottom volcanoes dissipated from her ears. The ocean's dreams writhing with ecstasies obscured from her eyes. Only her obsession with the Divine Realm still gleaming, more glorious than ever.

Mind her docility, a mere temporarily disguise. Her king's throne calls to her, like a lighthouse reaches through the aeons; her sacrifice will always be everything, like a wick's devotion to the light.]]
  },
  AwakerStory_11366_Title = {Text = "Story: IV"},
  AwakerStory_11366_UnlockDesc = {
    Text = "Affinity Level 9"
  },
  AwakerStory_11367_Content = {
    Text = "Doll is an indispensable figure at Mythag University and in the entire academic community. \n\nAmong the Awakeners managed by the school, Doll is neither the most stable in gnostic index nor the strongest in combat abilities, but she is certainly the calmest and most rational one. \n\nFor some Awakeners who were once human, the initial phase of \"being reborn\" is often accompanied by confusion, panic, and agitation. However, Doll seems unaffected by such \"growing pains.\" \n\nOn the second day after being awakened, she returned to the laboratory and compiled a technical manual that integrates outer domain knowledge and human wisdom within a year. \n\nCurrently, Doll spends half her time innovating \"silver chip technology\" and the other half \"cleaning up the mess for stupid students.\" \n\n— By the way, based on the influence of h-dim existence, Doll employed an unknown language in writing that \"Technical Manual,\" and the translation work is being orderly conducted during her leisure time"
  },
  AwakerStory_11367_Title = {Text = "Story: I"},
  AwakerStory_11367_UnlockDesc = {
    Text = "Awakener Level 3"
  },
  AwakerStory_11368_Content = {
    Text = [[
"I am the Daughter of God, and simultaneously the Bearer of God."

This is how she confirms her authority. Only by maintaining this universally admired dignity can she preserve a precarious balance. So what if it's hypocrisy? So what if it's a delusion? Who isn't living in the "present" moment?

Murphy holds the swaddling cloth, which conceals the grotesque Divine Fetus, and acts as the God's proxy, speaking one lie after another:
"He has descended." "The Divine Realm will rise." "Please wait for the next moment of Stellar Alignment."

Rather than letting others' hypocrisy fabricate an illusion, she would rather decorate this prison with her own hands to a likeness she finds acceptable. As long as the "Mother," "Companions," and "Servants" she desires are still by her side, whether it is superficial deference or insincere mystification, she accepts it and finds it sweet.

"My name is Murphy, the Princess who bore the God. Regarding Lemuria, regarding the Seafarers' long-cherished wish... you need not inquire. I have my own arrangements."]]
  },
  AwakerStory_11368_Title = {Text = "Story: IV"},
  AwakerStory_11368_UnlockDesc = {
    Text = "Affinity Level 9"
  },
  AwakerStory_11368_UnlockDesc_1 = {
    Text = "Clear Main Story Astral Reign: Chapter 4 Normal"
  },
  AwakerStory_11369_Content = {
    Text = [[
On April 2, A.F.3@2, a temple remain in the Ashdod region was vandalized.

As the only one who had university education, I, a mere visitor, was invited by the regional administrator to participate in the architectural assessment of the ruins. Haha, I should never let them know that my "university" isn't quite what it seems.

On the afternoon of April 3, I entered the center of the temple. Ancient Semitics used it as a place of worship, and their pagan belief once flourished among the pillars before lost in history.

Yet what appeared before me was a sculpture that could be mistaken by no one. I clearly knew that the folds on its clothes should indicate the texture of striped linen.

However, its both hands were broken, its head severed from the body, and its lower limbs shattered on the threshold. Mucilage covered everywhere like the trace of a sticky slug. Upon inspection, there were few peculiar scratches buried within, accompanied by a giant, webbed footprint.

The pagan belief may still circulate nearby, but a formal investigation is not urgently necessary. I will extend my stay in the Ashdod region.

Fin@1@2sen, "An account of a trip around five cities of the Philistines"]]
  },
  AwakerStory_11369_Title = {Text = "Story: I"},
  AwakerStory_11369_UnlockDesc = {
    Text = "Affinity Level 3"
  },
  AwakerStory_11370_Content = {
    Text = "It is an unspoken rule among the students: keep your distance from the library basement, the cemetery, and Leigh.\n\nThe pale and frail girl enjoys provoking others and then savoring their anger with quiet pleasure. Like the serpent of Eden, she knows precisely when to cast her whispered temptation: <Italic:Hurt me... Come on...>\nMost of the time, she is met with nothing but eye-rolls, confusion, and curses. Only once did she finally get what she wanted—Uvhash beat her up without hesitation, and even knocked out one of her teeth. He is a man utterly devoid of curiosity about others; you asked for it, you got it—simple as that.\n\nAs the warrior strode away into the distance, a smile of pure contentment bloomed on Leigh's face. The soft morning light washed over her—it was another beautiful, sunny day.\n\n<Italic:I still have plenty of teeth; take them all... Anyone, please, just take them all...>"
  },
  AwakerStory_11370_Title = {Text = "Story: II"},
  AwakerStory_11370_UnlockDesc = {
    Text = "Affinity Level 5"
  },
  AwakerStory_11371_Content = {
    Text = "\"...In the southern Constante Federation, there was told a legend of 'The Blessing Bishop.' Before the Flood, 'The Blessing Bishop' came from the Central Church, and in his devotion and kindness, established the only orphanage in the area, sheltering the many sick and displaced refugees during a devastating plague.\n\nThe plague was fierce, sparing noone from its wrath. The bishop prayed day and night, eventually receiving the Father's blessing—a life-giving tablet. He performed miracles, resurrecting the dead and healing those gravely ill from the plague, using his own flesh and blood as divine offerings. Yet regardless of his miracles, this benevolent bishop was framed as a cohort of demons, and ultimately sentenced to death by burning at the stake.\n\nCoincidentally, during the same period, there were reports of a 'Blood Heretic' in the central @2 (now near Bondos in the southern Constante Federation). According to the 'Continental Inquisition Heresy Records,' this heretic held a tablet marked with demonic symbols, performing rituals with flesh and blood, and conducting wicked ceremonies on moonless nights. The heretic was captured by the Inquisition in 107 BD,and in his sincere repentance to the Father, was also sentenced to death by burning at the stake.\n\n Undeniably, there are many similarities between 'The Blessing Bishop' and the 'Blood Heretic': The same era, same region, same use of tablets and rituals. Considering the Inquisition's strong subjectivity, it is likely they stigmatized certain individuals as heretics. If we were to believe coincidences, the legendary 'Blessing Bishop' might have indeed been real, possibly even the 'Blood Heretic' recorded by the Inquisition...\"\n\n—Excerpt from 'Our Gods: Religion and Folk Beliefs in Southern Constante Federation'"
  },
  AwakerStory_11371_Title = {Text = "Story: III"},
  AwakerStory_11371_UnlockDesc = {
    Text = "Affinity Level 7"
  },
  AwakerStory_11372_Content = {
    Text = [[
Yearning for an entity she calls "Mommy", this girl obediently follows the commands of her "Master".

Her true name lost to the world, she is now known only by the form she inhabits: a delicate white filament, reminiscent of a lily, blooming at the center of a giant black eyeball made of sludge. Hence, they named her Lily.]]
  },
  AwakerStory_11372_Title = {
    Text = "Basic Information"
  },
  AwakerStory_11372_UnlockDesc = {
    Text = "Awakener Level 1"
  },
  AwakerStory_11373_Content = {
    Text = [[
Liz is a reliable Awakener; although her attitude cannot be called "enthusiastic", she shows considerable cooperation with all school affairs.

The only concern is that, though Liz spends every night in the dance classroom, no one has seen her true dance performance.

As an excellent ballet dancer, Liz's name has appeared in several related publications. Unfortunately, due to the impact of the D-phenomenon, the information department of the awakening system could only determine that Liz had stepped onto the stage of the second theater in A.F. 29@1.

School reporter Hannah Peasley proposed gathering dance enthusiasts on campus, using their passion for dance to "open Awakener Liz's heart".

Currently, this proposal has yet to be approved by the Awakener Management Office.]]
  },
  AwakerStory_11373_Title = {Text = "Story: II"},
  AwakerStory_11373_UnlockDesc = {
    Text = "Affinity Level 5"
  },
  AwakerStory_11374_Content = {
    Text = [[
Sorel always knew she was beautiful, and in her heart, she regarded this beauty as a gift from heaven.

As long as she pleads with tearful eyes, people will melt with pity; a hint of vulnerability was all it took for her childhood playmates to take her side unconditionally.

However, beauty was worthless in the face of true power.

When her own parents sought to trade her to nobility for their own future, Sorel's tears tasted the bitterness of failure for the very first time.

Is there anyone who can help her? Could anyone rescue her from this ignorant and backward fate?

Is there anything, anywhere, that can transform her beauty into a real weapon?

As Sorel sobbed with her face buried in her hands, the messenger capable of stirring the currents of fate manifested before her.]]
  },
  AwakerStory_11374_Title = {Text = "Story: III"},
  AwakerStory_11374_UnlockDesc = {
    Text = "Affinity Level 7"
  },
  AwakerStory_11375_Content = {
    Text = "— How can this not be his fault? What he has done is far from enough.\n\nWith such extreme self-blame, Ogier executes his tasks at twice the frequency of other Awakeners, burying \"Death\" under universally praised \"Virtue\".\n\nThe excessive work and the words of gratitude from young Investigators seem to wash away the pain etched into the Soul.\n\nChronic ailments are pushed into the Shadows of the heart, emitting a rotting smell, secretly leading the knight towards the deep black mire.\n\n\"Sorry? Hello?\"\n\nSomeone came to Ogier with a ray of sunshine, or a gust of wind.\n\n\"Senior said Ogier will join me and Ramona to carry out my initial Investigation task, right?\"\n\nHe couldn't protect the princess for a second time, but Heaven gave him another chance to protect the \"Keeper\".\n\n\"My name is Ogier, and it is an honor to form a Contract with you. I will guard your Life with my Soul. Today's vow will be remembered forever.\""
  },
  AwakerStory_11375_Title = {Text = "Story: IV"},
  AwakerStory_11375_UnlockDesc = {
    Text = "Affinity Level 9"
  },
  AwakerStory_11376_Content = {
    Text = "\"Tired of the mundane parks? Bored with dull animal exhibitions? Then come to Casiah's Magical Carnival! For kids who love animals, there are tenor-singing lions, ballet-dancing flamingos, acrobatic elephants, and the world's one and only donkey tamer! For couples looking to rekindle the spark, try our unique Live-Horse Carousel for a rare romantic experience! And for the brave souls who crave genuine thrills in their lives, we dare you to challenge the Mirror Maze, hand-designed by the carnival's very own mistress! If you manage to take away those 41 mischievous visitors who never came out, you can win great prizes!\n\nBesides these exclusive entertainment facilities, Magician Casiah will usher you into a spectacular world of revelry, featuring sawing-in-half illusions, human vanishings, extreme escapes, and more magic! Lucky audience members may even be invited on stage to experience Master Casiah's exquisitely refined cutting techniques up close and personal. Guaranteed to shatter your perception of reality and render your ordinary daily life utterly flavorless! And best of all? Every last bit of it is absolutely free—FREE! Your joy is all the reward Master Casiah could ever ask for!\n\nTo all at the Mythag—Master Casiah will be waiting for you this weekend on the open ground behind the cafeteria. Don't you dare miss it!\n\nNote: Once entering the carnival, attendees must fully experience it; mid-way exits are not allowed. Those with low stress tolerance or fragile mental and cardiac conditions should enter with extreme caution.\n\nThe carnival is not responsible for any symptoms such as loss of appetite, missing limbs, lost eyes, or abdominal ruptures that occur afterward.\"\n\n—<Italic:Grand Opening: Master Casiah’s Magical Carnival!>"
  },
  AwakerStory_11376_Title = {Text = "Story: II"},
  AwakerStory_11376_UnlockDesc = {
    Text = "Affinity Level 5"
  },
  AwakerStory_11377_Content = {
    Text = "No one could point to the exact moment the \"salon\" wove itself into the upper crust of Londinium.\n\nIn this mysterious salon, one won the chance to have a master paint their portrait; another was granted a private supper with the Prime Minister; and yet another even received a promise from the Queen herself.\n\nThe host, the venue, the time—all remain a mystery. People only know that everyone can obtain what they desire most in the salon.\n\nYet none can say what it takes to please the hostess and earn an invitation.\n\nEven Lord Dexter, famous for his social charm, was flatly turned away.\n\n\"Our apologies, sir. The hostess currently prefers the company of artists.\"\n\n\"The nobility? Please await a future invitation.\""
  },
  AwakerStory_11377_Title = {Text = "Story: I"},
  AwakerStory_11377_UnlockDesc = {
    Text = "Affinity Level 6"
  },
  AwakerStory_11378_Content = {
    Text = "The lady who deigned to lower herself took her hand, promising to give her all the love in the world.\n\nShe believed in the lady's gentleness and the master's indulgence, trusted every smile and every hug, unaware that in their eyes, she was merely a pet—something to be discarded the moment it posed any threat.\n\nThey were the ones who cast her into a cage, shattering her trust to pieces. But neither the warden's whip nor the torment from her own people hurt as much as the betrayal from her loved ones.\n\nHate, such hate! She hated them for using lies to win her genuine heart, hated them for using her life to create this painful farce. If trusting others led to this, then she would forever rely on no one but herself.\n\nHer trust is reserved for herself alone."
  },
  AwakerStory_11378_Title = {Text = "Story: IV"},
  AwakerStory_11378_UnlockDesc = {
    Text = "Affinity Level 9"
  },
  AwakerStory_123300_Content = {
    Text = "One day, she will return to her own world.\n\nBut before that, she wants to see the conclusion of this world—\n\nWill the one known as the \"Keeper\" be consumed by this chaotic and terrifying world, or will they shine brightly, bringing true redemption and light to this crumbling world?\n\nThis is a mystery, a challenge, a gamble.\n\nAnd she wants to know the answer."
  },
  AwakerStory_123300_Title = {Text = "Story: IV"},
  AwakerStory_123300_UnlockDesc = {
    Text = "Affinity Level 9"
  },
  AwakerStory_123301_Content = {
    Text = "On January 17, A.F.3, after receiving the notification of the review meeting regarding the human sacrifice held by the Sect of Astral Dawn in region @4, I immediately set out to investigate the area.\n\nBy the time I arrived, it was already evening, and the area was shrouded in thick fog for unknown reasons, making visibility nearly impossible.\n\nI did not carry any devices to disperse the fog, but considering the seriousness of the situation, I rushed into the mist anyway. If time could rewind, I would never have made such a reckless move, because, because there were terrifying @2 in the fog...\n\nWhen those indescribable, twisted beings attacked me at inhuman speed, I couldn't react at all. My body went rigid, unable to move.\n\nBut ultimately, I did not die. That girl, the enigmatic girl from the fog, saved me.\n\nShe may have shouted \"Tornado\"? I didn't catch it clearly; I only saw an axe flying out of the fog, cleaving the head of that terrifying creature. Then the girl took the axe and slung it over her shoulder.\n\n\"It's very dangerous in the fog; if you don't want to die, leave this place.\"\n\nAs she said this, her expression was smiling, a sweet smile of a young girl, but for some reason, I found that smile even more chilling than the monsters in the fog.\n\nA human, or rather something with a human form, traversing through the mist filled with monsters, yet remaining unscathed while maintaining that \"sweet\" smile...\n\nIn fear, I finally got up and screamed, distancing myself from her.\n\nSoon, the thick fog occupied my line of sight, and I fell into a state where I could see nothing again. But her laughter, her innocent, youthful laughter, kept echoing in the fog.\n\n— \"File: Investigation of the Sect of Astral Dawn in Region @4\""
  },
  AwakerStory_123301_Title = {Text = "Story: I"},
  AwakerStory_123301_UnlockDesc = {
    Text = "Affinity Level 3"
  },
  AwakerStory_123302_Content = {
    Text = "In the eyes of most students, Mouchette is definitely the most suitable person to be friends with. She always wears a smile, enthusiastically engages in conversations, and is unlikely to refuse any requests made to her, which is why she often gets invited to go shopping, chat, or eat.\n\nBut only a few know her true nature. In front of these people, she no longer has to pretend to be friendly or hide her contempt for rules and order.\n\n\"What friends? Just a way to pass the time out of boredom. If I don't do this, I'll be seen as a problem student and taken to see Principal Kellett for questioning—what a hassle.\""
  },
  AwakerStory_123302_Title = {Text = "Story: II"},
  AwakerStory_123302_UnlockDesc = {
    Text = "Affinity Level 5"
  },
  AwakerStory_123303_Content = {
    Text = "Her life seemed to always be full of surprises: first, she encountered the rampant unknown fog, and then she was inexplicably summoned to another world.\n\nWhen the summoning ritual was completed and she first set foot on the land of this other world, Mouchette saw the familiar thick fog, and within it, the screams of people.\n\nThose were the sacrifices fleeing from the cultists.\n\nSacrifices? Cultists? What... exciting and fresh vocabulary.\n\nThis represented a new world, running a jungle game of survival of the fittest, and coincidentally, she had never been the weak one.\n\nCalmly, she hunted the cultists in the fog, happily even humming a tune.\n\n\"One by one, and again... in the unknown fog, I vent freely ♪\"\n\n\"Knock open your skull, delve into your brain, let's pass the time in this chase ♪\"\n\nAmidst this casual humming, Mouchette sensed the hollow hunger within her—\nthis mad world could not fill the void in her heart, but it could alleviate her soul's hunger for destruction and madness."
  },
  AwakerStory_123303_Title = {Text = "Story: III"},
  AwakerStory_123303_UnlockDesc = {
    Text = "Affinity Level 7"
  },
  AwakerStory_123304_Content = {
    Text = "Strictly speaking, she does not belong to this world on the brink of collapse, but she appreciates it.\n\nShe admires the magnificent spectacle of this world burning, appreciates the suffering and breakdown of these humans in despair.\n\nFaith is dead, society has come to a halt, morals have crumbled, and nature no longer needs to disguise itself as a boring \"normal person\" —\nshe can finally unleash the beast within her and reveal her true self, becoming her authentic self."
  },
  AwakerStory_123304_Title = {
    Text = "Basic Information"
  },
  AwakerStory_123304_UnlockDesc = {
    Text = "Awakener has reached level 1"
  },
  AwakerStory_126929_Content = {
    Text = "Xu appeared on campus just as naturally as she once drifted through palaces, royal tents, and various societies in the Far East. No one can say for certain when she first appeared.\n\nTo all who meet her, she feels instinctively familiar—a long-lost friend, or perhaps a cherished lover—even if they have never shared a single moment of their lives.\n\nOnly a rare few among the Awakeners maintain a preternatural wariness of her. Or, more accurately, only those of exceptional power can detect the anomaly: Xu, clinging and pervasive like a mist, seeping into their memories.\n\n The Mythag Administration once debated whether she required strict containment, even considering the development of specialized countermeasures. Yet, Xu dissolved these anxieties with a series of clandestine deals and a single promise:\n\n\"My intentions do not lie with these little ones.\""
  },
  AwakerStory_126929_Title = {Text = "Story: II"},
  AwakerStory_126929_UnlockDesc = {
    Text = "Affinity Level 5"
  },
  AwakerStory_126930_Content = {
    Text = "In A.F. @16@1, a cargo ship with no traceable voyage records or authorized paperwork silently docked at the Londinium Freight Harbor.\n\nThe vessel was later confirmed to have originated from a port in the ancient Panlong Empire of the Far East. On the night of its arrival, harbor workers and nearby residents reported a collective dream of an Eastern woman with raven hair, obsidian eyes, and skin like ivory.\n\nWitnesses described her as both \"fascinating\" and \"hauntingly familiar.\" Notably, several male witnesses exhibited catatonic symptoms while providing their accounts.\n\nMythag's Investigators searched the ship immediately. Strangely, despite pervasive sounds of giggling and high-level Gnostic Responses, no trace of a Silver Core was initially found.\n\nThe following day, Lord Dexter entered the hold. Inside a ceramic vase that had already been searched multiple times, he discovered a Silver Core enveloped in a thin, clinging mist. As of A.F. 314, this Silver Core was deemed \"unawakenable\" by all known methods.\n\nIt was not until the arrival of the current Keeper, @3, that the Silver Core awakened spontaneously. The resulting entity identifies herself as \"Xu\" and has requested a permanent link with @3.\n\n—Excerpt from \"Mythag University Silver Core Storage Records"
  },
  AwakerStory_126930_Title = {Text = "Story: I"},
  AwakerStory_126930_UnlockDesc = {
    Text = "Affinity Level 3"
  },
  AwakerStory_126931_Content = {
    Text = [[
Have you ever felt the world grow so deathly quiet that you felt the urge to shatter something, just to hear the sound?

Lust is the silver vase she hurls; the prey startled by its chime... they will slaughter for love and be slaughtered by love, until their spirit is bled dry and only a hollow shell remains.

Then, those drained husks will offer her ever greater dominion, staining everything in sight with a bloody, delicious chaos.

A chaos that never ends.]]
  },
  AwakerStory_126931_Title = {Text = "Story: IV"},
  AwakerStory_126931_UnlockDesc = {
    Text = "Affinity Level 9"
  },
  AwakerStory_126932_Content = {
    Text = "...To offer sacrifice where none is due is named Profane Rites. It is a delusion that devours the wealth of the people, persisting despite every decree of prohibition.\n\nThe coastal folk are steeped in the habit of venerating false gods, driven by a passion for raising rustic shrines and unhallowed altars. Vast fortunes are squandered while fields and looms lie fallow, yet the hamlets remain blind to the rot within. Time and again, the magistrates raze these dens to the ground, only for them to sprout anew the moment the garrison withdraws.\n\nMost grievous are the foreign vagabonds. Settling among our villages, they have taken their own sacred icons and turned them upside down, distorting them to resemble the sign for a \"Well\"—the character \"井\".\n\nThe deities enshrined therein—both the masters and their attendants—possess verifiable histories; they are largely women who met with violent or unjust ends. In the beginning, the flock consisted of mere peasant women, stage-players, and common streetwalkers.\n\nBut soon, wife brings husband, mother brings son, and the prostitute brings her patron. Having swollen in rank, they form shadow factions for private gain. It has become a dark wonder to see entire clusters of villages rally behind a single figure—some to infiltrate the halls of officialdom, others to raise private militias to wage war upon their neighbors.\n\n@4@4@3@2\nThe following handwriting is illegible, except for several lines of very neat handwriting in @3. Translated by the Linguistics Department, the text reads:\n\n<Italic:\"Shameless old wretch. His views are so warped, his prose so utterly tedious. I was bored, so I raised a few crickets to watch them fight—and still, he must wag his tongue and prattle on about it...\"\n\n<Bold:\"It's none of your damn business.\">>\n\n—Excerpt from a handwritten copy of <Italic:Wild Fox Study Gazetter>."
  },
  AwakerStory_126932_Title = {Text = "Story: III"},
  AwakerStory_126932_UnlockDesc = {
    Text = "Affinity Level 7"
  },
  AwakerStory_126933_Content = {
    Text = "Elegant, alluring—an Eastern \"deity\" of fatal charm.\n\nLegend has it that when she lowers her fan, you will see the face of your most beloved reflected beneath.\n\nYet legends are merely legends. Pray that her gaze never falls upon you. Once she seeps into your memories like a pervasive night mist, nothing will remain of your mind but a delirious, hollow obsession."
  },
  AwakerStory_126933_Title = {
    Text = "Basic Information"
  },
  AwakerStory_126933_UnlockDesc = {
    Text = "Awakener Level 1"
  },
  AwakerStory_129596_Content = {
    Text = "The condition of Awakener Vortice is highly irregular. In an unrestrained state, her abilities do not activate at her own will. Irregular energy fields resembling the Moskstraumen vortex spontaneously form around her, pulverizing anything within range.\n\nPhysical contact with water-containing objects or people (including blood and other bodily fluids) accelerates field formation at the point of contact. Given both the involuntary trigger and the manic state she endured early in her Awakening, she was classified as \"Extreme Danger.\"\n\nTo address this, the Awakener Department collaborated with the Physics and Chemistry Departments to develop \"Vorticesteel\"—a specialized synthetic alloy capable of withstanding her destructive power. This metal was fashioned into a muzzle and restraints for her to wear all the times.\n\nVortice's mental state began to stabilize after Researcher Caldwell's 11th \"O-1841 Contact Experiment.\" During this trial, Vortice successfully internalized Moskstraumen's influence, significantly reducing the threat to her surroundings.\n\nHowever, she cannot maintain this state without the \"Vorticesteel\" gear. Only when properly restrained can she stably contain Moskstraumen's effects within her core and channel its power for combat.\n\nUpon regaining sanity, Vortice has revealed a cheerful disposition and an unexplained fondness for the Awakener Nautila. This likely stems from a shared experience tied to their spiritual origins.\n\n—Excerpt from <Italic:Awakener Profile: Vortice>"
  },
  AwakerStory_129596_Title = {Text = "Story: II"},
  AwakerStory_129596_UnlockDesc = {
    Text = "Affinity Level 5"
  },
  AwakerStory_129597_Content = {
    Text = [[
Even if she could speak in complete sentences, she couldn't tell you where she was born. In truth, regardless of which "home" you mean, all she can recall now is blinding white sand, dense jungle, and a boundless sea.

But if you ask her where home is, she will tell you in broken phrases and passionate gestures: Home is on the sea, drifting wherever the currents take it.

Long-time isolation kept her from understanding loneliness. Yet on that ship, she first knew the warmth of a family and the bond of friendship: She shared grilled fish and iridescent shells with her companion whose name was derived from Nautilus, sharing dreams of land, of voyage, of adventure. And in the end, they shared a death swallowed by black waves and the whirlpool.]]
  },
  AwakerStory_129597_Title = {Text = "Story: III"},
  AwakerStory_129597_UnlockDesc = {
    Text = "Affinity Level 7"
  },
  AwakerStory_129598_Content = {
    Text = "The North Atlantic whirlpool Moskstraumen was first observed in AF 1■■. Over the following centuries, it steadily grew in size. By AF 29■, Moskstraumen had evolved into a massive whirlpool roughly 260–300 feet (80–90 meters) in diameter, with currents stretching about 5 miles (8 kilometers) wide.\n\nBeyond the powerful suction of the currents and devastating effects (claiming both marine life and fishing vessels in the vicinity), a greater threat lurked beneath Moskstraumen—a D-Rift. After prolonged observation and research conducted by Academy members, it was confirmed that the formation of Moskstraumen was directly linked to the D-Rift beneath it. In 1898, a formal operation was launched to purge it.\n\nWithin the D-Rift, the Academy recovered vast quantities of biological remains and shipwreck debris, along with a Silver Core later designated O-1841.\n\n—Excerpt from <Italic:The Moskstraumen Incident Records>"
  },
  AwakerStory_129598_Title = {Text = "Story: I"},
  AwakerStory_129598_UnlockDesc = {
    Text = "Awakener Level 3"
  },
  AwakerStory_129599_Content = {
    Text = "Language barriers? Not a problem—gestures work just fine. Uncontrollable power? At this school, that's par for the course. A few days in the lab usually resolve the issue.\n\nWith her beaming smile and a personality so blunt it borders on feral, Vortice quickly wins over the other Awakeners. Sure, she often wreaks havoc because she forgets what she's capable of (spare a thought for that fountain, rebuilt three times by now). But come on—she doesn't mean it!\n\n...Probably."
  },
  AwakerStory_129599_Title = {
    Text = "Basic Information"
  },
  AwakerStory_129599_UnlockDesc = {
    Text = "Awakener Level 1"
  },
  AwakerStory_129600_Content = {
    Text = "Out on the boundless ocean, in the salty breeze, the ship gave her a family and friends beyond blood ties before the torrent swallowed everything. For the first time, she truly understood what loneliness was, and she never wanted to feel it again.\n\nYet for her best friend, her little family, she was willing to return to that pitch-black silence.\n\nAfter the darkness covered everything, she was reborn in a new form. Sure, this new life comes with inconveniences—she keeps forgetting how destructive her power is—but the chance to make more friends still fills her with pure joy.\n\nOf course, it would be even better if her best friend could remember the stories they once shared.\n\n\"Even better than better—super-duper better!\""
  },
  AwakerStory_129600_Title = {Text = "Story: IV"},
  AwakerStory_129600_UnlockDesc = {
    Text = "Affinity Level 9"
  },
  AwakerStory_134315_Content = {
    Text = "The weaver ensnared by her own web; the playwright and eternal spectator of the Theater of Fate. \n\nThreads cascade from Arachne's fingertips, twining into curtains, scripts, and cages—each strand spun by her own hand, only to shroud her in an inescapable cocoon. \n\nThe auditorium remains forever vacant, with none but herself to gaze upon the solitary performance onstage—a drama repeating without end, a play that knows no final curtain. She is the phantom haunting the theater, and the very incarnation of Fate itself."
  },
  AwakerStory_134315_Title = {
    Text = "Basic Information"
  },
  AwakerStory_134315_UnlockDesc = {
    Text = "Awakener Level 1"
  },
  AwakerStory_134316_Content = {
    Text = "At first, Arachne did not know she could see Fate.\n\nThe world, like everyone and everything around her, was blurred, clamorous, and ruled by chance.\n\nAt the age of two, she spoke her very first word.\n\nIt was not \"Mama,\" nor was it \"Papa.\" Instead, standing beneath the porch, she whispered a single \"Goodbye\" to the old family butler.\n\nThat night, the butler died of a heart attack. Clutching the pocketwatch he had left behind, she wept herself to sleep outside the lodge. She did not yet understand death or destiny, but she had already tasted the bitter sting of a future revealed too soon.\n\nAt five, amidst the flushed faces and raucous cheers of banquet guests, she mimicked her mother, rising on tiptoe for a clumsy waltz.\n\nHer red dancing shoes were as vivid as blood—an omen in plain sight. When she tripped during a turn, no one noticed the flash of a vision in her eyes, as if the fall itself had been destined.\n\nOn her seventh birthday, her father gifted her a spinning wheel named \"Moirae,\" after the three Goddesses of Fate. She ran through the woods, her laughter bright and unguarded—until she tripped, and heard the crack: the spinning wheel was broken.\n\nShe knelt among the fallen leaves, tracing the fracture with her fingers, and she suddenly saw it: countless threads surging from the break, coiling around her fingertips and stretching into the invisible distance.\n\nThen came the \"firsts\"—her first time in an opera house, her first true friend, the first time she buried a beloved dog...\n\nEvery \"first\" was haunted by a silent final act flashing before her eyes. She began to understand: every opening scene already carried the shape of its finale.\n\nFrom then on, her gaze could no longer rest on surfaces. Human faces became mere veils, through which she could peer at the destinies churning beneath. She knew who would wither at the end of summer, who would hang themselves on the eve of their wedding, and whose child would bury them ten years hence. Surprise died; anticipation withered. \n\nThe \"future\" was nothing more than an obituary she had opened ahead of time.\n\nShe tried, at first, to warn those around her of the misfortunes to come. But every time the words left her lips, they only hastened the prophecy's fulfillment.\n\nSeeing the terror and recoil in their eyes, she finally grasped the truth: To foresee is not to forestall.\n\nThe Web of Fate was already woven. Her \"foresight\" was merely a stray beam of light slipping through the mesh—it illuminated the end, but was powerless to alter the weave.\n\nAnd so, she took up the spinning wheel named \"Moirae\" again.\n\nThe break had been mended, but the scar remained. Day after day she spun, and her gift for fate merged itself into the wheel in ways she could not explain.\n\nFrom that moment, the destinies of all flowed and intertwined through her fingers, woven into a colossal web spanning space and time.\n\nImperceptibly, she too was ensnared within this eternal web. She bore witness to laughter and grief beyond counting; infinite turning points, infinite possibilities, each one dragging its foredoomed destruction to the stage again and again...\n\nYet Arachne would not stop—not to weave, but to sustain. Should she cease, the entire Web of Fate might unravel, dragging countless lives into nothingness along with it. But she also saw that when the web was finally complete, Its awakening would bring devastation nothing could avert...\n\nShe is the weaver and the captive, the spectator and the prisoner, the playwright and the player.\n\nIs it a blessing or a curse to see the ends of others?\n\nArachne stopped asking long ago."
  },
  AwakerStory_134316_Title = {Text = "Story: III"},
  AwakerStory_134316_UnlockDesc = {
    Text = "Affinity Level 7"
  },
  AwakerStory_134317_Content = {
    Text = "The curtain had not yet fully risen when the stage lights cascaded down like a relentless tide.\n\nThe audience of Mythag held their breath, waiting for the hero of fate to take the stage.\n\nThe stage was small—so small it could barely accommodate the heavy tread of Oedipus. Yet, as the boy in the school uniform raised his hand, his voice pierced the silence of that modest stage, his opening line falling like a divine oracle: <Italic:\"It is I, the wretched man, doomed to slay my father and wed my mother.\">\n...\n\n<Italic:\"What law of the mighty gods have I transgressed?\n\n Why look to the heavens any more, tormented as I am?\n\n Whom to call, what comrades now? Just think, my reverence only brands me for irreverence!\" >\n\nSo questioned the young Antigone, challenging the injustice of divine law.\n\n...\n\nIn the castle of Denmark, Hamlet paced in contemplation. <Italic:\"To be, or not to be, that is the question: Whether 'tis nobler in the mind to suffer the slings and arrows of outrageous fortune, or to take arms against a sea of troubles, and by opposing end them?\">\n...\n\nBefore the high bench, John Proctor slowly lifted his head and declared his answer: <Italic:\"Because I am not worth the dust on the feet of them that hang! How may I live without my name?\">\n...\n\nThose words concerning fate had coalesced into today’s performance.\n\nArachne stood in the wings, her fingers digging unconsciously into her palms.\n\nThe tears shed in empathy for the characters, the thunderous applause at the final curtain call...\n\nAs she took in the myriad of faces in the audience, she suddenly felt that her heart—whose beating she had long ceased to regard—had finally found its rhythm.\n\nAt this very moment, her voice, her very existence, was etched into the vast current of fate. She was no longer a mere witness to destinies; she was now the unfolding lines of a brand-new script. Audience, performer, playwright—their fates had become inextricably bound through this living drama...\n\nThe triumph of the heart, it turned out, was this quiet—and this deafening."
  },
  AwakerStory_134317_Title = {Text = "Story: II"},
  AwakerStory_134317_UnlockDesc = {
    Text = "Affinity Level 5"
  },
  AwakerStory_134318_Content = {
    Text = "As the Weaver of the Web of Fate, Arachne governed the threads of countless lives, with past and future flowing through her hands. Yet, she harbored a hobby that bordered on the frivolous. \n\nShe loved the theater. Not for the twisting plot or the well-turned phrase: those were already etched into her mind. As the creator of the script, she knew every turn of the story and every line of the actors by heart. \n\nYet, time and again, she stepped into the theater. \n\nWhat she truly craved was the immersive sense of \"presence\"—the feeling of truly being there. \n\nWhen the curtain rises and the audience sinks into darkness, the stage becomes the only true world. In that moment, time is no longer a river running in a single direction, but an enactment within a confined space—past, present, and future overlap here. Everything ceases to be a script upon a page and becomes a tremor of life unfolding in the living present. \n\nAnd she, at last, is no longer the exile gazing at the threads she can never touch. \n\nInside the theater, she can briefly seal away her memories. She can step onto the stage as the girl gasping out her final words, or sit among the crowd, granting the actors their freedom. Casting off the prophet’s burden, she allows herself to simply tremble, weep, and hold her breath at every stirring pulse of the performance. Not as a seer, but as a living soul—adopting the posture of the ignorant, breathing in sync with the characters, shattered by a single line. Even knowing the end is written, even knowing the tragedy is foreordained. This illusion allows her a fleeting escape from her sentence as an eternal spectator. \n\nNo longer exiled from fate, but welcomed into it—even for a single instant, even as a phantom. \n\nThis small indulgence was already the most luxurious grace fate could bestow upon Arachne."
  },
  AwakerStory_134318_Title = {Text = "Story: IV"},
  AwakerStory_134318_UnlockDesc = {
    Text = "Affinity Level 9"
  },
  AwakerStory_134319_Content = {
    Text = "In the late autumn of A.F. 3@7, I traveled to the \"Theater of Fate\" in the old district to audition for a mezzo-soprano position.\t\n\nI arrived at 4:17 PM. The sky was gloomy, yet no rain fell. The main entrance was unlocked, and the auditorium stood empty; there was no sign of any interviewers.\t\n\nYet at the center of the stage, a puppet show was unfolding—there was no puppeteer, no music, only several pale humanoid marionettes dancing in silence. Their movements were unnervingly precise, and the faint clicking of their joints as they turned was spine-chilling. As for the strings... those threads descending from the dome seemed alive; they trembled slightly, tightening and slackening as if keeping time with an invisible rhythm.\t\n\nJust as I turned to leave, a woman’s voice drifted down from Box Five.\t\n\n<Italic:\"Welcome, Christine.\">\n\nThe voice was neither young nor old; it sounded like an echo seeping through dust-laden silk curtains sealed for centuries—eerie and terrifying.\t\n\nA cold shiver ran through me. I hadn't even introduced myself; how did she know my name? And these puppets...\t\n\nI bolted for the exit, but just as my hand reached for the handle, countless spiders swarmed from the darkness. Their eyes glimmered with ghostly light as they spewed out silvery threads, attempting to block my escape. More horrifying still, the spiders began to speak in human voices, chanting over and over: <Italic:\"Sing, my angel... sing for me...\">\n\nI screamed. I tore at the webs. I ran with all my might. Somehow, I managed to escape.\n\n...\n\nSince then, I could not bear the thought of any gaze cast down from VIP Box Five, and so I requested that the opera house have the box sealed.\t\n\nAnd yet... now, whenever I stand beneath the spotlight and sing, I feel the faint tug of strings at the tips of my brow.\t\n\nHave I, too, become a puppet manipulated by invisible strings? I dare not think on it further.\n\n—Excerpt from <Italic:The Memoirs of Christine, the Singer>"
  },
  AwakerStory_134319_Title = {Text = "Story: I"},
  AwakerStory_134319_UnlockDesc = {
    Text = "Affinity Level 3"
  },
  AwakerStory_139857_Content = {
    Text = [[
When all things are eroded by twisted flesh, when the everyday life is overturned, a dandelion drifts down upon this wasteland amid the keening noise. 

Reach out your hand. Take hold of her. Love will break through the surface, and anchor you to the one you love once more.]]
  },
  AwakerStory_139857_Title = {
    Text = "Basic Information"
  },
  AwakerStory_139857_UnlockDesc = {
    Text = "Awakener Level 1"
  },
  AwakerStory_139858_Content = {
    Text = "Like what is yet to come but has not yet come to pass. Like what is held in the heart and will never be forgotten.\n\nNo matter what form they take, no matter what shape the world assumes, the two beings—utterly different, yet utterly alike—will always arrive at the same answer.\n\n<Italic:\"There is someone we want to see again.\"\n\n\"We will stop at nothing to find them... and the world where we can stay by their side.\"\n\n\"If the path there has no end, then we will spend our whole lives walking it. A lifetime measured in searching.\"\n\n>\nPerhaps this is why, amid the screeching, ugly blobs of flesh, a brilliant Silver Core fell into the Keeper's palm."
  },
  AwakerStory_139858_Title = {Text = "Story: I"},
  AwakerStory_139858_UnlockDesc = {
    Text = "Awakener Level 3"
  },
  AwakerStory_139859_Content = {
    Text = "What exactly is Saya? The key to that answer lies somewhere far beyond reach.\n\n<Italic:\"The creature known as Saya manifested in this universe by no coincidence. It is the result of an instinct hardwired into her biology. What that instinct points toward is the ultimate purpose of all life: reproduction. She and her kind are capable of crossing the walls between dimensions, scattering their seeds across the void...\"\n\n\"...It is theorized that Saya, as an individual, may be an exception even among her own kind. Humanity is a species that has used its intellect to override its instincts. Could that same flaw have been inherited by Saya? In the course of absorbing human ways, the contradictions between emotion and instinct may have dismantled Saya's reproductive drive...\"\n\n\"—One day, the blessing of what is called love will find her. The white-hot agape will burn within her, and she will be free to wander the world as her true self, restored to her former radiance.\">\n\nShould we judge her by morality? Or by the authenticity of her love?\n\nPerhaps none of it has an answer. Carrying with her the unanswerable questions of another world, Saya arrived in this universe by accident, where none of <Italic:that> has happened yet. Led by the answers living in her memories, she moves forward, toward the far shore of what she has forgotten.\n\nShe waits for the day the dandelion blooms."
  },
  AwakerStory_139859_Title = {Text = "Story: III"},
  AwakerStory_139859_UnlockDesc = {
    Text = "Affinity Level 7"
  },
  AwakerStory_139860_Content = {
    Text = "Saya quickly became a well-liked student. Exceptional capacity for learning and a hunger for knowledge that never seemed to be sated—in Mythag, an Awakener with these qualities was rarer, even, than her unusual state of being.\n\nTo everyone's surprise, Saya took a peculiar interest in Ramona. Perhaps it's the bond between Ramona and the Keeper, or perhaps it's the special relationship between Ramona and Dexter—father and daughter, in their own strange way.\n\nGiven that Saya's understanding of morality diverges entirely from that of humans, the Academic Affairs Office once offered Ramona special security measures, but she refused.\n\nWhat the two of them usually talks about, no one knows. But very occasionally, on some warm afternoon, the gentle wind moving across the lawn would join their long, private conversations."
  },
  AwakerStory_139860_Title = {Text = "Story: II"},
  AwakerStory_139860_UnlockDesc = {
    Text = "Affinity Level 5"
  },
  AwakerStory_139861_Content = {
    Text = "She is of a species furthest from humanity—and yet, in learning how to become human, she has grown to resemble them even in the places where she contradicts her own nature.\n\nWithout love, the world she was meant to create would mean nothing.\n\nWith love, the only world worth creating is one where she could stay with her beloved.\n\nNothing more terrifying. Nothing more cruel. Nothing more innocent. Nothing more radiant."
  },
  AwakerStory_139861_Title = {Text = "Story: IV"},
  AwakerStory_139861_UnlockDesc = {
    Text = "Affinity Level 9"
  },
  AwakerStory_142869_Content = {
    Text = "Pontos spent a long time tracing the cause of Leisha’s death. She had endured far too many grueling battles and claimed far too many glorious victories—perhaps by poison, perhaps by some obscure sorcery; surely there had to be a reason, a reason for her to fall before such a feeble sea monster.\nIt was only much, much later, when a single strand of silver appeared in the hair of a human companion who had never joined Ebwynnos, that the truth finally dawned on him.\nThe waning stamina, the slowing responses, the unspoken but palpable longing for a peaceful, settled life... it was all so familiar.\nAnd all at once, Pontos understood the name of the enemy that had eluded him all this time: \"Aging.\"\nIt's the reason for Leisha's seclusion, her defeat, and the ruin of everything he might have lived for—it was something so commonplace, yet utterly inexorable.\nBut it mattered no longer. His own destruction had come early, and the power he gained in exchange was more than satisfactory.\nNo matter what unfathomable entity he must serve, whatever the price he must pay, the ravages of time shall never befall Ebwynnos again."
  },
  AwakerStory_142869_Title = {Text = "Story: III"},
  AwakerStory_142869_UnlockDesc = {
    Text = "Affinity Level 7"
  },
  AwakerStory_142870_Content = {
    Text = "<Italic:\"Is it that you won't allow aging—or that you won't allow anything beyond your control?\">\nHe did not answer, nor did he need to.\nThe abyss had chosen him long before the disaster struck, for his unspoken obsessions aligned perfectly with the abyss itself.\nObedience, companionship, and stasis... he was as inescapable as the abyss: suffocating all things, yet preserving them for eternity."
  },
  AwakerStory_142870_Title = {Text = "Story: IV"},
  AwakerStory_142870_UnlockDesc = {
    Text = "Affinity Level 9"
  },
  AwakerStory_142871_Content = {
    Text = "Most faculty and students at Mythag are more than happy to seek Pontos’s aid during field missions, and he never hesitates to lend a helping hand.\nGenerous, genial, and dependable—even though he is clearly at serious odds with certain members of Mythag, this Awakener leaves a staggeringly positive first impression.\nHowever, while Pontos has agreed with Mythag to stop expanding the \"population\" of Ebwynnos, a flood of migration applications have poured into the Administration Office following several field operations that ended in \"unconventional ways.\"\nWhile Sylvia conducts group counseling for the applicants, the administration has hastily added two new field regulations:\n1. Except in extreme emergencies, seeking aid from Pontos is strictly prohibited.\n2. Except in extreme circumstances, entry into Ebwynnos is strictly prohibited."
  },
  AwakerStory_142871_Title = {Text = "Story: II"},
  AwakerStory_142871_UnlockDesc = {
    Text = "Affinity Level 5"
  },
  AwakerStory_142872_Content = {
    Text = "The heroic epic destined to soar across the night sky was broken mid-flight. He chose to plunge into the abyss, offering himself up to an existence far greater and more inscrutable.\nNever again would he face the pangs of parting, the sting of mediocrity, or the inescapable ravages of time.\nHis kin, his friends, and even his foes—he has kept them all forever within Ebwynnos, a realm now fused with his very being."
  },
  AwakerStory_142872_Title = {
    Text = "Basic Information"
  },
  AwakerStory_142872_UnlockDesc = {
    Text = "Awakener Level 1"
  },
  AwakerStory_142873_Content = {
    Text = "In August of A.F. 2@17, a series of anomalous spiritual events manifested within a three-mile radius of Nara@1Bay.\n@1 recorded emergency calls reported sightings of several individuals, previously registered as deceased, lingering near the ruins of @3. These individuals were later verified to have all perished in the explosion that struck @2 Port Town in 1@19. The cause of that explosion remains unconfirmed to this day, and all individuals involved exhibited varying degrees of amnesia.\n<Italic:\"I saw her, I swear... she was as young as the day we parted. But that's impossible.\">\n<Italic:\"It's been @2 years since she bade me farewell, yet she remained as beautiful as ever. She just stood there on the cliffside with the others, smiling at me from afar.\">\n<Italic:\"...When we are cherished, we will always be granted a second chance. EBWYN@2OS... Ebwy@1noss...\">\nThe recording concluded with an unidentified static resembling the churning of seawater. Twenty hours later, the witness died at home of organ failure at the age of 76.\nThe day after this material reached Mythag University, Irene Caldwell—a retired researcher from the Awakening Studies Department and distant relative of the witness, Chambers Caldwell—received an O-@1 Silver Core that Chambers had delivered to her.\nAccording to Irene, Chambers looked no different from his younger self.\nHe left only one sentence before vanishing:\n\"Please take Him to Mythag. He shall wait there for the last wanderer of Ebwynnos to return.\"\n—Excerpt from <Italic:Mythag University Silver Core Storage Records>"
  },
  AwakerStory_142873_Title = {Text = "Story: I"},
  AwakerStory_142873_UnlockDesc = {
    Text = "Awakener Level 3"
  },
  AwakerStory_146395_Content = {
    Text = "No matter which dimension she's from, Lotan has little use for words—Lotan: Cetarchon even less so. Words mean nothing to her. Strength itself is the ultimate eloquence.\nBeneath a regal, unhurried composure lies her truest hunger, burning in heterochromatic eyes like dying stars—she is an ancient force risen from the abyss of the universe, a bone blade forged in the wrath of chaos. To her, all things fall into two categories: those worthy of a fight, and those not.\nCarved from the bones of the Astral Cetus, her twin blades hunger endlessly—just like her own unquenchable thirst for the zenith of strength."
  },
  AwakerStory_146395_Title = {
    Text = "Basic Information"
  },
  AwakerStory_146395_UnlockDesc = {
    Text = "Awakener Level 1"
  },
  AwakerStory_146396_Content = {
    Text = "Her earliest memory was nothing but rage.\nThere was no face, no form, only an endless, boiling instinct for violence. She was chaos coalesced in the depths of the cosmos, a calamity brewed over billions of years. She tore, she burned, she devoured—it was the only thing she knew.\nUntil the \"goddess\" in the white veil arrived. Like a star split in half from its core, she felt her power ebb away, her flesh and bone uprooted from her spirit, her surging fury torn raw from her soul.\nUnable to quell her rage, the goddess chose to sever her spirit from her flesh. The Beast of Chaos was no more; her body became Leviathan, sinking into the void with all her strength. And she, a mere mental remnant, awoke in an empty consciousness.\nYet her wrath had not died. It had transformed into something more enduring and terrifying: hunger. An endless hunger for strength drove her back to her feet.\nShe began to walk, to fight. She wandered the desolate sea of stars, challenging every formidable being that stood in her way. Each victory was like a handful of sand filled into her hollow shell—and grain by grain, she ground out a shape, a will, the very contour of \"Lotan: Cetarchon.\"\nThen she heard the whale's song.\nThe Astral Cetus, Its body an entire world, a colossus that bound and enslaved countless living beings—in It she saw neither desire nor fear, but kinship. Her memories began to return. She knew that was her strength. She knew that, from the very beginning, It had belonged to her.\nSo she came before It.\nSo she drew her sword against It.\nThe whale's power surged into her body like an unleashed torrent, nearly tearing her apart. Yet she remained standing—and when the tide receded, nothing was left of the whale but a carcass drifting in the void.\nThe enslaved planet was freed. The souls lost to desire looked up, calling her savior, guardian goddess, offering the Crown at her feet.\nLotan: Cetarchon did not respond to their praises. She simply stood atop the great whale's remains, feeling the newborn power surging within her, listening to the call deep in her soul growing clearer than ever.\nIt was the voice of the Astral Cetus. It was her own flesh and blood calling out to her. She placed her hand upon Leviathan's skull. Spirit and flesh, severed for countless eons, fused once more. Bone-plated armor clad her body; strength welled up within her.\nThe Beast of Chaos was reborn—but she was no longer the calamity who had known only fury. The long wandering, the countless battles, all those who had bested her and been bested by her—all had forged that pure chaos into a blade with a will of its own. She closed her eyes, savoring the surging, complete power within. But she also knew clearly that this was not the end.\nThe power of the Astral Cetus, the strength of Leviathan, all the stars she had devoured... all of it was but stepping stones beneath her feet. She lifted her bone blades, and turned toward the next unknown expanse of the universe.\nShe yearned for the next battle that would set her blood aflame."
  },
  AwakerStory_146396_Title = {Text = "Story: III"},
  AwakerStory_146396_UnlockDesc = {
    Text = "Affinity Level 7"
  },
  AwakerStory_146397_Content = {
    Text = "Lotan: Cetarchon never looks back at the corpses left in her wake.\nDefeated opponents. Shattered wastelands. Devoured stars. One by one she steps over them all, seeking her next destination.\nSomeone once asked her what she'd do after reaching the summit of strength. She did not answer. The question was meaningless; fire never contemplates where it goes once it burns out. Fire has no \"after.\" Burning is the whole of its existence.\nShe walks. She fights. She raises her blades again and again—never to prove, to protect, to avenge, or to satisfy any petty desire.\nShe does it simply because, in the clash of blades and the collision of raw strength, she can feel most vividly that she is alive.\nThe path toward strength has no end.\nAnd she wouldn't have it any other way."
  },
  AwakerStory_146397_Title = {Text = "Story: IV"},
  AwakerStory_146397_UnlockDesc = {
    Text = "Affinity Level 9"
  },
  AwakerStory_146398_Content = {
    Text = [[
Upon her arrival at Mythag, Lotan: Cetarchon remained quiet for two days. At dusk on the third, she appeared at the public training grounds, bone blades in hand.
The Awakeners of Mythag had every reason to be proud, especially those who frequented the training grounds. Yet they remained highly wary of this insolent, uninvited guest. Word of what happened on the volcanic island had already spread among the Awakeners; they knew exactly what kind of opponent awaited them.
Their caution, as it turned out, wasn't nearly enough.
When the first challenger was swatted out of the training grounds by a single strike, shattering a stone wall twenty meters away, the entire crowd erupted into an unprecedented frenzy. A second challenger stepped up, then a third... On that ordinary dusk in A.F.@3, nine Awakeners challenged Lotan: Cetarchon in succession.
According to campus reporter Hannah, who witnessed the events firsthand, Lotan: Cetarchon did not utter a single word throughout. She stood like a silent, unbreakable lighthouse amidst the crashing tides of assault. Her twin bone blades gleamed like light through the dusk, their elegant arcs ending every offensive with absolute precision.
By the end of that day, over 80% of Lotan's armor was shattered. She bore two severe wounds on her shoulder and abdomen, and a massive notch was gouged into her bone blade, leaving it on the verge of snapping. At the cost of all this, she became the only one left standing on the training grounds.
Looking at the deep gouges carved into the walls, the huge craters left on the ground, and the Awakeners watching her with conflicted expressions, she gave her first smile since arriving in this world.
"A pleasure meeting you all. You may call me Lotan: Cetarchon."]]
  },
  AwakerStory_146398_Title = {Text = "Story: II"},
  AwakerStory_146398_UnlockDesc = {
    Text = "Affinity Level 5"
  },
  AwakerStory_146399_Content = {
    Text = "Mythag University Astronomical Observatory: Anomaly Report\n\nSince A.F.@3, several observatories across the northern hemisphere have reported anomalous spectral attenuation at the galactic rim. Initial data showed that at least three catalogued stars vanished from the observable range within an extremely brief span, and their residual spectra matched no known stellar death models. No supernova radiation signature, no gravitational lensing from black hole accretion. The stars were simply swallowed whole—clean, swift, leaving no trace.\nIn March of A.F.@3, the Committee's Celestial Anomaly Task Force detected a series of extremely low-frequency Gnostic Fluctuations at the coordinates of the fourth vanished star. That August, following the fifth disappearance, the observatory finally captured a fleeting visual signal through the upgraded Silver-Core Long-Range Detection Array: a colossal, whale-like creature composed of bone, its abdomen bristling with spikes, its oral cavity emitting a high-temperature spectrum incompatible with the material plane. The instant it opened its maw, the stars' light poured in like water into the abyss—gone without a sound.\nThe footage lasted only 0.7 seconds before the array overloaded and cut out. Subsequent examination revealed irreversible structural collapse in one-third of the array's Silver-Core components.\nIn the winter of A.F.@3, the observatory detected a sudden shift in the Gnostic pulse's trajectory; its destination was our exact location.\nThe Committee was put on maximum alert, yet the anticipated catastrophe never came. The signal condensed into a harmless state upon approaching low orbit, ultimately settling on an uninhabited volcanic island in the northwestern seas. When the first survey team landed, they found twin massive blades of some unknown bone-like material deeply embedded in the basalt wall of the crater, and beside them, a humanoid figure \nseated cross-legged, as if she had long been waiting.\nThe entity appeared female, clad in bone-plated armor bearing alien motifs, with heterochromatic eyes. As the team approached, she opened her eyes.\n\"Any of you worth a strike?\"\nHer tone carried no hostility, only a calm bordering on arrogance.\nThe team exchanged glances. No one answered. After a moment's silence, she closed her eyes again.\n\"Then go find one. I'll wait.\"\nThereafter, the Committee and Mythag University jointly designated the island a Special Surveillance Zone, dispatching several Awakeners to assist in the investigation. After months of remote observation and cautious contact, the entity finally concurred with a state of loose supervision and was registered in the Committee's Awakener list—on the condition of being provided \"a truly worthy opponent.\"\nThe stellar disappearances ceased entirely following her containment. But detection data suggested the energy of the devoured stars remained stored within her body. During prolonged observation, her Gnostic Index continued to climb, showing no sign of decline."
  },
  AwakerStory_146399_Title = {Text = "Story: I"},
  AwakerStory_146399_UnlockDesc = {
    Text = "Affinity Level 3"
  },
  AwakerStory_147418_Content = {
    Text = "The farm located in the western hills of Jinbote City has now turned into a wasteland, with no one living there anymore.\n\nOn June 15, Year 2, a meteorite fell here. Several weeks later, the ecosystem in the meteorite impact area began to mutate: plants grew wildly and bore strange fruits; animals mutated, and an entire family of residents went mad and died mysteriously.\n\nMythag investigators carried out a thorough search locally and eventually discovered a Silver emitting unusual colors at the bottom of a well. According to the investigator who handled it at the time, the colors of the Silver were \"pure, flowing colors that differed from any known color in the spectrum.\"\n\n—Excerpt from \"Mythag University Silver Storage Records\""
  },
  AwakerStory_147418_Title = {Text = "Story: I"},
  AwakerStory_147418_UnlockDesc = {
    Text = "Awakener Level 3"
  },
  AwakerStory_147419_Content = {
    Text = "1. Avoid direct eye contact with D03, or she'll rush at 20 yards per second asking for help to find her sister.\n\n2. She constantly emits heat; I once saw a daffodil in her hand wither rapidly. Oh, what a nightmare for environmentalists!\n\n3. She really glows at night! So bright! With D03 around, Mythag truly doesn't need streetlights. My eyes can't handle it!\n\n4. I accidentally touched D03's arm in the cafeteria—I swear it wasn't on purpose! The sensation was strange... If I had to describe it, it felt like touching malt syrup, goat cheese, and apple pudding... Ugh, now I'm hungry.\n\n5. I heard that the Shadow Choir once invited D03 to join, but they kicked her out as fast as possible. It's understandable—human vocal cords have their limits, and I can empathize with their shock.\n\n—Excerpt from Hannah's \"Awakener Observation NotesD03\""
  },
  AwakerStory_147419_Title = {Text = "Story: II"},
  AwakerStory_147419_UnlockDesc = {
    Text = "Affinity Level 5"
  },
  AwakerStory_147420_Content = {
    Text = [[
Her singing moved countless people on her home planet.

On sleepless nights, children drifted into dreams to the sound of her songs.

In the drizzling rain, wanderers sighed as they listened to her melodies.

In the winds of lost love, lovers shed their final tears to her voice.

Now, her audience has turned to the wind, leaving behind unfinished stories...]]
  },
  AwakerStory_147420_Title = {
    Text = "Basic Information"
  },
  AwakerStory_147420_UnlockDesc = {
    Text = "Awakener Level 1"
  },
  AwakerStory_147421_Content = {
    Text = "\"Sing! The song is a gentle breeze\nSoaring beyond the clouds, crossing the stars\nThe world no longer concerns me.\"\n\n—From the album \"Color of the Stars\" overture\n\nOnce a famous singer on the wasteland star.\n\nWhen the disaster struck, she gave her ticket to her manager because she \"could not part from her sister.\"\n\nShe watched the ship of nobles leave leisurely. The once-opened glamorous door now completely shut. All that remained were the desert, her sister, and countless compatriots.\n\nThey silently listened to the countdown to death.\n\nTen years, twenty years, a hundred years... Tinct soothed everyone with her singing.\n\nUntil her throat bled, she couldn't change the reality of her sister and compatriots dying one by one.\n\nSinger Tinct walked alone in the white desert, often imagining her sister still alive.\n\nThey embraced each other as before, watching the stars fall piece by piece, remnants of warships burning quietly.\n\nShe never stopped singing. Even with a hoarse voice, devouring all nearby life with each breath.\n\nThe singer just sang numbly, day by day.\n\nAs long as she sang, \"the world no longer concerned her.\""
  },
  AwakerStory_147421_Title = {Text = "Story: III"},
  AwakerStory_147421_UnlockDesc = {
    Text = "Affinity Level 7"
  },
  AwakerStory_147422_Content = {
    Text = [[
"When one constantly reminisces about the past, it means they've grown old."

If this saying holds true, Tinct would be as ancient as the stars revolving for eons.

Her mind knows neither the present nor the future, only the endlessly prolonged and repeatedly looping past.

She once saw golden fireworks rise like a tsunami, unfurling their wings in the cosmic river;
She once saw tens of thousands of different faces concealed in darkness, wildly dancing to her melody;
She once saw the heavens calling to her, surrounding her, revealing their eternal splendor.

Yet, her eyes remain fixed on this land of suffering.]]
  },
  AwakerStory_147422_Title = {Text = "Story: IV"},
  AwakerStory_147422_UnlockDesc = {
    Text = "Affinity Level 9"
  },
  AwakerStory_148397_Content = {
    Text = "This Silver Core was recovered by Mythag's Keeper %player% in the aftermath of the Mount Ever@2t collapse incident. As the dimension in which it originally resided is no longer observable, the consequences of Silver Core extraction—as well as the proper awakening method—remain undetermined.\n\nThe following observations are transcribed from the paper handbook carried by Keeper %player%:\n\nUpon visual inspection, the Silver Core presents as exceptionally pure, showing no discernible impurities. In the absence of external interference, its overall structure trends toward regularity—as though some underlying will were straining to keep it appearing whole and composed, radiating a bright luster not unlike firelight.\n\nIts Gnosis Index, however, sits near the absolute lower bound. The actual internal structure is extraordinarily fragile and loosely bound. When the observation distance falls below 1/@1 inch, the Silver Core's self-protection response is triggered: the observer is abruptly confronted with a dense flow of particles resembling drifting ice crystals. It is presumed these particles were previously refracting incident light in a highly unusual manner, shielding the interior from direct observation.\nTo put it less professionally... I'd call this a Silver Core steeped in \"deception.\"\n\nOnce the self-protection mechanism is triggered, the observer's body enters a brief paralytic state, the pupils gradually fading until fully blanched. Throughout this window, the Silver Core continues to adjust itself, returning to the stable configuration it maintained prior to observation.\nRepeated trials indicate that the mechanism inflicts no lasting harm; however, the accompanying hypothermic symptoms pose a non-negligible risk. Note: prompt consumption of sweets—apple-based desserts in particular—provides a distinctly soothing effect. The reason for this... remains unclear... <Italic:Right?\n>\n\n\nLuckily, after everything, it's plain enough that this selfish, tightly-guarded little trickster bears no genuine ill will toward us.\n\n—Excerpt from <Italic:Mythag University Silver Core Storage Records>"
  },
  AwakerStory_148397_Title = {Text = "Story: I"},
  AwakerStory_148397_UnlockDesc = {
    Text = "Awakener Level 3"
  },
  AwakerStory_148398_Content = {
    Text = "Caraboo was still a child when the Crusades were at their height. Alone and with no one to turn to, she resolved to travel east to the Principality of Antioch to seek out her aunt's family. Word had it that the new lands of the East stood for freedom and dreams, that even someone without a penny to their name could carve out a way there. Her Aunt Rosa had even started up a farm and was doing quite well for herself. Caraboo had been close with Aunt Rosa in her early childhood, and she made up her mind to save enough for the fare to Antioch.\n\nCaraboo drifted through the city's slums, a girl with no connections, scraping by on stealing, swindling, cheating, and conning; whatever innocence she once had was worn away completely. In time, she crossed paths with a wizard named Evagh, who made her a promise: work with him, and they'd split the offerings of his followers thirty-seventy—enough for her to save her travel fare east, and plenty left over to buy heaps of her beloved candy. And so the two formed a con artist duo, with Caraboo enshrined as a little fairy godmother in a makeshift rural temple, while Evagh gathered followers in her name as her high priest.\n\nAs Caraboo's fame in the region grew, she found herself no longer content with the current split, and threatened to walk out on the partnership, forcing Evagh to flip the arrangement into a seventy-thirty split in her favor. Now finally with the upper hand, Caraboo lived at her leisure as a false godmother, until she discovered that Evagh had been embezzling her offerings all along, secretly taking three wives and fathering four sons behind her back. Faced with this betrayal, Caraboo showed no anger. She told Evagh, in the tenderest of tones, that she had long known heading east was nothing but an empty, distant dream, that money was of no use to her, and it would be better left in his hands; her only wish was to share a meal with Evagh's family, and together discuss their future ventures in fraud.\n\nDelighted to find that Caraboo had finally come to her senses, Evagh happily extended the invitation for her to attend the banquet. As dinner drew near its end, Caraboo's expression suddenly changed, and at a single word from her, the nearby villagers—her loyal believers—came storming in, wielding farming tools and kitchenware, beating the wizard's household of eight half to death, while everything of value in the house was swept clean away. \"You're still too green to fool me\"—Caraboo departed in satisfaction, not yet noticing the small black triangle upon her own forehead..."
  },
  AwakerStory_148398_Title = {Text = "Story: III"},
  AwakerStory_148398_UnlockDesc = {
    Text = "Affinity Level 7"
  },
  AwakerStory_148399_Content = {
    Text = "As everyone knows, what do they call a school?\n\nAn ivory tower!\n\nIt sounds a perfect match for the title of \"Fairy\"—after all, where else could one find such a flawless paradise, filled with wealthy, leisurely people whose hearts brim with precious, naive trust, all just waiting to become devoted followers?\n\nCaraboo's cult grew at a truly astonishing pace, amassing a considerable number of followers in a very short time. The core faithful were almost entirely young Awakeners, who believed in this \"Fairy Godmother\" with near-devout fervor, willingly turning over fixed offerings of candy and sweets at regular intervals. Surprisingly, or perhaps not, Caraboo did indeed bestow blessings from time to time, most often during the traditional holidays of the Kingdom of Leonia, such as the impossible snowfall that came during the Silverfrost Eve of 3@1, and the candy rain on New Year's Eve that people still speak of to this day.\n\nThe Academic Affairs Office, it seems, never once discussed whether to put a stop to this \"on-campus proselytizing\" that, in principle, ought not to exist in the first place.\n\n\"Let them play. We all know what these children have been through. There are certain things only another child can do.\"\n\n\"Of course, don't let it go too far.\"\n\nA certain school staff member, who prefers to remain unnamed, offered the above remarks with a warm smile. According to unreliable sources, the incident preceding her afternoon tea with Caraboo was the one and only time Caraboo has ever truly attempted to cross the school's rules."
  },
  AwakerStory_148399_Title = {Text = "Story: II"},
  AwakerStory_148399_UnlockDesc = {
    Text = "Affinity Level 5"
  },
  AwakerStory_148400_Content = {
    Text = [[
Like the most precocious of children, she is always attuned to your innermost thoughts, forever drawing out your trust and confessions, then, at just the right moment, offering you the "blessing" you've longed for. 
But bear this in mind: never let her dainty frame and pitiful eyes stir compassion within you, lest you become one more of the many greedy souls that pure white form has devoured.]]
  },
  AwakerStory_148400_Title = {
    Text = "Basic Information"
  },
  AwakerStory_148400_UnlockDesc = {
    Text = "Awakener Level 1"
  },
  AwakerStory_148401_Content = {
    Text = "Have you ever tried telling a lie? The first lie to leave your lips always comes with a stumbling tongue, a heart that nearly leaps out of your throat, and sweat gathering in your palms; even the gentle sunlight becomes a dizzying, blinding glare.\n\nBut once a lie has been repeated ten thousand times, the fear fades away. The words spoken grow smooth, the mind grows ever clearer, and the smile settles into something quite natural.\n\nPlaying the fairy, playing the godmother, playing the kin of some figure in power—she had long since mastered the myriad layered identities she had fabricated, grown accustomed to hiding herself behind her lies, until she herself became but a part of the lies.\n\nAnd that first little hare still hides within a small farm bathed in the sunset light of her memories.\n\nOn nights when the ice thaws and the snow melts away, it quietly peeks its head out once more."
  },
  AwakerStory_148401_Title = {Text = "Story: IV"},
  AwakerStory_148401_UnlockDesc = {
    Text = "Affinity Level 9"
  },
  AwakerStory_148994_Content = {
    Text = "Though his form remains unchanged, anyone can tell at a glance the difference between him and the small knight they once knew.\nThe once-clear eyes no longer shine, the white garments are stained with filth, and he always keeps a deliberate distance from everyone.\nBut there is no need for fear — beneath that terrible black mire, the heart you know still beats, faithful and just.\nThough he once lost his way, he ultimately reclaimed those knightly vows.\nHe will continue to fight — against the other voice within him, and against all that would harm what he holds dear."
  },
  AwakerStory_148994_Title = {
    Text = "Basic Information"
  },
  AwakerStory_148994_UnlockDesc = {
    Text = "Awakener Level 1"
  },
  AwakerStory_149051_Content = {
    Text = "A paranormal incident once shook the entire Mythag campus. The following is an interview transcript compiled by campus journalist Hannah:\n\"In the dead of night, there were rustling sounds in the library... I didn't dare look. But the next morning, I found every book inside had been arranged perfectly — even neater than I could have done myself!\" — School librarian\n\"Haven't you noticed the campus has been a lot cleaner lately? Is there some ghost that tidies up the trash at night?\" — A practical studies teacher\n\"When I'm out on missions, I always feel like someone is following me... Sometimes I hear the sounds of fierce combat, and when I turn around, all that's left is a pile of dissolved monster remains.\" — A rookie Investigator\nA few bold students spontaneously formed an investigation team, trading a night's sleep for answers.\nThe one responsible for it all admitted to their \"crimes\" and sincerely apologized for causing panic. Yet when faced with the gratitude that followed, he seemed rather flustered. In his own words, \"I just can't sit still.\"\nOn this matter, school counselor Sylvia offered her diagnosis: \"As a genuinely kind-hearted child, he carries far too much guilt over the past. Over time, it has become a deep-rooted sense of unworthiness — the overly direct goodwill of others actually makes him more uncomfortable.\"\nThe incident quietly came to a close, yet the legend of the \"invisible ghost\" spread from that day on. Teachers and students all tacitly refrained from revealing his identity. Gradually, however, everyone came to understand that this \"ghost\" simply wanted to help.\nEveryone seemed to know: for this boy who wished not to be seen, the best expression of gratitude was to let this secret remain his alone."
  },
  AwakerStory_149051_Title = {Text = "Story: II"},
  AwakerStory_149051_UnlockDesc = {
    Text = "Affinity Level 5"
  },
  AwakerStory_149052_Content = {
    Text = "Dear readers, this is an afterword — and my confession.\nTo complete this old-fashioned classical knight novel, I spent a fortune at auction to obtain a mysterious helmet, one said to belong to no nation with any recorded history. As you can see, thanks to it, my inspiration flowed ceaselessly; I felt as though I truly beheld a vast and sweeping ancient battlefield, where armored knights clashed blade against blade. Relying on these wondrous visions, I completed what I consider my most perfect work.\nYet I never imagined that this antique, while granting me inspiration, concealed within it a terrifying demon.\nReaders, try to imagine: a voice — chaotic, unceasing, day and night without rest. Then imagine your limbs beginning to move beyond your control, your consciousness fragmenting again and again — no, not fragmenting, more like your will departing your body. You are aware of everything you are doing, yet can only watch... but that is unmistakably my body.\nJust last night, the moment I finished this novel, I heard It again.\nAnd then — damn it, I have no wish to recall those images —\nI committed an unforgivable sin. The newspapers will tell you before this book ever does...\nIt — is here again, starting again —\n(handwriting becomes erratic)\nNo no no no no no no no, I cannot —\n......\n\n(handwriting becomes clear again)\nAstonishingly, It has stopped — as though something is holding It down. I do not know what that is, but I am grateful for its resistance.\nPerhaps God is granting me one final chance, so that I do not fall utterly into damnation.\n\nMy gun is already loaded.\nMay God forgive me.\n\n\n— Excerpted from the afterword of \"The Shadowless Knight,\" the final work of author Clark Zilos"
  },
  AwakerStory_149052_Title = {Text = "Story: I"},
  AwakerStory_149052_UnlockDesc = {
    Text = "Awakener Level 3"
  },
  AwakerStory_149064_Content = {
    Text = "The deep black mire that embodies sin still churns within him, desperate to seize control of this body once more. He must constantly grip that fragile thread, lest he be overcome.\nAnd what he has found anew — something worth defending — has become the sole anchor keeping his sanity intact.\nHe can no longer return to his homeland, but Mythag has become his new castle.\nHe can no longer protect his princess, but fate will still create new encounters.\nIn a place where no one bears witness, the young man kneels on one knee, one hand placed over his cold chest, and makes his declaration to a liege lord who is not present.\n\"I will faithfully follow your commands, and protect you and your world forever — even if it burns away my life, even if it drains my very soul.\"\n\"...This is the vow I have taken up once more.\""
  },
  AwakerStory_149064_Title = {Text = "Story: IV"},
  AwakerStory_149064_UnlockDesc = {
    Text = "Affinity Level 9"
  },
  AwakerStory_149065_Content = {
    Text = "He too had once set out on a journey, just as the bedtime fairy tales described.\nYet he was no knight singing the praises of justice, and no princess awaiting rescue existed in this world any longer.\nWhat he slew were not fearsome evil dragons, but many fleeing, wailing, unarmed civilians.\n\"The young knight slew the wicked sorcerer, routed the stubborn enemy forces, burned the monster's fortress to the ground...\nHe was brave, he was mighty, undefeated in every battle. Along this road with no end in sight, he left behind only a long, trailing streak of blood.\"\nIf there existed in this world a bard who could not tell dream from reality, they would surely dress up this experience in just such a manner.\nBut the protagonist of this story was in truth clear-eyed — those eyes never once reflected anything false.\nHe knew: his spear had pierced through an old man's chest, the black mire had swallowed soldiers who had already surrendered, and a delicate little house belonging to some family had turned to ash in his wake... all because these things were connected to those who had taken what he was sworn to protect.\nHe knew: he had never been inside a fairy tale. Those romantic illusions had died completely along with his homeland. Perhaps he had grown up in that moment, or perhaps he was still an immature child.\nUntil at last he came to his senses, and in the act of giving his life for strangers he had never met, he suddenly saw — within his own tears — a phantom that should never have existed.\n\"Ogier, I am deeply disappointed in you. You are a knight in name only — the most unworthy knight of all.\"\nThe face of the \"princess\" seemed veiled in gauze, yet her voice was unnervingly clear, sharper than any blade in the world, carving into his heart.\nThis cruel phantom remains a nightmare that torments him to this day, and did not fade with his death.\nHe will live for eternity in the remorse of having broken his vow."
  },
  AwakerStory_149065_Title = {Text = "Story: III"},
  AwakerStory_149065_UnlockDesc = {
    Text = "Affinity Level 7"
  },
  AwakerStory_60980_Content = {
    Text = "At first glance, Hameln always reminded you of a kind of Eastern porcelain—white, luxurious, with graceful curves and a wave-like gentle sheen, yet somewhat cold to the touch.\n\nBeneath that respectable, meticulous exterior lies a soul of extreme, empty purity. His entire life revolved around a single thought, like a machine programmed with one command, devoid of all other responses.\n\nTo him, everything was merely a sequence of musical notes.\n\nPlay, play, endlessly play."
  },
  AwakerStory_60980_Title = {
    Text = "Basic Information"
  },
  AwakerStory_60980_UnlockDesc = {
    Text = "Awakener has reached level 1"
  },
  AwakerStory_60981_Content = {
    Text = [[
Hameln did not always appear before students. Even though he was willing to attend Mythag's musical events and guide the less adept students, most of the time, he played alone in a soundproof room or in secluded woods.

Except for official events, he called all of his playing simply "practice," as if the practice was endless, and the perfect performance would never arrive.

 People praised his work, "Such a diligent and humble master," they sung, intoxicated by its melody.

Yet, Hameln never knew humility; his words were always straightforward and overly harsh.

Such an obsessive pursuit of perfection in music made his classes a primary source of stress for students, earning him the title the "devil's teacher."

If, for some reason, you wished to get his attention, simply play the wrong note, and his frowning expression would be upon you almost immediately.

He bore no grudge against those he "tormented," merely imposing his passionate, impossibly perfect standard upon them, even if it was much milder compared to what he demanded of himself.

He was like a horse with a carrot dangling overhead, forever striving for somethung unattainable.

Except for pausing for the elegant dancer, he rarely initiated contact with other Awakeners. However, he always displayed a surprising patience with requests and initiating conversation.

Perhaps it wasn't indifference that hindered him, but too narrow a mind.]]
  },
  AwakerStory_60981_Title = {Text = "Story: II"},
  AwakerStory_60981_UnlockDesc = {
    Text = "Affinity Level 5"
  },
  AwakerStory_60982_Content = {
    Text = [[
A.F. 31@1, @1, @2, a famous tycoon who loved collecting music was found dead in his study by his butler late at night. There were no visible wounds or signs of poisoning on his body, and a strangely satisfied smile lingered on his lips.

Following extensive examination by forensic experts, the death was ruled an accidental one, as the room was locked with no way to get inside.

However, doctors could not provide a reasonable explanation for why this robust tycoon, who was in good health and even enjoyed horseback riding, suddenly died on such an ordinary and quiet night. Under pressure from his family, the police handed over the case to the Committee.

Initially intending to quietly resolve the matter, the Committee unexpectedly detected traces of Gnosis on scattered sheet music found on the tycoon's desk. The eerie sheet music was sent to Mythag posthaste, where research identified it as fragments of the lost second half of the famous "Requiem in A Minor." The final page of the score remained incomplete, with numerous frantic drafts scattered around, seemingly attempts by the tycoon to complete it.

Scholars at Mythag speculated that this attempt to complete the score caused the tycoon's descent into madness and eventual death, completing the awakening ceremony in an unconventional manner and prompting its immediate sealing.

For a long time, Mythag found no evidence of this unknown Awakener appearing or causing harm, causing the case to gradually fade from investigators' minds and into obscurity.

Only scholars in the field of music continued to yearn for the sealed half-sheet, hoping for the legendary composer to emerge.]]
  },
  AwakerStory_60982_Title = {Text = "Story: I"},
  AwakerStory_60982_UnlockDesc = {
    Text = "Affinity Level 3"
  },
  AwakerStory_60983_Content = {
    Text = "Talent seemed to be a rare favor of destiny. Hameln had never witnessed it in anyone around him during his long adolescence. It became a vague image—a symbol driving him forward under his father's whip.\n\nHe firmly believed that relentless diligence was the endless ladder to the perfection just out of reach. Even when he stood at the pinnacle of the world stage, it remained an unchanging truth.\n\nThis was until he met someone that could stand beside him.\n\n\"What a dazzling genius!\" they cried: this gift of so-called talent was not within him, but another.\n\nFrom festering envy and jealousy, he suddenly felt an indescribable confusion and helplessness.\n\nWithout such talent, can I still reach the perfect end?\n\nThe rungs of the ladder of diligence had suddenly turned to ashes, while the door to perfection remained ever distant.\n\nHe often lingered outside the crowds that swarmed this genius, deliberately aloof.\n\nBut whenever he looked in that direction, he always silently rehearsed his greetings.\n\nThose mediocre insects always surrounded them, murmuring malicious whispers.\n\nHe was far too clumsy, silent for so long without being able to argue.\n\nWords meant little, he thought. Let music be his medium—for only music is the perfect language; surely they would understand.\n\nHowever, fate was a fickle beast, and would always come to reclaim the gifts it had so generously given.\n\nGeniuses die young, and yet the mediocre still stand.\n\nIn the past, provocations and scheming had never shaken him in the slightest.\n\nYet at this moment, looking at the stack of unsent, unsatisfactory music scores, he could only shed tears of anger.\n\nHameln suddenly understood: before reaching this perfect kingdom of heaven, he must use all means available in world below.\n\nFortunately, compared to those mediocre people, he already possessed the intellect to do it.\n\nAfter all, in his eyes, everything was nothing more than a calculation, like notes arranged on a score."
  },
  AwakerStory_60983_Title = {Text = "Story: III"},
  AwakerStory_60983_UnlockDesc = {
    Text = "Affinity Level 7"
  },
  AwakerStory_60984_Content = {
    Text = "His life was monotonous and dull, with loneliness as a contant companion, alongside feelings of resentment, confusion and hatred that had long been digested since before he could even remember.\n\nNow, he has become one with music, transcending mere passion—unavoidable, inescapable.\n\nAll that remains to him is music.\n\nKeep moving upward; do not look back at those nine hundred and ninety-nine steps behind.\n\nAfter all, he has already touched the ultimate melody, the destined flute.\n\nAccept this endless flow of music, and let it saturate your soul and dreams.\n\nFor he has long since used his own soul as an instrument to resonate with yours."
  },
  AwakerStory_60984_Title = {Text = "Story: IV"},
  AwakerStory_60984_UnlockDesc = {
    Text = "Affinity Level 9"
  },
  AwakerStory_66033_Content = {
    Text = [[
Tawil has manifested in Mythag only three times.

The first time, Tawil ignited the spark of "Wisdom." The Gatekeeper opened the passage to dream, imparting rare Knowledge to the ignorant founders of Mythag. They provided Mythag's original "think tank," along with clues and insights about Dissolution.

The second time, Tawil delivered the prophecy of "Change." The Black Pool churned, welcoming the Arrival of the one who would "Transform" the world.

The third time, They transmitted the signal of "Finale." Their cries and wails resonated across the earth, yet could not prevent the inevitable descent of Chaos and Destruction.]]
  },
  AwakerStory_66033_Title = {Text = "Story: II"},
  AwakerStory_66033_UnlockDesc = {
    Text = "Affinity Level 5"
  },
  AwakerStory_66034_Content = {
    Text = [[
Kadath is not the only dream Tawil seeks to protect.

The Gatekeeper has witnessed the birth and destruction of countless planets and galaxies, with the histories of past and future sedimented into knowledge, absorbed into the Ultimate Gate behind Them. With a gaze full of compassion, Tawil looks down upon these scenes, which dissolve into fleeting glimpses in Their dreams, vanishing into the darkness of the boundless abyss.

Tawil once stepped onto a piece of land, but in the moment They glanced back, everything They cherished crumbled beneath the breath of the "Supreme Will."

After endless repetitions, They finally realized a harsh truth: Their very existence serves as the prelude to a nightmare; Their immense presence alone draws the gaze of the "Supreme Will." Their interference would only bring deeper misfortune to the world They hold dear.

Thus, Tawil retreated. Tawil fell silent.

Until They perceived a glimmer of change emanating from "It" within the drifting fragments of consciousness in the infinite expanse...]]
  },
  AwakerStory_66034_Title = {Text = "Story: III"},
  AwakerStory_66034_UnlockDesc = {
    Text = "Affinity Level 7"
  },
  AwakerStory_66035_Content = {
    Text = "In a mysterious dream, I first saw Them.\n\nIn an endless and foggy space, They guarded a majestic and eternal Gate linking countless vast universes. Beyond the deep cracks of the Gate, strange illusions flickered like undeciphered signals. Upon catching a signal, I felt my body vanish, aimlessly floating among the stars, enshrouded by an incredible darkness. I was terrified; the dream violently shook, the heavy Gate irresistibly opening, with countless sphere-like objects shining like stars beyond it. The vast and unfathomable scene made me dizzy... and the Gate's guardian—Tawil—silently and eternally watched me.\n\n—Ward Phillips, Silver Key Notes"
  },
  AwakerStory_66035_Title = {Text = "Story: I"},
  AwakerStory_66035_UnlockDesc = {
    Text = "Affinity Level 3"
  },
  AwakerStory_66036_Content = {
    Text = "As the Aeon of Sagacity's Proxy and Gatekeeper, Tawil has not lacked the desire to explore Their own essence. Tawil yearns to walk the earth like those The Gatekeeper watches over, witnessing the changes in civilization and the vicissitudes of history, gathering all They see into a treasury called 'Omniscience.' But Their existence does not allow Them to abandon Their post. Deep in Tawil's heart, perhaps what They envy most is the girl who carries a thread of Their will..."
  },
  AwakerStory_66036_Title = {Text = "Story: IV"},
  AwakerStory_66036_UnlockDesc = {
    Text = "Affinity Level 9"
  },
  AwakerStory_66037_Content = {
    Text = "Tawil does not exist in the current world. Their existence would draw the attention of the 'Supreme Will,' so They cannot and must not exist. Wisdom and silence are all The Gatekeeper can offer to these tireless seekers. In Their daily vigil, Tawil quietly bestows Their wisdom, courage, and silent blessings upon the fate of humanity."
  },
  AwakerStory_66037_Title = {
    Text = "Basic Information"
  },
  AwakerStory_66037_UnlockDesc = {
    Text = "Awakener Level 1"
  },
  AwakerStory_76412_Content = {
    Text = "I do not believe Robert would commit suicide by gunshot. No, I do not believe it.\n\nHe received a medal for bravery and solved many difficult murder cases; he is a determined veteran agent. Most importantly, he was about to get married, and the girl loved him back, so there must be a conspiracy here! Someone murdered him and staged it as a suicide scene!\n\nWhoever the murderer is, I will find him and make him pay. This is something I must do as a brother and an agent.\n\n...\n\nThe scene had no clues, so I had to return to my hometown, which was the last place Robert visited before his suicide. After many inquiries, I learned that he had entered deep into the mountains.\n\nAs for why he went there, I suspect it has something to do with local traditions: the first child in every family is taken to the mountains during their coming-of-age ceremony.\n\nSince my parents moved away from here when we were young, Robert never practiced this tradition. I think it was the sense of responsibility before starting a family that awakened his adherence to tradition.\n\nRegardless, I need to take a trip to the deep mountains. After finishing this entry, I’ll set off immediately.\n\n...\n\nA grand structure was carved out in the mountains, I do not know which era it belongs to, I can't tell. I only know that cruel rituals have been continuously conducted here, with dismembered limbs and larvae... I can't write anymore.\n\n...\n\nThese larvae... no, those are not my grandparents, not my ancestors... I cannot have the bloodline of a monster. Ah—\n\n...\n\n...I was discovered by the monsters conducting the rituals; they want to turn me into a monster too!\n\n...\n\nIf someone reads this diary, kill me, immediately...@2\n\n...\n\nPraise the great @2, hiss @2... Praise blind folly @4... hssss... @1 hiss...\n\n—Excerpt from the diary of the late involved agent @3, with omissions"
  },
  AwakerStory_76412_Title = {Text = "Story: I"},
  AwakerStory_76412_UnlockDesc = {
    Text = "Awakener Level 3"
  },
  AwakerStory_76413_Content = {
    Text = "<Thank you, Clementine, I feel much better. You really are the person who understands me best in this world.>\n\n When entering and exiting Clementine's counseling room, the Keeper often hears such voices. Regardless of how those patients and Awakeners were before they entered, they emerge light-footed and beaming with smiles.\n\n There was even a time when the Keeper saw Clementine providing psychological counseling to a stray cat that accidentally wandered into the consultation room.\n\n The results are apparent; everyone who has undergone counseling has praised Clementine, rapidly spreading her influence. However, this also brought troubles —\n\n \"Good afternoon, Keeper.\"  \n\nClementine appeared with a smile on your path, and you weren't surprised; her continuously ringing communicator had already said it all. Those patients who trusted her unconditionally have become her eyes and ears, helping her achieve various goals, whether directly or indirectly.\n\n \"I think that even if you wanted to become the mayor of this city, those who received counseling would unconditionally help you achieve that.\"  \n\nFacing the Keeper's joke, Clementine smiled nonchalantly.\n\n \"I'm not interested in any of that.\"  \n\nYes, Clementine is not interested in those things. Thankfully, she is not.\n\n Otherwise, the dark secrets poured out during psychological counseling would be enough to disturb this city.\n\n \"Right now, I just want to explore the secrets deep within your heart, Keeper.\"\n"
  },
  AwakerStory_76413_Title = {Text = "Story: II"},
  AwakerStory_76413_UnlockDesc = {
    Text = "Affinity Level 5"
  },
  AwakerStory_76414_Content = {
    Text = [[
At first, some trivial pain could satisfy her. 

Then, her craving for sweetness led her to embrace more and more malice during psychological guidance. 

This malice surged like a river, flooding one after another island of the soul. 

But it was not enough. Far from it. 

Only with the awakening of that ancient long dream, will the entire world turn into a sea of pain, bringing ultimate joy. 

So, she was excited, she prayed, she waited. 

When everything merged into chaos, she would bow her head, joyfully savoring the most extreme lament of the world. 

Even if this sea of pain would drown her.
]]
  },
  AwakerStory_76414_Title = {Text = "Story: IV"},
  AwakerStory_76414_UnlockDesc = {
    Text = "Affinity Level 9"
  },
  AwakerStory_76415_Content = {
    Text = "Everyone wears different masks of personality, and she chose the one that most numbs the heart —\n\nShe smiles gently, saying every expression and every word so soothing, making the patients who come for psychological counseling genuinely feel they have met their soulmate and guide in this life.\nThat is enough.\n\nThe doomed moth needs not to know the ending, only to follow her guidance.\n\nIn that seemingly warm redemption, the flames consume, no turning back.\n"
  },
  AwakerStory_76415_Title = {
    Text = "Basic Information"
  },
  AwakerStory_76415_UnlockDesc = {
    Text = "Awakener Level 1"
  },
  AwakerStory_76416_Content = {
    Text = [[
In fact, the true Clementine had already died the moment the Passing Great Will became a parasite.

What broke free from that altar full of flesh and blood was a newborn with a great essence, far surpassing human life.

New life, old memories. The body nurtured by this planet, the soul born from the depths of the universe.

Such a contradictory existence puzzled Clementine, but soon, the hunger from the Soul left her unable to think.

Human food is so bland; only painful memories are somewhat palatable. And the more torment and despair those memories carry, the sweeter and more delicious they taste.

In that moment, she finally understood her way of survival.

"Speak to me, whether it be pain or despair, show it all to me."

She sat behind her desk, gazing maliciously at the patient who came for consultation, her expression filled with tenderness, enough to disarm anyone.

That was the disguise and mask of insect hunting.
]]
  },
  AwakerStory_76416_Title = {Text = "Story: III"},
  AwakerStory_76416_UnlockDesc = {
    Text = "Affinity Level 7"
  },
  AwakerStory_81334_Content = {
    Text = "The experience of interacting with Castor often reveals two strikingly contrasting extremes.\n\nAt first glance, his overly serious and composed demeanor closely resembles that of a middle-aged clerk who has spent twenty years working at Londinium Bank: rigid, unromantic, drained of all vitality by monotonous work. When he frowns, he indeed carries a saint-like presence—calm yet exuding authority without raising his voice.\n\nHowever, upon deeper interaction, you'll discover that all his seemingly conservative behaviors stem from an extremely limited knowledge base and an unparalleled level of bluntness, to the point where he takes any joke directed at him completely seriously.\n\nHe often clutches a thick notebook, ceaselessly questioning the Keeper as if he were a toddler still learning to speak. Faced with such earnest and sincere gaze, most people find it difficult to express disdain for those naive questions.\n\nBeyond scriptures related to various beliefs, Castor is insatiably curious about any new knowledge, especially regarding modern society and science; he has even developed a strong interest in experimental research. After being ruthlessly ignored by Doll: Inferno, he turned to relentlessly pursue poor Winkle, who tries to escape from him daily.\n\nIf he were in a school classroom, he would be the kind of diligent student adored by teachers—he does not see studying as a burden, but rather views the freedom to absorb interesting knowledge as a heartfelt joy.\n\nHowever, while the teacher might feel content, some boastful Awakeners become infuriated when faced with his endless logical inquiries, unable to answer them, leaving behind a bewildered Castor reflecting on the profound difficulty of learning and the long road ahead."
  },
  AwakerStory_81334_Title = {Text = "Story: II"},
  AwakerStory_81334_UnlockDesc = {
    Text = "Affinity Level 5"
  },
  AwakerStory_81335_Content = {
    Text = [[
If born into an ordinary family, Castor might have grown into a modest young man as warm and steady as a tree. But now, he is the only one among the twins who retained a complete body and soul; he remains silent like a stone, waiting to bury that ember the two of them shared in their youth deep within, never giving up, never wavering.
Those already matured wings, capable of stirring up a storm, are now retracted in dormancy, as a bird quietly awaits the moment the cage door opens to once again soar in the sky.]]
  },
  AwakerStory_81335_Title = {
    Text = "Basic Information"
  },
  AwakerStory_81335_UnlockDesc = {
    Text = "Awakener Level 1"
  },
  AwakerStory_81336_Content = {
    Text = "While carrying out a mission on a remote, barren, and little-known plateau far from Londinium, I happened upon an astonishing account in a mountain village with only a handful of residents remaining.\n\nOn the night the monster appeared, the sky itself seemed shrouded by an eerie shadow. Fog rolled across the ground, and deep within the clouds, a dim green hue emerged—this was by no means a mere natural phenomenon, but the projection of something alive, something breathing.\n\nFrom deep within the desolate mountains, bristling with tall trees, a sudden roar—a howling shockwave—erupted. That shriek, belonging to no known creature, stirred fear from the deepest recesses of human instinct.\n\nA massive shadow swept swiftly overhead. The entire mountain shuddered beneath that sky-blotting form, and every branch and leaf trembled in unison, producing a synchronized, whisper-like rustling.\n\n<Italic:\"I saw it! Those long, densely packed tentacles, those eyes glowing green—that was without question the source of the horror in the sky. It discovered me, even locked its gaze firmly on me! I truly thought my life would end at that very moment, but perhaps it had just finished a full meal. Before I blacked out from suffocation, it mercifully turned and left.\">\n\nThis is the only interview with a confirmed eyewitness. The villager, still deeply mired in nightmares to this day, refused to recall further details. However, from the available evidence, this massive dark-green monster—aside from destroying part of the mountain forest like a passing hurricane and leaving behind a few beast skeletons with only traces of blood remaining—showed no greater aggression, behaving much like a predator feeding normally. Perhaps its approach toward the village was driven by nothing more than idle curiosity.\n\nBut in the face of any unknown horror, we must prepare for the worst. I will continue my investigation on the @3 Plateau for a period of half a month. Should any other noteworthy signs of danger arise, I will append them to the mission report at once.— Excerpt from <Italic:\"Mythag Overseas Investigation Notes, A.F.3@2 Annual Compendium\">"
  },
  AwakerStory_81336_Title = {Text = "Story: I"},
  AwakerStory_81336_UnlockDesc = {
    Text = "Affinity Level 3"
  },
  AwakerStory_81337_Content = {
    Text = "What is the price of pursuing freedom and escaping the church? The twins anticipated horrifying punishments, even the loss of their own lives, but they never expected that the most painful thing was never the physical torture, but the flaying of the soul.\n\nCastor stared with bloodshot eyes as Pollux's treasured, lively and magnificent wings were brutally torn off. His own lips were bitten raw, and he waited in madness and guilt, craving for the same pain to befall him.\n\nHowever, Juliette merely waved her hand, and the severely injured Castor was taken down like a broken sack, thrown into a pool filled with d-slime for the \"sin-effacement rite.\"\n\nThe black, viscous slime soaked his injured body, seeping into every wound and covering every feather, making it even harder to breathe.\n\nIn the cycle of wounds repeatedly corroding and healing, the image of the torn-out wings spiraled in Castor's dazed mind. He sat in the small cage in agony, wishing he could bear all the torment for his brother. He wished he had been the one to have his wings pulled out that day, yet later he resolutely thought that he must use these wings to fly with his brother towards freedom again.\n\nCastor endured day after day in this hellish pool; time became unperceivable through pain. It felt like waiting for dozens of years, waiting until Castor nearly died again, before he finally crawled out from that dark hell. The eager eyes he faced were met with a cold and disdainful gaze.\n\n\"Stop looking at me with that disgusting look! Let me give you another piece of advice, Lord Castor. You and I are merely serving as the Twin Divi of the Lightbearer together. Leave me alone unless you have a serious matter to discuss. It gets annoying, you know?\"\n\nCastor did not understand why his brother had completely forgotten him, but he finally realized the meaning of Juliette's deeply meaningful gaze when he left the pool of sin—because she now tightly held the collar that could control him, a guarantee of her absolute confidence."
  },
  AwakerStory_81337_Title = {Text = "Story: III"},
  AwakerStory_81337_UnlockDesc = {
    Text = "Affinity Level 7"
  },
  AwakerStory_81338_Content = {
    Text = "Twins are born with nothing but each other, yet Castor continues to savor the taste of loss. Hurt, forgotten, and betrayed—his silent heart is not made of iron, yet he keeps getting back up.\n\n\"But it's okay. I'll hold on to your share too,\" Castor said, looking at his disfigured brother with blind faith. In his heart, he clutches tightly to that faint flame, tirelessly resisting the knife-like wind and snow.\n\nOne day, he will climb to the peak of freedom and use his wings to touch the sky's low-hanging curtain. He believes that at the end of that thorny path must lie the bright daylight his younger brother promised him in childhood."
  },
  AwakerStory_81338_Title = {Text = "Story: IV"},
  AwakerStory_81338_UnlockDesc = {
    Text = "Affinity Level 9"
  },
  AwakerStory_81615_Content = {
    Text = "She is the flag that flutters high as the ship sails, guiding its course; she is also the dirge that holds to its duty until the very last moment, when the ship sinks beneath the waves.\n\nHer responsibility, her duty, her life—all are bound to the ship; nothing else remains.\n\nFor guiding the course is the very meaning of her existence."
  },
  AwakerStory_81615_Title = {
    Text = "Basic Information"
  },
  AwakerStory_81615_UnlockDesc = {
    Text = "Awakener Level 1"
  },
  AwakerStory_81616_Content = {
    Text = "Before learning to speak, having grown up on a cruise ship, Corposant could already mimic the rhythm of waves crashing against the ship.\n\nSometimes the rhythm was \"splash, \" sometimes it was \"boom, \" like a lullaby sung by nature, making her feel secure, making her feel familiar, making her yearn.\n\nShe always understood the \"mood\" of the sea quicker than others, always read the \"language\" of the clouds quicker than others, and everyone said she was a natural \"navigator.\"\n\nIn reality, when she first heard the term, young Corposant couldn't understand. She only instinctively wanted to help the captain and sailors who took her in, wanting them to return home safely, not to be lost to storms or disasters from other ships.\n\nThe navigator who understood her wish said, \"Become a navigator, Corposant, become a navigator, fulfill your duty, and then your wish will come true.\"\n\nThe naive Corposant nodded, and thus, that navigator became her mentor. He taught her how to observe the stars, how to calibrate the sextant, and told her the ballads passed down through generations of navigators, those ominous ballads.\n\n\"I don't want to be embraced by saltwater, that's too cold, nor do I want to become phosphorescence.\" Young Corposant objected.\n\nHer mentor didn't teach her anything further, just touched her head and smiled.\n\nBecause time will teach her the meaning of the \"navigator's\" duty—\n\nShe is the sole guide on the vast ocean, the only hope."
  },
  AwakerStory_81616_Title = {Text = "Story: III"},
  AwakerStory_81616_UnlockDesc = {
    Text = "Affinity Level 7"
  },
  AwakerStory_81617_Content = {
    Text = "No one knows where that ghost ship lies, nor can anyone confirm whether \"it\" truly exists. The only clue I have is that ivory head sculpture, which seems to possess some sort of strange magic.\n\nEver since I came into possession of it, I have had the same dream every night—yes, the dream of that ghost ship, drifting somewhere unknown. Its hull burns with a glimmer that writhes like a living thing, as though opening a gateway to dimensions beyond mortal reach. Upon waking, I can still recall those blasphemous, pathological whispers.\n\nHow I wish I were mad, or that I could forget those bizarre sounds—sounds that no human throat could ever produce. But I cannot.\n\nThat cursed dream, that cursed flicker of intellect, torment me without rest. And so I must find \"it,\" led by the ivory sculpture. Frtunately, the professors from Miskatonic will walk this road with me, and together we shall seek out the ghost ship and the St. Elmo's Fire—that is what they call the writhing glimmer.\n\nWish me luck. May the Lord watch over us.\n\n—Excerpt from <Italic:Miskatonic Supernatural Phenomena Investigation Archives>"
  },
  AwakerStory_81617_Title = {Text = "Story: I"},
  AwakerStory_81617_UnlockDesc = {
    Text = "Awakener Level 3"
  },
  AwakerStory_81618_Content = {
    Text = "Corposant's daily schedule is very fixed; you just need to be at a specific place at a specific time to find her.\n\nGenerally speaking, Corposant gets up at 6:00, takes a cold bath, and does exercises. 7:00 is breakfast time, and besides oatmeal and pickled fish, a large amount of caffeine supplements is also required.\n\nFrom 9:00 to 12:00, it is Corposant's study time; she will revise nautical charts or calibrate equipment during this period. When the class bell rings, Corposant will come outdoors, waving a flag as a traffic officer, which greatly alleviates the road congestion during lunch.\n\nCorposant's lunch time depends on the \"traffic conditions, \" but no later than 12: 30. After a short break, at 14:00, Corposant will appear at the seaside on time, observing wind direction and weather. At this point, attention should be paid to the movements of Corposant, Faros, and Celeste, to avoid them \"commandeering\" the museum model ships or luring passersby out to sea.\n\nDinner time is at 19:00. To numb her sleep cycle, completely destroyed by long-term sailing, Corposant needs to consume a large amount of alcohol and sleep-inducing tinctures. Only in this way can she successfully fall asleep at 22:00; otherwise, she will force herself to stay awake to deal with possible \"accidents\" during the voyage.\n\nConsequently, situations resulting from this include, but are not limited to, the phenomenon of St. Elmo's fire going out of control, leading to the entire area shining like daylight, or abnormal, uncontrolled area voltage, machinery running erratically, fires, etc.\n\n<Red:Note, during this time absolutely do not let Erica and Corposant come into contact with each other!>\n\nFinally, a criticism notification:\n\nAfter Corposant's arrival, Winkle made several attempts to extract and study @2 at Corposant's chest as a light source. A verbal criticism has been issued; if any abnormalities are found, be sure to inform the Keeper in time.\n\n—Keeper %player%"
  },
  AwakerStory_81618_Title = {Text = "Story: II"},
  AwakerStory_81618_UnlockDesc = {
    Text = "Affinity Level 5"
  },
  AwakerStory_81619_Content = {
    Text = "Until the last moment, Corposant was diligently fulfilling her duties, yet the ship she piloted still sank.\n\nEvery night, she dreams of those lost passengers: water flooding into the cabins, sea monsters' Tentacles rampaging, people drowning, jumping overboard, kneeling for one last guidance, but hope was lost.\n\nThis brutal reality reproaches her, tortures her—she has desecrated her profession.\n\nFor this, she must be punished, and the lightning that eternally entwines and torments her is the retribution. But it's not enough; she must atone for her negligence.\n\nFortunately, the great entity provided the answer: when the Divine Realm descends, the world will become paradise.\n\n\"So, to quell the eternal roaring of the sea, for the innocent buried at sea, for guiding the direction of all beings, I request the Divine Realm's arrival.\"\n\nThis is her last, final navigation."
  },
  AwakerStory_81619_Title = {Text = "Story: IV"},
  AwakerStory_81619_UnlockDesc = {
    Text = "Affinity Level 9"
  },
  AwakerStory_95006_Content = {
    Text = "■File Number: DIOL-A3-27\n■Awakener Code Name: ■■■■\n\nBased on the behavior patterns, decision-making style, and attitude toward various tasks of this Awakener (hereinafter referred to as Kathigu-Ra), investigators conducted relevant speculations and later launched detailed investigations. The following content is now being synchronized:\nKathigu-Ra is an orphan from Region @2; their parents abandoned them during early childhood.\n\nKathigu-Ra survived in that region by unknown means and took in many unfortunate children. It should be noted that this process involved extensive use of bloody and violent methods. In one well-documented case, the subject brutally murdered all family members of one of the individuals they had taken in.\n\nFor a long time afterward, Kathigu-Ra and their subordinates mainly earned income through secretive commissions such as gangland killings, factional conflicts, looting stolen goods, and other black-on-black criminal activities.\n\nAccording to local testimonies and combined with data from that area, it has been preliminarily inferred that there was a specific point in time when a group centered around Kathigu-Ra and the children they had taken in successfully consolidated control over the majority of the region's criminal organizations.\n\nCurrently, we still cannot determine exactly how Kathigu-Ra became an Awakener, but the timeframe aligns with the destruction of the Lantern Church outpost in that area. Given Kathigu-Ra's evident disdain for the Church of the Lightbearers, it is reasonably speculated that their transformation into an Awakener may have been connected to the Church.\n\nAccording to incomplete statistics, up to now, Kathigu-Ra has destroyed 43 Lantern Church outposts, including 7 major outposts, 12 divine-summoning altars, and 17 research facilities.\n\nBased on the above investigation report and the daily behavioral patterns of this Awakener, the Committee, under the proposal of Honorary Chairman K. Trak, has re-evaluated the threat level posed by Kathigu-Ra. The evaluation results are recorded as follows:\nAfter deliberation by all committee members, this Awakener poses no direct or indirect threat to Mythag. Provided the current cooperation treaty remains unchanged, no intervention regarding its existence or actions is necessary.\n\nTherefore, it is hereby decided that Kathigu-Ra shall be removed from DIOL, and all related investigation activities shall be suspended immediately. All file records shall be fully sealed, and no personnel below Ω clearance are permitted access.\n\nRecorder: K. Trak\n(Small handwriting at the bottom of the document)\n\nCongratulations! Finally managed to get those overly cautious fools to cancel this damned project. Not bad for all the time I wasted pushing things forward.\n\nThis concludes the final record concerning Lady Kathigu-Ra. Unless something unexpected occurs, no further documentation will be added under this file number. So whoever you are, feel free to close this cursed folder now, step outside for some fresh air, and focus your attention on more deserving subjects!\n\n— Karapolis Trak, your good friend who has become a member of the idle class."
  },
  AwakerStory_95006_Title = {Text = "Story: III"},
  AwakerStory_95006_UnlockDesc = {
    Text = "Affinity Level 7"
  },
  AwakerStory_95007_Content = {
    Text = "■File Number: DIOL-A3-1\n■Awakener Code Name: ■■■■\nA.F.3@2, this Awakener initiated contact with Mythag.\n\n\"Sun! Sun! I saw the Sun! No! No!! Destroy it! Or we will all die!\"\n\nAccording to eyewitness accounts, the involved personnel shouted the above statement upon discovering this Awakener, and then ordered relevant units to attack it.\n\nDue to the incorrect judgment of the involved personnel, this Awakener displayed extreme aggression, directly resulting in the destruction of 31 anti-Awakener units, 76 standard equipment sets, and 2 academic buildings, with total property damage estimated at @2@4. The case has now been transferred to the relevant department for accountability procedures.\n\nPost-incident investigation revealed that this individual had been brainwashed by the Church of the Lightbearers. For subsequent details, please refer to related documents, as it will not be elaborated in this file.\n\nAfter a period of communication, negotiation personnel successfully convinced the Awakener to abandon its aggressive stance. Subsequently, the Awakener handed a letter signed by Lord Dexter to the school administration, claiming it was the last possession of a missing Investigator. Later confirmation by Lord Dexter verified the authenticity of the letter.\n\nIt is currently known that, through the mediation of Professor Doll, this Awakener has reached a certain agreement with the school administration. In exchange for some unspecified compensation, the Awakener has agreed to undertake certain commissions that the school finds difficult or inconvenient to handle directly.\n\nGiven the destructive capability demonstrated by this Awakener, despite displaying the highest level of stability and communicability in subsequent conversations, the Committee has decided to include it in the DIOL and will continue updating its file under the highest protocol.\n\nMay the Silver Key guide us.\n\nRecorder: L. Nadia"
  },
  AwakerStory_95007_Title = {Text = "Story: I"},
  AwakerStory_95007_UnlockDesc = {
    Text = "Awakener Level 3"
  },
  AwakerStory_95008_Content = {
    Text = "(Small text at the beginning of the file)\n\nDamn it, how did you find this file? I clearly forbade anyone from accessing it... Well, since you're able to see this file, it means your clearance is far above mine, which indicates you're one of Them, so naturally I have no authority to stop you from knowing these things.\n\nHowever, please keep in mind, this file should not exist anywhere. The following content is not any formal investigation, but rather an unofficial product composed by myself through secondary inferences based on certain real situations.\n\nI must seriously remind you that the process of compiling this file contains a large amount of investigative methods that cannot be described in detail, subjective assumptions from personal thinking, and even acts of accepting bribes from investigated subjects. If you are not bothered by my aforementioned actions, please continue reading. I guarantee with my reputation that the following content is undeniably authentic.\n\n■Subject Number: ■■■■-A■■-SSS\n■Awakener Codename: Lord of Combustion\n\"Honestly, I don't really like fighting.\"\n\nI was quite surprised to hear such an answer, considering in all the reports, investigators would use words like \"madness,\" \"joy,\" and \"elation\" when describing her in combat.\n\nI originally thought her attitude toward fighting was \"not initiating, not hating, not refusing,\" never expecting her to actually feel disgusted by the act itself.\n\nAs the conversation continued deeper, I gradually began to understand certain things. When I asked if I could record these words, Kathigu-Ra generously gave me permission to do so.\n\n\"You must understand, for most people in this world, simply being alive is already a luxury.\"\n\nI expressed agreement with this statement. Although most people I've encountered live comfortable lives—I could even go to the biggest opera house in Lentienni anytime I wanted—I clearly know the hidden truth of this world, and how many people are carrying burdens behind my comfortable life.\n\n\"Therefore, in many cases, intense fighting spirit is the price you pay to stay alive.\"\n\n\"We don't get to choose how we live. Once you step into the mud, it's nearly impossible to pull yourself out again.\"\n\nI originally wanted to argue against this viewpoint, but upon carefully recalling several cases, I found they were all people who could hardly be considered ordinary. As for those nameless nobodies, they mostly only exist within the memoirs of others.\n\n\"Perhaps some naive person might say, if that's the case, then why not just not do it from the beginning? That idea sounds good. I once carved it onto a certain tombstone to commemorate someone who strictly followed that principle.\"\n\n\"To protect everyone in this cruel world, I must appear strong and mad enough to make the ever-present malice hesitate.\"\n\n\"Of course, those emotions I display during battle are not fake. I truly enjoy the sensations battle brings me.\"\n\n\"It might be a bit hard to understand, but it's like how you might enjoy the content of your job, but not the act of working itself.\"\n\nUpon hearing this explanation, I immediately understood her meaning. Indeed, I really enjoy prying into others' privacy to satisfy my own guilty curiosity, but that doesn't mean I enjoy having to drag myself out of bed at eight o'clock every morning and follow orders to stay somewhere the entire day.\n\n\"When I was first abandoned, I was just like many other girls—lost, hesitant, and clueless.\"\n\n\"I hoped to receive help from others, but the world gave me nothing but countless betrayals and pains.\"\n\n\"Gradually, I began using cruelty and madness to forge armor against malice, adapting to everything in this world like drinking poison to quench thirst.\"\n\n\"Until finally, they melted within the ceaseless flames, merging with my flesh and blood.\"\n\nAs if to prove her words just now, Kathigu-Ra suddenly gave me an extremely cruel, evil, and mad smile, so much that I spilled the pale yellow liquid in my cup all over myself.\n\nOh, maybe it's a good thing, because this way, if I ever lose muscle control and accidentally spill something, I can naturally explain it as just the drink I spilled earlier.\n\nIn the end, Kathigu-Ra never directly answered my question, but I think my previous judgment was correct—she simply shouldn't exist within DIOL.\n\n—Recorder Karapolis Trak\n\n\"My original wish was simply to have a home.\"\n\n\"A home without betrayal, without pain, filled with laughter and joy.\"\n\n\"Unfortunately, I didn't understand until that day.\"\n\n\"This was the most luxurious delusion in this cruel world.\"\n\n—Kathigu-Ra"
  },
  AwakerStory_95008_Title = {Text = "Story: IV"},
  AwakerStory_95008_UnlockDesc = {
    Text = "Affinity Level 9"
  },
  AwakerStory_95009_Content = {
    Text = [[
Kathigu-Ra excels at using her signature smile to draw out the cruel, crazed chill that lurks in the deepest reaches of any observer's awareness.

Those two inseparable twin guns, with powder dust swirling around their barrels, warn every ill-intentioned petty criminal that the sacrifice of the nameless is the cornerstone of all greatness.

However, anyone who has truly dealt with her will understand that hunting these ordinary, sunless people is merely her pastime during the tedium of daily life.

After all, when she truly opens fire, the barrels hold no gunpowder at all.]]
  },
  AwakerStory_95009_Title = {
    Text = "Basic Information"
  },
  AwakerStory_95009_UnlockDesc = {
    Text = "Awakener Level 1"
  },
  AwakerStory_95010_Content = {
    Text = "■File Number: DIOL-A3-9\n■Awakener Code: ■■■■\n\nFrom continuous observation, it appears this Awakener does not show any unusual interest in Mythag—she seems almost indifferent. She only comes to campus when accepting commissions and leaves quickly afterward.\n\nAlthough the returned investigation report indeed records several instances of her lingering on campus for extended periods,\n\nfurther investigation revealed that her primary reason for staying was helping students resolve certain issues. It has been determined there is no security threat involved, so no intervention is necessary.\n\nOne point worth noting is that this Awakener appears unusually interested in the Keeper. She has repeatedly brought the Keeper @3 items classified as contraband and invited the Keeper to various dinners attended by unknown individuals. Considering the Keeper's importance to Mythag, if this Awakener attempts any dangerous action against the Keeper, at least four γ-class armed personnel must be arranged to ensure the Keeper's safe evacuation.\n\nRecorder: K. Trak\n\n(Small handwriting on the back of the file)\n\nHey, buddy. Or perhaps sister—it doesn't matter.\n\nThe last poor bastard quit, and now I'm stuck with this damn project.\n\nIf you're reading this, it means you're not some lazy good-for-nothing, but rather someone observant. Give yourself a round of applause.\n\nListen, although we keep saying we're \"monitoring her secretly,\" I feel like she already knows about us—it's just that she chooses to ignore it.\n\nI don't understand why we are monitoring someone like her. Although our first encounter had some misunderstandings, that was entirely caused by cultists, and had nothing to do with her personally.\n\nBesides, her relationship with the students—especially the Keeper—is like a grandmother buying candy for her grandchild! Surely nobody constantly suspects their own grandmother of planning to sacrifice them to cultists... Well, actually, maybe somewhere that really is the case—but that's not important!\n\nWhat matters is, if she truly has ulterior motives, I guarantee whatever she intends to do has already begun unnoticed, long before the Committee slowly drags out its ridiculous countermeasures.\n\nPhew, feels good to vent. Anyway, I've decided to remove her from this list before the Committee does something unforgivable to her.\n\nAnd once those bastards really piss her off—I promise it won't just be two buildings destroyed next time. I hope I'm dead by then, or else I'll probably die a very painful death.\n\nIf you're the one who will be watching her next, remember—not any rash actions. If you don't like her, just treat her like a mercenary hired to handle dirty work for the school. Unless she clearly shows signs of instability, under no circumstances should you provoke direct confrontation!\n\nOf course, if you want a little gift... I doubt she'll mind that you once monitored her. Go ahead and ask boldly. Honestly, the snacks in her pockets are actually pretty tasty.\n\n—Karapolis Trak, your fellow friend who curses the Committee alongside you."
  },
  AwakerStory_95010_Title = {Text = "Story: II"},
  AwakerStory_95010_UnlockDesc = {
    Text = "Affinity Level 5"
  },
  AwakerStory_95094_Content = {
    Text = [[
His entire life was lived under manipulated strings, and the script written long ago was a laughable lie that made him constantly lose, forget, and miss out. 

 When he was young, what he desired most was to freely flap his wings and see the world beyond that lake. 

 It wasn't until he lost everything for this wish that he could no longer regard such a light and carefree life as his ultimate dream. 

 Endless rage ignited that pitch-black heart, and the pain and hatred he repressed like blood needed to be washed away with the deaths of those false believers.]]
  },
  AwakerStory_95094_Title = {Text = "Story: IV"},
  AwakerStory_95094_UnlockDesc = {
    Text = "Affinity Level 9"
  },
  AwakerStory_95095_Content = {
    Text = [[
Considering the potential relationship between Pollux's "Sacred Heart" and the Church of the Lightbearers' divine ritual, Mythag formed a research team to conduct a series of inspections and experiments on the heart.

 To Pollux's regret, the "Sacred Heart" had entirely replaced his original heart's function, becoming integrated into his body, making direct removal or replacement impossible.

During observational experiments, researchers discovered that the "Sacred Heart," which resembles an eye pupil, often exhibited subtle tremors and rotations independent of Pollux's will, much like a real eye.

However, light source testing proved the "Sacred Heart" did not possess visual functions. Instead, this activity appeared to be sensitivity to other living beings or objects. In comparative trials with varied items, proximity to items related to dissolution and the silver core triggered the heart's activity more easily.

Its activity was particularly pronounced in front of Dissolutes and Awakeners. After Pollux actively used the "Sacred Heart's" power, the physical and chemical properties of ordinary items remained unchanged. However, when directed at dissoluted items and creatures, a remarkable expansion of dissolution occurred. Living organisms visibly in the early stages of dissolution rapidly accelerated towards the late stages. The more severe the dissolution originally suffered by the organisms, the faster this spread occurred.

In experiments with strict protective measures on Awakeners, the subjects reported a sense of approaching dark danger when faced with the "Sacred Heart's" power, prompting the experiment to be quickly halted.

After a stern explanation from the school, Pollux promised not to use his power against Awakeners. Due to Pollux's cooperation and excellent self-control, Mythag did not impose mandatory controlling items on him, but instead arranged regular health checks and power training.

It is said that after hearing the experimental results, Awakener Winkle almost fainted screaming and posted notices prohibiting Pollux from approaching on the doors of her laboratory and dormitory. The school repeatedly tried to persuade her to no avail, and Pollux graciously stated that he would respect Winkle's wishes.]]
  },
  AwakerStory_95095_Title = {Text = "Story: I"},
  AwakerStory_95095_UnlockDesc = {
    Text = "Awakener Level 3"
  },
  AwakerStory_95096_Content = {
    Text = "In the original design of the God of Fate, Pollux was probably never meant to be born.\n\nInitially, only Castor had been successfully created in the artificial Twin Divi experiment. Just as this single, clueless embryo was to be disposed of, Pollux struggled and twisted himself free from his brother's flesh. He absorbed his life force, yet in doing so, he also saved it—from that moment on, their flesh, souls, and fates were irrevocably intertwined.\n\nIn the monotonous routine of the church's teaching, their lives and destinies were identical. But with the start of the \"Holy Transformation\" ritual, the pain and ruthless torment awakened something within Pollux—a defiance of his ordained fate as a Divus. The two children committed the boldest act of their lives: they sketched a world map from an outdated book and escaped from one false world to another imagined one.\n\nAfter the fragile, fleeting beautiful dream shattered, the cruel punishment that followed did not crush their souls, yet that merciless fork in fate had already driven them apart.\n\nJuliette ordered the two to be separated and \"re-educated.\" Castor, submerged in the pool of sin, remained unaware that the tortures they had imagined were never inflicted upon Pollux. Instead, with an air of near mercy, Juliette ended the physical punishment and soon released Pollux from the dark room's confinement, steering him instead toward intense and rigorous theological teachings.\n\nPollux's unyielding doubts transformed into a deep-seated unease and fear under Juliette's utterly calm gaze; she must have mastered a method of control he could not resist, to appear so completely at ease.\n\nHe struggled, he disguised himself, and he never gave up. It seemed he did so many things... but what, in the end, had he truly accomplished? In the mirror, only the soul of a stranger remained, dutifully wearing the crown of the Divus.\n\nHe, and all their shared memories, had been completely forgotten."
  },
  AwakerStory_95096_Title = {Text = "Story: III"},
  AwakerStory_95096_UnlockDesc = {
    Text = "Affinity Level 7"
  },
  AwakerStory_95097_Content = {
    Text = "He is flesh born from a twisted existence—stitched together from cut skin, a hollow chest cavity, a tainted heart, and invisible chains.\n\nHe is placed upon a pedestal, worshipped at the feet, said to possess a pure soul.\n\nWhat, then, is he? Lost in countless dreams, he asks in confusion; and among the dark-green lake waters and the empty fog, only his own voice echoes back in lonely reply."
  },
  AwakerStory_95097_Title = {
    Text = "Basic Information"
  },
  AwakerStory_95097_UnlockDesc = {
    Text = "Awakener Level 1"
  },
  AwakerStory_95098_Content = {
    Text = "Compared to Castor's active and studious attitude, Pollux's approach to the world is one of quiet vigilance.\n\nHe observes, he thinks, he doubts. It was his meticulous consideration and caution that once enabled their successful escape from the church's heavy control. From a young age, he learned to gauge the intentions of others, to lie, and to hide his true thoughts behind a disarming smile. Even with his intimately close brother, he would subconsciously use a relaxed demeanor to soothe and reassure.\n\n\"It's okay.\"\n\n\"It will be alright.\"\n\nBeneath the shadow of a giant, the weak must exhaust every means to grasp a single glimmer of hope.\n\nHaving endured a long period of forced forgetting and deception, he now tolerates no danger or mistakes. Even after heeding Thais's advice and coming to Mythag, he remained profoundly vigilant for a long time.\n\nTo other Awakeners, Pollux appears as a quiet, patient, and friendly individual who often offers a gentle smile. But seasoned elders who see him can only sigh at the profound difference between the two brothers.\n\nAccording to Thais, even in her presence, Pollux will intentionally or unintentionally position himself between her and Castor—since reclaiming his memory, he no longer wishes for Castor to always be his sole protector.\n\nJenkin once earnestly complained to the Keeper about Pollux's duality, claiming that when she \"accidentally\" picked up an item belonging to Castor, she witnessed his expression turn terrifying in an instant. \"His usual good temper must be fake! He's the type who would eat children in private!\"\n\nHowever, after witnessing the Keeper's true power, Pollux's attitude underwent a complete transformation. He claims to have learned the truth of the world from that great soul and has now taken the Keeper as his new, unwavering faith."
  },
  AwakerStory_95098_Title = {Text = "Story: II"},
  AwakerStory_95098_UnlockDesc = {
    Text = "Affinity Level 5"
  },
  AwakerStory_96418_Content = {
    Text = "The founder of Necrovia, the eternal king of ghouls. \n\nHis banquet is worthy of the deepest anticipation—grand dining hall, elegant dance, and those exquisite dishes handcrafted from corpses will surely be unforgettable for your entire life."
  },
  AwakerStory_96418_Title = {
    Text = "Basic Information"
  },
  AwakerStory_96418_UnlockDesc = {
    Text = "Awakener Level 1"
  },
  AwakerStory_96419_Content = {
    Text = "After leaving Necrovia, Doresain demonstrated remarkable adaptability within human society. This was inevitable; for him, human society was not a new beginning, but rather a return.\n\nHis speech, mannerisms, demeanor, and etiquette were flawless, maintaining the aura of a monarch while showing none of the arrogance typically festering in those who have held power too long.\n\nDoresain does not avoid social interaction, yet he shows little interest in topics like politics, economics, or academia. The only thing drawing him to such occasions is food.\n\nBeyond mere appreciation of cuisine, Doresain takes visceral pleasure in the kitchen process itself—from ingredient selection and preparation techniques to spice usage and heat control. His vast culinary knowledge and refined taste captivate everyone he converses with.\n\nThey come to realize all their previous decades of dining were nothing more than hurried survival, no different from beasts eating merely to stay alive. Even those unfortunate souls born without a sense of taste can experience food's artistry through his descriptions, achieving what he calls \"a rebirth of flavor perception.\"\n\nThis revelation is inseparable from Doresain's impeccable manners—he understands with crystal clarity the differences between human and ghoul culinary preferences. He respects these species distinctions and has no desire to impose his own tastes on others.\n\n\"Some people always regard difference as heresy,\" he remarks, the ghost of a smile playing about his lips. \"In my city-state, such behavior was considered profoundly inelegant. I celebrate individual differences. It is precisely through these variations that we discover food's greatest beauties.\"\n\nThen the purple mist around him swirls as he adds, voice dropping to a intimate murmur: \"But you are different, Keeper. As such a singular being in this world... I believe you, above all others, might experience unparalleled beauty in the act of eating, just as I do...\"\n\nAs he speaks these words, Doresain's smile flickers through the violet haze like the grin of some elegant, patient serpent whispering in your ear, waiting to lead you out of—or perhaps into—a very particular Garden of Eden."
  },
  AwakerStory_96419_Title = {Text = "Story: II"},
  AwakerStory_96419_UnlockDesc = {
    Text = "Affinity Level 5"
  },
  AwakerStory_96420_Content = {
    Text = "When Doresain awoke in the sunless temple of Necrovia, pain slithered through him like a nest of awakened serpents. The poison's work was unfinished, its blades still carving hymns of agony from his abdomen outward, thorned and relentless. He'd known his father's wine was tainted—had seen the old king's trembling hands, the shadows whispering behind his eyes—yet he drank it anyway, smiling as the bitterness kissed his throat.\n\nClever. Kind. Unshakable. By every measure, Doresain had been the perfect heir. But in a city where the living called corpse-eating a sin, even princes were not spared the pyre. He'd tried to teach them—the poetry of decay, the sacrament of bones—but understanding was a bridge between worlds, and his family had burned it long ago.\n\nHe never expected to open his eyes again. Yet here he was, choking on a new torment. The black mist coiled around him, alive with teeth and hunger, peeling him apart layer by layer. It gnawed. It sculpted. His flesh regrew only to be stripped anew, a grotesque dance of devouring and rebirth. His scream was soundless, lost in the temple's hollow belly.\n\nThen—a flavor. Unimaginable. Divine. Amid the rending and the howling dark, it bloomed on his tongue: the god of Necrovia was feasting on him, and the taste was ecstasy. Pain dissolved. Poison became ambrosia. The god's laughter echoed in his marrow, their suffering and rapture now one and the same.\n\nFor seven nights, the feast endured. When Doresain rose at last, the altar's chill still humming in his veins, he felt no rage, no sorrow. Only gratitude. His murderers had given him a gift—the exquisite last meal of his own flesh, the delirious joy of being known.\n\nBeyond the temple, the full moon hung like a bone-white hook. Necrovia knelt in the dark, and its new king smiled."
  },
  AwakerStory_96420_Title = {Text = "Story: III"},
  AwakerStory_96420_UnlockDesc = {
    Text = "Affinity Level 7"
  },
  AwakerStory_96421_Content = {
    Text = "The abandoned cemetery in the northwest of London County has been listed as an absolute forbidden zone by local residents since AF 3@2.\n\nAccording to archived reports from The Times and Scotland Yard's missing persons files, 37 people have gone missing in the thick night fog of the cemetery in recent years, including: Cyril, a habitual grave robber with a taste for noble tombs; Cook, a shivering vagrant seeking shelter; Officer Grayson, who stumbled in during patrol; and White, the Oxford scholar who studied how medieval bones were laid to rest.\n\nAll vanished when the fog grew thick, leaving not even a scrap of fabric for search teams to find.\n\nPrior to AF 3@2, the MTC had always treated the area as barely worth noting in their ledgers.\n\nThat changed when the Duke of Derbyshire—Samuel Curzon, that notorious patron of unnatural studies—failed to return from his midnight visit.\n\nRoyal inquiries have a way of focusing attention, and soon a special operation was mounted.\n\nIn July of AF 3@2, Elias ThOrnn led twelve armed agents and three silver-equipped mediums into the cemetery's hungry mists.\n\nTheir anti-hypothermia medication hissed in its cases; their directional locators spun like dowsing rods in a haunted well.\n\nAfter advancing precisely 1.2 kilometers in tight formation, they found it—a hexagonal entrance hidden beneath the shattered statue of the Ghoul King, its stone face worn smooth by centuries of bad weather and worse company.\n\nFive thousand steps down (each counted twice by nervous lips) brought them to the temple.\n\nWhere they expected charnel houses and stacked bones, they found instead 800 square meters of impossible precision: floors flatter than mathematics, air cleaner than a surgical theater.\n\nOnly the altar broke the perfection—2.3 meters of granite carved with endless thorns, wreathed in black mist that clung like cobwebs to something moving inside.\n\nThere knelt the Duke, dressed for dinner but quite dead, showing no marks save those left by perfect preservation.\n\nWhen the mist was disturbed, he came apart like sugar in tea—dissolving until even the mass spectrometers wept empty data.\n\nThen the mist turned its attention to the living.\n\nEvery investigator heard the same voice—cultured, gentle, the sort that might recite poetry before the cutting begins:\n\"Please do not seek out Necrovia. Please do not disturb the King of the Ghouls during his meal.\"\n\n\"Consider this your final warning.\"\n\nThey awoke outside the rusted gates, equipment intact but all recordings curiously blank.\n\nLater, the MTC chairman and Miskatonic's occult dean would visit, then quietly declare the matter closed.\n\nThe cemetery now only punishes those who come seeking secrets; mere wanderers get off with nothing worse than lost hours and strange dreams.\n\nBut sometimes, when the fog rolls in particularly thick, the locals swear they can hear something chewing below their feet.\n\n——Investigation Report on the Abandoned Cemetery of Etherington"
  },
  AwakerStory_96421_Title = {Text = "Story: I"},
  AwakerStory_96421_UnlockDesc = {
    Text = "Awakener Level 3"
  },
  AwakerStory_96422_Content = {
    Text = "He had once believed that his entire life existed for the pursuit of ultimate deliciousness.\n\nThe duties of a crown prince, the estrangement from loved ones, the weight of moral teachings... He had cast all this pain aside in his relentless quest for culinary perfection.\n\nFrom prince to monarch, from mortal to divine, his hunger never waned. He mastered every cooking technique, could detect the most fleeting nuance in every corpse's flavor profile.\n\nHe attained everything he desired, yet after each ephemeral moment of satisfaction, that hollow feeling remained - like a flavor just beyond his palate's reach.\n\nIt wasn't until he consumed Celina's corpse and glimpsed her lingering soul that understanding came.\n\nThe stories etched in flesh before death's arrival, the unfinished yearnings that clung to bones - these were the missing ingredients he'd been chasing, the true essence he'd been tasting without realizing.\n\n\"Eating is remembrance; every feast a reunion between departed and living\" —these are the words carved into Necrovia's throne. He will grant those who seek his protection remembrance and eternal rest."
